{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793915985146,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adb99cfa0011dNSC8qj14X2Qw","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adb9910f001ppO0rHgezwLKWp","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9423d092324b187734053d0606c04c3a4a2c21c5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793915986232,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adb99f31001JeDghhfJyorg8r","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adb9910f001ppO0rHgezwLKWp","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4c623c46b74345d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\ncat packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml; echo \"===CATALOG===\"; grep -n \"dsh-headless\\|permissionMode\\|approvalPolicy\\|effort\\|reasoning\" docs/config-catalog.md | head -40"},"output":"# The dsh-headless bundle patch: one-shot task mode directly over dsh-base.\n# It mounts no Host, HTTP server, Web runtime, or browser plugin. An ordinary\n# provider plugin injects `cmdlineArgs`, parses the task positional\n# (`dsh --profile headless \"<task>\"`), Session identity, permission and output\n# options, and this app's --help, then the direct driver creates a fresh Agent, or adopts\n# the exact Session the flag names, through the core registry and prints its\n# durable result.\n\n- id: system-prompt\n  config:\n    personaPrefix: >-\n      You are a coding agent powered by the {{model}} model.\n\n- insert:\n    - id: headless-startup\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless/startup'\n\n    # Reads its task and run options from the ordinary headlessStartup provider.\n    - id: headless-runner\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless'\n      inject: [headlessStartup]\n      config:\n        task: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.task\n        sessionId: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.sessionId\n        json: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.json\n\n# Replacing config retains the base mode/root defaults while adding the CLI grants.\n- id: sandbox-policy\n  inject: [headlessStartup]\n  config:\n    mode: !!js process.env.DSH_PERMISSION_MODE ?? 'workspace-write'\n    workspaceRoot: !!js process.cwd()\n    additionalWritableRoots: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.additionalWritableRoots\n\n- id: hmr\n  disabled: true\n\n# One-shot jobs use launch-time credentials instead of the interactive store.\n- id: credentials\n  disabled: true\n\n- id: authorization\n  disabled: true\n\n- id: deepseek-account\n  disabled: true\n===CATALOG===\n66:  /** Adapter-owned reasoning effort; omission follows the provider default. */\n67:  reasoningEffort: Volatile<string | undefined>\n1434:  /** Native reasoning effort; unsupported choices fail during startup. */\n1435:  effort?: string\n1612:<!-- BEGIN GENERATED config-catalog:@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless -->\n1613:<a id=\"deepseek-aidsh-headless\"></a>\n1615:## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless`\n1631:  permissionMode?: string\n1633:  approvalPolicy?: ApprovalPolicy\n1636:<!-- END GENERATED config-catalog:@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless -->\n2030:  /** Provider-neutral pi-ai reasoning level. */\n2031:  reasoning?: ModelThinkingLevel\n2032:  /** Token budgets used by reasoning providers that support them. */\n2102:   * Selectable reasoning efforts. Absent inherits the installed catalog\n2104:   * `false` declares a non-reasoning model, which is how a profile strips\n2105:   * reasoning from a catalog model its gateway cannot serve; a non-empty dict\n2108:  reasoningEfforts?: false | PiAiReasoningEfforts\n2145:   * which pi-ai sends only to a reasoning model; `false` keeps `system`.\n2149:  /** Whether the endpoint accepts `reasoning_effort`; `openai-completions`. */\n2166:  /** Whether replayed assistant messages need an empty `reasoning_content` while reasoning is on; `openai-completions`. */\n2182:  /** Request field carrying the reasoning budget from `thinkingBudgets`; omitted unless configured. `openai-completions`. */\n2218: * Selectable reasoning efforts for one model: each key is a level the model\n2227:/** One reasoning-dispatch wire format a profile may name. */\n2230:/** The reasoning-budget field spellings pi-ai accepts. */\n2301:  /** Optional reasoning-effort ids from least to greatest selectable effort. */\n2302:  reasoningEfforts?: string[]\n2304:   * Optional effort materialized when callers omit one; must appear in\n2305:   * {@link reasoningEfforts} or call resolution rejects the route.\n3714:  permissionMode?: ClaudeCodePermissionMode\n3745:  permissionMode?: CodexPermissionMode\n4408:   * Expose optional child `provider`, `model`, and `reasoning_effort` fields.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# The dsh-headless bundle patch: one-shot task mode directly over dsh-base.\n# It mounts no Host, HTTP server, Web runtime, or browser plugin. An ordinary\n# provider plugin injects `cmdlineArgs`, parses the task positional\n# (`dsh --profile headless \"<task>\"`), Session identity, permission and output\n# options, and this app's --help, then the direct driver creates a fresh Agent, or adopts\n# the exact Session the flag names, through the core registry and prints its\n# durable result.\n\n- id: system-prompt\n  config:\n    personaPrefix: >-\n      You are a coding agent powered by the {{model}} model.\n\n- insert:\n    - id: headless-startup\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless/startup'\n\n    # Reads its task and run options from the ordinary headlessStartup provider.\n    - id: headless-runner\n      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless'\n      inject: [headlessStartup]\n      config:\n        task: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.task\n        sessionId: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.sessionId\n        json: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.json\n\n# Replacing config retains the base mode/root defaults while adding the CLI grants.\n- id: sandbox-policy\n  inject: [headlessStartup]\n  config:\n    mode: !!js process.env.DSH_PERMISSION_MODE ?? 'workspace-write'\n    workspaceRoot: !!js process.cwd()\n    additionalWritableRoots: !!js ctx.headlessStartup.additionalWritableRoots\n\n- id: hmr\n  disabled: true\n\n# One-shot jobs use launch-time credentials instead of the interactive store.\n- id: credentials\n  disabled: true\n\n- id: authorization\n  disabled: true\n\n- id: deepseek-account\n  disabled: true\n===CATALOG===\n66:  /** Adapter-owned reasoning effort; omission follows the provider default. */\n67:  reasoningEffort: Volatile<string | undefined>\n1434:  /** Native reasoning effort; unsupported choices fail during startup. */\n1435:  effort?: string\n1612:<!-- BEGIN GENERATED config-catalog:@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless -->\n1613:<a id=\"deepseek-aidsh-headless\"></a>\n1615:## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless`\n1631:  permissionMode?: string\n1633:  approvalPolicy?: ApprovalPolicy\n1636:<!-- END GENERATED config-catalog:@deepseek-ai/dsh-headless -->\n2030:  /** Provider-neutral pi-ai reasoning level. */\n2031:  reasoning?: ModelThinkingLevel\n2032:  /** Token budgets used by reasoning providers that support them. */\n2102:   * Selectable reasoning efforts. Absent inherits the installed catalog\n2104:   * `false` declares a non-reasoning model, which is how a profile strips\n2105:   * reasoning from a catalog model its gateway cannot serve; a non-empty dict\n2108:  reasoningEfforts?: false | PiAiReasoningEfforts\n2145:   * which pi-ai sends only to a reasoning model; `false` keeps `system`.\n2149:  /** Whether the endpoint accepts `reasoning_effort`; `openai-completions`. */\n2166:  /** Whether replayed assistant messages need an empty `reasoning_content` while reasoning is on; `openai-completions`. */\n2182:  /** Request field carrying the reasoning budget from `thinkingBudgets`; omitted unless configured. `openai-completions`. */\n2218: * Selectable reasoning efforts for one model: each key is a level the model\n2227:/** One reasoning-dispatch wire format a profile may name. */\n2230:/** The reasoning-budget field spellings pi-ai accepts. */\n2301:  /** Optional reasoning-effort ids from least to greatest selectable effort. */\n2302:  reasoningEfforts?: string[]\n2304:   * Optional effort materialized when callers omit one; must appear in\n2305:   * {@link reasoningEfforts} or call resolution rejects the route.\n3714:  permissionMode?: ClaudeCodePermissionMode\n3745:  permissionMode?: CodexPermissionMode\n4408:   * Expose optional child `provider`, `model`, and `reasoning_effort` fields.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\ncat packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml; echo \\\"===CATALOG===\\\"; grep -n \\\"dsh-headless\\\\|permissionMode\\\\|approvalPolicy\\\\|effort\\\\|reasoning\\\" docs/config-catalog.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1793915985713,"end":1793915986232}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793915987237,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adb9a081001g4sI97qt2WgwOa","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adb9910f001ppO0rHgezwLKWp","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a275f2c5fb44c3be","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\ndsh headless --help </dev/null 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\""},"output":"Usage: dsh --profile headless [options] [task...]\n\nAnswer one task and exit; the answer goes to stdout and diagnostics to stderr.\n\nArguments:\n  task                        the task text; multiple words are joined by\n                              spaces, and `-` reads stdin\n\nOptions:\n  --json                      write newline-delimited run events to stdout\n                              instead of the final message\n  --session-id <id>           adopt the persisted Session with this id; an\n                              unknown id is an error\n  --permission-mode <preset>  select a configured permission preset for this\n                              task, including on resume\n  --approval-policy <policy>  set approval behavior after selecting the\n                              permission preset (choices: \"ask\", \"never\")\n  --add-dir <path>            allow an additional physical absolute directory\n                              under workspace-write (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                  show this help\n\nExamples:\n  dsh --profile headless \"run the tests\"          answer one task and exit\n  echo \"run the tests\" | dsh --profile headless   read the task from stdin\n  dsh --profile headless --json \"run the tests\"   emit machine-readable run events\n  dsh --profile headless --session-id session-… \"continue\"   resume an existing Session\n  dsh --profile headless --permission-mode workspace-write --add-dir /repo/.git \"commit the fix\"\n                                                        grant shared Git metadata for this task\n\nexit=0\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Usage: dsh --profile headless [options] [task...]\n\nAnswer one task and exit; the answer goes to stdout and diagnostics to stderr.\n\nArguments:\n  task                        the task text; multiple words are joined by\n                              spaces, and `-` reads stdin\n\nOptions:\n  --json                      write newline-delimited run events to stdout\n                              instead of the final message\n  --session-id <id>           adopt the persisted Session with this id; an\n                              unknown id is an error\n  --permission-mode <preset>  select a configured permission preset for this\n                              task, including on resume\n  --approval-policy <policy>  set approval behavior after selecting the\n                              permission preset (choices: \"ask\", \"never\")\n  --add-dir <path>            allow an additional physical absolute directory\n                              under workspace-write (repeatable)\n  -h, --help                  show this help\n\nExamples:\n  dsh --profile headless \"run the tests\"          answer one task and exit\n  echo \"run the tests\" | dsh --profile headless   read the task from stdin\n  dsh --profile headless --json \"run the tests\"   emit machine-readable run events\n  dsh --profile headless --session-id session-… \"continue\"   resume an existing Session\n  dsh --profile headless --permission-mode workspace-write --add-dir /repo/.git \"commit the fix\"\n                                                        grant shared Git metadata for this task\n\nexit=0\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\\ndsh headless --help </dev/null 2>&1; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1793915986049,"end":1793915987237}}}}
