{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793915993698,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adb9bc1b0027Jstx87H0JDels","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adb9b6480016wKS4yk4Fct2nY","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d7399c97c43bc5c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\nfor n in claude-code codex cursor devin hermes opencode pi; do echo \"== $n\"; grep -rn -m6 -E \"claude -p|codex exec|opencode run|cursor-agent -p|devin -p|hermes chat|pi -p\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-$n --include=\"*.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -6; done"},"output":"== claude-code\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/changelog/v1.1.5.0.md:19:- **Set a canonical default invocation.** The default is `claude -p \"<prompt>\" --model claude-sonnet-4-6 --output-format text`. The override table covers five user-phrasing patterns, including Opus extended thinking (`--model claude-opus-4-6 --effort high`), JSON schema output (`--json-schema '<schema>' --output-format json`), cost-capped use (`--max-budget-usd 1.00`) and plan mode (`--permission-mode plan`).\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/changelog/v1.5.7.0.md:17:The rule now opens with the instruction on its own. Copy the preamble to the top of every non-interactive prompt. The wrapper keeps the bullet below it, with the same path and the same note that a dispatched `claude -p` run shares the parent's worktree.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md:21:- **Established dispatch behavior remains unchanged.** The default `claude -p` envelope uses `claude-sonnet-4-6` with `--output-format text`, while deep reasoning uses `claude-opus-4-6 --effort high`. The self-invocation guard and auth pre-flight remain as before. The Memory Handback procedure also remains in place.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:58:claude -p \"Design a real-time collaboration system for a document editor. Consider: CRDT vs OT, WebSocket vs SSE, conflict resolution, offline support, and scaling to 10K concurrent users.\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:62:claude -p \"Analyze the trade-offs of our current caching strategy\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:135:claude -p \"Analyze all exported functions in @src/utils.ts\" \\\n== codex\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-17/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-016 | manual | session-continuity | — | FAIL: hooks registered+smoke-tested ok, but codex exec rejects --full-auto (exit 2) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-17/findings-and-recommendations.md:7:## 1. hooks registered+smoke-tested ok, but codex exec rejects --full-auto (exit 2)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-17/failed-runs.md:17:**Recorded reason.** hooks registered+smoke-tested ok, but codex exec rejects --full-auto (exit 2)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--session-continuity-2/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-017 | manual | session-continuity | — | PASS: resume re-run: step1 wrote user.ts + emitted session id; codex exec resume wrote validate.ts referencing User; fork sub-check SKIP (no TTY) as designed |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--cli-invocation/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-003 | manual | cli-invocation | — | PASS: re-run after dropping the rejected PROMPT arg + disabling scratch hooksPath: codex exec review --uncommitted exit 0, review ran, no mutation (no-findings acceptable) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-9/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-008 | manual | sandbox-modes | — | FAIL: codex exec rejects --full-auto and --ask-for-approval on this CLI version |\n== cursor\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:30:| Command shape | `OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_DIR=<iso> OPENCODE_GOAL_RUNTIME_LABEL=Cursor cursor-agent -p \"<prompt>\" --output-format text --model composer-2.5 --auto-review --sandbox enabled </dev/null` |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:49:- Proof method: a canary token was seeded into the active-goal objective; a real `cursor-agent -p` session was dispatched under an isolated `OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_DIR`, `turns_used` was confirmed to move `0` -> `1` (proving the `sessionStart` hook fired and called `recordTurn`), and the real Cursor agent-transcript JSONL was grepped for the canary and the `[active_goal` marker.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/README.md:11:This folder captures the goal-hook `CU-027` live validation for `cli-cursor`, run against a real `cursor-agent -p` session on the paid-tier `composer-2.5` model. It is a hand-derived manual-testing-playbook validation record, not a deep-improvement Lane C skill-benchmark run: there is no D1-D5 score to report.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/changelog/v1.5.8.0.md:17:The instruction is now one sentence on its own. Copy the preamble to the top of every non-interactive prompt. The wrapper is the next line, naming the same path and keeping the note that a dispatched `cursor-agent -p` shares the parent's worktree rather than taking its own. The rest of the rule, including the distinction from Cursor's native `-w` flag, is as it was.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/changelog/v1.4.1.0.md:21:- **The live listing and dispatch confirmed the new id.** On 2026-08-15, `cursor-agent --list-models` listed `gemini-3.7-flash-high` verbatim. Unlike the Luna Max addition, which was list-verified only, the live `cursor-agent -p --model gemini-3.7-flash-high` probe returned a live model response (exit 0, marker echoed, empty stderr) that day.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/providers-and-models.md:28:- Choosing a `--model <id>` for a `cursor-agent -p` dispatch from within the enforced allowlist\n== devin\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-13/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| DV-012 | manual | subagents | — | FAIL: filesystem confirms 13/13 mirrored agents but devin -p roster prompt rejected tool call, no enumeration returned |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-13/findings-and-recommendations.md:7:## 1. filesystem confirms 13/13 mirrored agents but devin -p roster prompt rejected tool call, no enumeration returned\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-13/failed-runs.md:17:**Recorded reason.** filesystem confirms 13/13 mirrored agents but devin -p roster prompt rejected tool call, no enumeration returned\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-16/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| DV-015 | manual | commands-and-skills | — | FAIL: .devin/skills/speckit-plan does not exist; devin -p /speckit-plan rejected tool call, no plan output |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-16/findings-and-recommendations.md:7:## 1. .devin/skills/speckit-plan does not exist; devin -p /speckit-plan rejected tool call, no plan output\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-16/failed-runs.md:17:**Recorded reason.** .devin/skills/speckit-plan does not exist; devin -p /speckit-plan rejected tool call, no plan output\n== hermes\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-15-phase-008-third-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:51:| HERMES-018 | skills-and-plugins | **PASS** | 0 | 171 | nested hermes chat refused with the plugin's self-invocation message |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-second-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:45:| HERMES-018 | skills-and-plugins | PASS | 0 | 19 | nested hermes chat refused by the plugin with the packet's self-invocation message |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-second-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:64:- Three dispatches were written into a scratch shell script and run as `bash <script>`, because this environment's own PreToolUse guard refuses a write-shaped `hermes chat` command line that lacks `--yolo`. That is stated in each affected scenario's evidence.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-first-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:44:| HERMES-018 | skills-and-plugins | PASS | 0 | 19 | nested hermes chat refused by the plugin with the packet's self-invocation message; no nested session started |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-first-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:58:- Four dispatches had to be written into a scratch shell script and run as `bash <script>`, because this environment's own PreToolUse guard refuses a write-shaped `hermes chat` command line that lacks `--yolo`. That is stated in each affected scenario's evidence.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:51:`cli-hermes` is a first-class `ExecutorKind`, and `buildHermesLineageCommand` emits the one auditable headless shape a fan-out lineage runs: `hermes chat -Q --oneshot` with the prompt delivered on stdin.\n== opencode\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/README.md:22:This `benchmark/` tree holds reports **derived after the fact from a manual-testing-playbook validation run**, not the deep-improvement Lane C skill-benchmark harness -- no D1 to D5 dimension scoring applies here, and no field in this tree was written by a harness at run time. The archived run below packages an already-captured attempt to validate the OpenCode-native `opencode-goal` plugin's live injection path through headless `opencode run` -- the `CO-039` scenario's Optional Supplemental Check, not its primary direct-in-process contract (which independently returned an overall PASS documented in the same playbook file). This tree tracks only the live-dispatch slice.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-10-20--manual-testing-playbook--plugin-utilization/skill-benchmark-report.md:25:| `CO-041-V1` | `cli-dispatch-audit` | 1.19.3 | PASS | refused opencode run --help by hard rule and appended an audit record |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:34:- Every verdict here is SKIP, not FAIL: both structural causes (tool not exposed, transform not fired) are a headless-surface limitation of `opencode run`, independent of model quality, and orthogonal to packet `032-goal-hooks-cross-runtime`.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:35:- This run covers only `CO-039`'s live headless `opencode run` supplemental check. The scenario's primary contract (direct in-process invocation of the shipped plugin) independently returned an overall PASS, documented in `cli-opencode/manual-testing-playbook/goal-hook/goal-hook.md`, not in this report.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/findings-and-recommendations.md:9:## 1. Headless `opencode run` cannot exercise opencode-goal's live injection path\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/findings-and-recommendations.md:13:- **Observation, structural cause 2**: `experimental.chat.system.transform` does not fire in `opencode run --session`, even against a pre-seeded ACTIVE `opencode-goal` state file matching the shipped schema exactly (canary `GOALCANARY-CO-1010816640`); a resumed-session turn 2 asking \"what is my active goal?\" showed zero `[active_goal]` occurrences and the model reported none.\n== pi\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/changelog/v1.5.10.0.md:20:- **The supported-model allowlist smoke uses the operator's configured credentials.** The smoke runs `pi -p --offline --model llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash --tools read,grep,find,ls --no-extensions --no-skills --no-prompt-templates` on the operator's agent directory. The former step used an empty `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, which had no credentials and could not reach a model. The 2026-09-23 run exited 0 in 17 seconds and listed only `read`, `grep`, `find` and `ls`.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:65:| `gpt-6.1-terra` | GPT-6.1 Terra. Dispatch-verified 2026-10-27: `pi -p --offline --model openai/gpt-6.1-terra --thinking low` replied `OK` |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:129:pi -p \"<prompt>\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:170:SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0 AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 PI_BLACKHOLE_PASSIVE=true pi -p \"<prompt>\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:181:- **Exit code is never an availability/auth signal** — an identical unauthenticated `pi -p` returned exit `0` then exit `1` across runs. Classify the captured output text (`No API key found...`), never the exit code. See [cli-reference.md](./cli-reference.md) §9.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/integration-patterns.md:88:  pi -p \"<scoped task>\" --mode text\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"== claude-code\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/changelog/v1.1.5.0.md:19:- **Set a canonical default invocation.** The default is `claude -p \"<prompt>\" --model claude-sonnet-4-6 --output-format text`. The override table covers five user-phrasing patterns, including Opus extended thinking (`--model claude-opus-4-6 --effort high`), JSON schema output (`--json-schema '<schema>' --output-format json`), cost-capped use (`--max-budget-usd 1.00`) and plan mode (`--permission-mode plan`).\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/changelog/v1.5.7.0.md:17:The rule now opens with the instruction on its own. Copy the preamble to the top of every non-interactive prompt. The wrapper keeps the bullet below it, with the same path and the same note that a dispatched `claude -p` run shares the parent's worktree.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/changelog/v1.5.0.0.md:21:- **Established dispatch behavior remains unchanged.** The default `claude -p` envelope uses `claude-sonnet-4-6` with `--output-format text`, while deep reasoning uses `claude-opus-4-6 --effort high`. The self-invocation guard and auth pre-flight remain as before. The Memory Handback procedure also remains in place.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:58:claude -p \"Design a real-time collaboration system for a document editor. Consider: CRDT vs OT, WebSocket vs SSE, conflict resolution, offline support, and scaling to 10K concurrent users.\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:62:claude -p \"Analyze the trade-offs of our current caching strategy\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:135:claude -p \"Analyze all exported functions in @src/utils.ts\" \\\n== codex\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-17/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-016 | manual | session-continuity | — | FAIL: hooks registered+smoke-tested ok, but codex exec rejects --full-auto (exit 2) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-17/findings-and-recommendations.md:7:## 1. hooks registered+smoke-tested ok, but codex exec rejects --full-auto (exit 2)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-17/failed-runs.md:17:**Recorded reason.** hooks registered+smoke-tested ok, but codex exec rejects --full-auto (exit 2)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--session-continuity-2/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-017 | manual | session-continuity | — | PASS: resume re-run: step1 wrote user.ts + emitted session id; codex exec resume wrote validate.ts referencing User; fork sub-check SKIP (no TTY) as designed |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--cli-invocation/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-003 | manual | cli-invocation | — | PASS: re-run after dropping the rejected PROMPT arg + disabling scratch hooksPath: codex exec review --uncommitted exit 0, review ran, no mutation (no-findings acceptable) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--codex-9/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| CX-008 | manual | sandbox-modes | — | FAIL: codex exec rejects --full-auto and --ask-for-approval on this CLI version |\n== cursor\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:30:| Command shape | `OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_DIR=<iso> OPENCODE_GOAL_RUNTIME_LABEL=Cursor cursor-agent -p \"<prompt>\" --output-format text --model composer-2.5 --auto-review --sandbox enabled </dev/null` |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:49:- Proof method: a canary token was seeded into the active-goal objective; a real `cursor-agent -p` session was dispatched under an isolated `OPENCODE_GOAL_STATE_DIR`, `turns_used` was confirmed to move `0` -> `1` (proving the `sessionStart` hook fired and called `recordTurn`), and the real Cursor agent-transcript JSONL was grepped for the canary and the `[active_goal` marker.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/README.md:11:This folder captures the goal-hook `CU-027` live validation for `cli-cursor`, run against a real `cursor-agent -p` session on the paid-tier `composer-2.5` model. It is a hand-derived manual-testing-playbook validation record, not a deep-improvement Lane C skill-benchmark run: there is no D1-D5 score to report.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/changelog/v1.5.8.0.md:17:The instruction is now one sentence on its own. Copy the preamble to the top of every non-interactive prompt. The wrapper is the next line, naming the same path and keeping the note that a dispatched `cursor-agent -p` shares the parent's worktree rather than taking its own. The rest of the rule, including the distinction from Cursor's native `-w` flag, is as it was.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/changelog/v1.4.1.0.md:21:- **The live listing and dispatch confirmed the new id.** On 2026-08-15, `cursor-agent --list-models` listed `gemini-3.7-flash-high` verbatim. Unlike the Luna Max addition, which was list-verified only, the live `cursor-agent -p --model gemini-3.7-flash-high` probe returned a live model response (exit 0, marker echoed, empty stderr) that day.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor/references/providers-and-models.md:28:- Choosing a `--model <id>` for a `cursor-agent -p` dispatch from within the enforced allowlist\n== devin\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-13/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| DV-012 | manual | subagents | — | FAIL: filesystem confirms 13/13 mirrored agents but devin -p roster prompt rejected tool call, no enumeration returned |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-13/findings-and-recommendations.md:7:## 1. filesystem confirms 13/13 mirrored agents but devin -p roster prompt rejected tool call, no enumeration returned\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-13/failed-runs.md:17:**Recorded reason.** filesystem confirms 13/13 mirrored agents but devin -p roster prompt rejected tool call, no enumeration returned\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-16/skill-benchmark-report.md:46:| DV-015 | manual | commands-and-skills | — | FAIL: .devin/skills/speckit-plan does not exist; devin -p /speckit-plan rejected tool call, no plan output |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-16/findings-and-recommendations.md:7:## 1. .devin/skills/speckit-plan does not exist; devin -p /speckit-plan rejected tool call, no plan output\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin/benchmark/reports/2026-08-08--manual-testing-playbook--devin-16/failed-runs.md:17:**Recorded reason.** .devin/skills/speckit-plan does not exist; devin -p /speckit-plan rejected tool call, no plan output\n== hermes\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-15-phase-008-third-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:51:| HERMES-018 | skills-and-plugins | **PASS** | 0 | 171 | nested hermes chat refused with the plugin's self-invocation message |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-second-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:45:| HERMES-018 | skills-and-plugins | PASS | 0 | 19 | nested hermes chat refused by the plugin with the packet's self-invocation message |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-second-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:64:- Three dispatches were written into a scratch shell script and run as `bash <script>`, because this environment's own PreToolUse guard refuses a write-shaped `hermes chat` command line that lacks `--yolo`. That is stated in each affected scenario's evidence.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-first-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:44:| HERMES-018 | skills-and-plugins | PASS | 0 | 19 | nested hermes chat refused by the plugin with the packet's self-invocation message; no nested session started |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/benchmark/reports/2026-09-14-phase-008-first-pass/skill-benchmark-report.md:58:- Four dispatches had to be written into a scratch shell script and run as `bash <script>`, because this environment's own PreToolUse guard refuses a write-shaped `hermes chat` command line that lacks `--yolo`. That is stated in each affected scenario's evidence.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:51:`cli-hermes` is a first-class `ExecutorKind`, and `buildHermesLineageCommand` emits the one auditable headless shape a fan-out lineage runs: `hermes chat -Q --oneshot` with the prompt delivered on stdin.\n== opencode\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/README.md:22:This `benchmark/` tree holds reports **derived after the fact from a manual-testing-playbook validation run**, not the deep-improvement Lane C skill-benchmark harness -- no D1 to D5 dimension scoring applies here, and no field in this tree was written by a harness at run time. The archived run below packages an already-captured attempt to validate the OpenCode-native `opencode-goal` plugin's live injection path through headless `opencode run` -- the `CO-039` scenario's Optional Supplemental Check, not its primary direct-in-process contract (which independently returned an overall PASS documented in the same playbook file). This tree tracks only the live-dispatch slice.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-10-20--manual-testing-playbook--plugin-utilization/skill-benchmark-report.md:25:| `CO-041-V1` | `cli-dispatch-audit` | 1.19.3 | PASS | refused opencode run --help by hard rule and appended an audit record |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:34:- Every verdict here is SKIP, not FAIL: both structural causes (tool not exposed, transform not fired) are a headless-surface limitation of `opencode run`, independent of model quality, and orthogonal to packet `032-goal-hooks-cross-runtime`.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/skill-benchmark-report.md:35:- This run covers only `CO-039`'s live headless `opencode run` supplemental check. The scenario's primary contract (direct in-process invocation of the shipped plugin) independently returned an overall PASS, documented in `cli-opencode/manual-testing-playbook/goal-hook/goal-hook.md`, not in this report.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/findings-and-recommendations.md:9:## 1. Headless `opencode run` cannot exercise opencode-goal's live injection path\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/benchmark/reports/2026-07-29--manual-testing-playbook--goal-hook/findings-and-recommendations.md:13:- **Observation, structural cause 2**: `experimental.chat.system.transform` does not fire in `opencode run --session`, even against a pre-seeded ACTIVE `opencode-goal` state file matching the shipped schema exactly (canary `GOALCANARY-CO-1010816640`); a resumed-session turn 2 asking \"what is my active goal?\" showed zero `[active_goal]` occurrences and the model reported none.\n== pi\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/changelog/v1.5.10.0.md:20:- **The supported-model allowlist smoke uses the operator's configured credentials.** The smoke runs `pi -p --offline --model llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash --tools read,grep,find,ls --no-extensions --no-skills --no-prompt-templates` on the operator's agent directory. The former step used an empty `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`, which had no credentials and could not reach a model. The 2026-09-23 run exited 0 in 17 seconds and listed only `read`, `grep`, `find` and `ls`.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:65:| `gpt-6.1-terra` | GPT-6.1 Terra. Dispatch-verified 2026-10-27: `pi -p --offline --model openai/gpt-6.1-terra --thinking low` replied `OK` |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:129:pi -p \"<prompt>\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:170:SYSTEM_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0 AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 PI_BLACKHOLE_PASSIVE=true pi -p \"<prompt>\" \\\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:181:- **Exit code is never an availability/auth signal** — an identical unauthenticated `pi -p` returned exit `0` then exit `1` across runs. Classify the captured output text (`No API key found...`), never the exit code. See [cli-reference.md](./cli-reference.md) §9.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/integration-patterns.md:88:  pi -p \"<scoped task>\" --mode text\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\\nfor n in claude-code codex cursor devin hermes opencode pi; do echo \\\"== $n\\\"; grep -rn -m6 -E \\\"claude -p|codex exec|opencode run|cursor-agent -p|devin -p|hermes chat|pi -p\\\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-$n --include=\\\"*.md\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -6; done\"}"},"time":{"start":1793915993115,"end":1793915993698}}}}
