{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793916018205,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adba1e1d001pKqEW1K32OJimw","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adb9f809001vkeRW23rNfcaUF","type":"step-start","snapshot":"107b78a16787ced2529408fdb5a5b1bb45a6bb01"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916031011,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adba2421001W9vFn5lY1TE1kd","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adb9f809001vkeRW23rNfcaUF","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ddff2b0fa92336d","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 1: Headless dispatch contract\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 1 of the ten-angle plan: what `dsh headless` accepts, emits and returns, and how that\ncontract compares with `pi -p` and the six other headless runtimes this repo already dispatches.\nThe goal is the exact command builder shape a `cli-deepseek` mode would emit, not a summary of the\nharness.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the generated CLI reference (`dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md`) and ran the read-only\n  `dsh headless --help` against the installed `0.2.2-rc.1`.\n- Read the headless bundle's own README, its `cordis.patch.yml` and its exit-mapping section.\n- Ran one permitted live smoke dispatch with `DSH_HOME` pointed inside the lineage directory, so\n  no write reached the operator's home. `dsh headless \"Reply with the single word OK\" </dev/null`.\n- Compared against `cli-pi`'s recorded CLI reference and the headless invocations named in the\n  other runtime packets.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. `dsh headless` takes the task as the positional argument (multiple words joined, `-` reads\n   stdin) and exposes exactly five real options: `--json`, `--session-id <id>`,\n   `--permission-mode <preset>`, `--approval-policy <ask|never>`, `--add-dir <path>` (repeatable),\n   plus `--help`. There is no `--model`, `--provider`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--cwd`, `--timeout`\n   or tool-allowlist flag. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\n2. The route, model and reasoning level are profile configuration, not dispatch flags: the runner\n   \"resolves the task and the shared `agentDefaultModel` selection\", and an adopted session\n   restores its saved route/effort unless the current deployment re-records it. Reasoning effort\n   is a model-catalog field (`reasoningEfforts`, or `effort` on a native route) and is saved by\n   `agentDefaultModel.saveSelection({ provider, model, reasoningEffort })`.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:128]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:53-54]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2102-2108]\n3. Working directory is the process cwd: the headless sandbox row sets\n   `workspaceRoot: process.cwd()` and `mode: process.env.DSH_PERMISSION_MODE ?? 'workspace-write'`.\n   A dispatch changes directory by changing the child process cwd, not by a flag.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:27-33]\n4. stdout carries only the final assistant answer (or the NDJSON `--json` stream); stderr carries\n   `dsh: reasoning:` deltas and `dsh: <code>: <message>` diagnostics. In `--json`, the stream is\n   `session` first, then `status`, `text`, `thinking`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `final`\n   last; every non-final string is capped at 8 KiB and a line at 32 KiB, with `truncated` flags.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:36]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:104]\n5. Exit status is a two-value contract: `0` only when the last turn ends `completed`; `1` for\n   aborted, error, no turn in the owned interval, usage errors, or an unusable `--session-id`.\n   A failing provider is not a distinct code. The trustworthy completion signal is the pair\n   \"process exit 0 AND `final.reason.kind === 'completed'`\", and the JSON `tool_result.error`\n   preserves the typed `{name, code}` that separates a policy denial (`AUTO_REVIEW_DENIED`) from a\n   reviewer failure. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:94]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:136]\n6. Live smoke on the installed package confirms the failure shape: exit 1, empty stdout, stderr\n   `dsh: MISSING_CREDENTIAL: llm-deepseek: no API key for provider route \"deepseek-official\";\n   store DEEPSEEK_API_KEY through the credentials service ... or export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`.\n   The same run initialized `$DSH_HOME/profiles/headless` from the shipped template and created a\n   session directory, so first boot needs no `pnpm install` and no manual profile creation.\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.events/smoke-1.stderr]\n7. Headless disables the managed credential store, `authorization` and `deepseek-account` rows.\n   API keys are read from the launch environment, then `<invocation cwd>/.env`, then\n   `$DSH_HOME/.env`; GUI-saved keys are ignored without modifying their file. This is the opposite\n   of `pi`'s stored-agent-directory model and means a repo-local `.env` is a viable, documented\n   key path for a `cli-deepseek` dispatch without touching `$DSH_HOME`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:56]\n8. Compared with `pi -p`, the harness moves every per-dispatch lever into configuration: Pi takes\n   `--provider`, `--model`, `--thinking`, `--tools`, `--skill`, `--session`, `--no-context-files`\n   on the command line, while `dsh headless` takes only permission and session identity. A faithful\n   `cli-pi` mirror therefore needs a repo-local profile overlay that pins the model roster and a\n   dispatch builder that passes the prompt on stdin and closes it, not a long flag string.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:94-96]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:112-134]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating exit `1` as a provider-auth signal: the contract collapses aborts, denials, timeouts and\n  missing credentials into one code. Classification must read the `dsh: <code>:` stderr line or the\n  JSON event stream.\n- Adding a `--model` flag to a hoped-for dispatch builder: the installed help has no such option.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Probing a successful dispatch: no provider key exists on this machine, and creating one is out of\n  bounds. The failure contract is the deliverable, not a passing reply.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: none; Angle 1 names the exact commands.\n- Contradictory evidence: none; the generated help, the installed live help and the bundle README\n  agree.\n- Missing dependencies: no provider credential (expected, recorded as the failure shape).\n- Partial success: the smoke reaches the provider boundary, so boot, task parsing, profile\n  initialization and credential failure are all observed, but no successful turn is.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12,36,46,56,94,104,128,136,190`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:27-33`\n- `dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:53-54`\n- `dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2102-2108`\n- Live `dsh headless --help` on 0.2.2-rc.1, exit 0\n- Live `dsh headless \"Reply with the single word OK\"` smoke, exit 1, stderr quoted above\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:94-134`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.86 (five fully new findings, two partially new against the resource map's\n  already-known launcher shape)\n- Questions addressed: Angle 1 headless contract and runtime comparison\n- Questions answered: What exactly does `dsh headless` accept, emit and return, and how does it compare with `pi -p` and the other seven runtimes' headless contracts?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: the generated `docs/cli-help.md` is authoritative and version-matched, and\n  the bundle README documents the exit mapping that the help omits. Pointing `DSH_HOME` inside the\n  lineage made a live failure observable without touching the operator's home.\n- What did not work and why: macOS has no `timeout`, so the first smoke attempt failed with exit\n  127 before the harness ran; the retry used `perl -e 'alarm 120; exec @ARGV'`.\n- What I would do differently: run the smoke before reading the README, so the failure text can\n  validate the documented mapping rather than illustrate it.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 2: providers, models and reasoning levels, including whether the LLM Gateway and OpenCode Go\ncan be expressed as custom OpenAI-compatible routes and what a closed roster would look like.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 1: Headless dispatch contract\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 1 of the ten-angle plan: what `dsh headless` accepts, emits and returns, and how that\\ncontract compares with `pi -p` and the six other headless runtimes this repo already dispatches.\\nThe goal is the exact command builder shape a `cli-deepseek` mode would emit, not a summary of the\\nharness.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Read the generated CLI reference (`dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md`) and ran the read-only\\n  `dsh headless --help` against the installed `0.2.2-rc.1`.\\n- Read the headless bundle's own README, its `cordis.patch.yml` and its exit-mapping section.\\n- Ran one permitted live smoke dispatch with `DSH_HOME` pointed inside the lineage directory, so\\n  no write reached the operator's home. `dsh headless \\\"Reply with the single word OK\\\" </dev/null`.\\n- Compared against `cli-pi`'s recorded CLI reference and the headless invocations named in the\\n  other runtime packets.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. `dsh headless` takes the task as the positional argument (multiple words joined, `-` reads\\n   stdin) and exposes exactly five real options: `--json`, `--session-id <id>`,\\n   `--permission-mode <preset>`, `--approval-policy <ask|never>`, `--add-dir <path>` (repeatable),\\n   plus `--help`. There is no `--model`, `--provider`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--cwd`, `--timeout`\\n   or tool-allowlist flag. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\\n2. The route, model and reasoning level are profile configuration, not dispatch flags: the runner\\n   \\\"resolves the task and the shared `agentDefaultModel` selection\\\", and an adopted session\\n   restores its saved route/effort unless the current deployment re-records it. Reasoning effort\\n   is a model-catalog field (`reasoningEfforts`, or `effort` on a native route) and is saved by\\n   `agentDefaultModel.saveSelection({ provider, model, reasoningEffort })`.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:128]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:53-54]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2102-2108]\\n3. Working directory is the process cwd: the headless sandbox row sets\\n   `workspaceRoot: process.cwd()` and `mode: process.env.DSH_PERMISSION_MODE ?? 'workspace-write'`.\\n   A dispatch changes directory by changing the child process cwd, not by a flag.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:27-33]\\n4. stdout carries only the final assistant answer (or the NDJSON `--json` stream); stderr carries\\n   `dsh: reasoning:` deltas and `dsh: <code>: <message>` diagnostics. In `--json`, the stream is\\n   `session` first, then `status`, `text`, `thinking`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `final`\\n   last; every non-final string is capped at 8 KiB and a line at 32 KiB, with `truncated` flags.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:36]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:104]\\n5. Exit status is a two-value contract: `0` only when the last turn ends `completed`; `1` for\\n   aborted, error, no turn in the owned interval, usage errors, or an unusable `--session-id`.\\n   A failing provider is not a distinct code. The trustworthy completion signal is the pair\\n   \\\"process exit 0 AND `final.reason.kind === 'completed'`\\\", and the JSON `tool_result.error`\\n   preserves the typed `{name, code}` that separates a policy denial (`AUTO_REVIEW_DENIED`) from a\\n   reviewer failure. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:94]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:136]\\n6. Live smoke on the installed package confirms the failure shape: exit 1, empty stdout, stderr\\n   `dsh: MISSING_CREDENTIAL: llm-deepseek: no API key for provider route \\\"deepseek-official\\\";\\n   store DEEPSEEK_API_KEY through the credentials service ... or export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`.\\n   The same run initialized `$DSH_HOME/profiles/headless` from the shipped template and created a\\n   session directory, so first boot needs no `pnpm install` and no manual profile creation.\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.events/smoke-1.stderr]\\n7. Headless disables the managed credential store, `authorization` and `deepseek-account` rows.\\n   API keys are read from the launch environment, then `<invocation cwd>/.env`, then\\n   `$DSH_HOME/.env`; GUI-saved keys are ignored without modifying their file. This is the opposite\\n   of `pi`'s stored-agent-directory model and means a repo-local `.env` is a viable, documented\\n   key path for a `cli-deepseek` dispatch without touching `$DSH_HOME`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:56]\\n8. Compared with `pi -p`, the harness moves every per-dispatch lever into configuration: Pi takes\\n   `--provider`, `--model`, `--thinking`, `--tools`, `--skill`, `--session`, `--no-context-files`\\n   on the command line, while `dsh headless` takes only permission and session identity. A faithful\\n   `cli-pi` mirror therefore needs a repo-local profile overlay that pins the model roster and a\\n   dispatch builder that passes the prompt on stdin and closes it, not a long flag string.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:94-96]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:112-134]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating exit `1` as a provider-auth signal: the contract collapses aborts, denials, timeouts and\\n  missing credentials into one code. Classification must read the `dsh: <code>:` stderr line or the\\n  JSON event stream.\\n- Adding a `--model` flag to a hoped-for dispatch builder: the installed help has no such option.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Probing a successful dispatch: no provider key exists on this machine, and creating one is out of\\n  bounds. The failure contract is the deliverable, not a passing reply.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: none; Angle 1 names the exact commands.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none; the generated help, the installed live help and the bundle README\\n  agree.\\n- Missing dependencies: no provider credential (expected, recorded as the failure shape).\\n- Partial success: the smoke reaches the provider boundary, so boot, task parsing, profile\\n  initialization and credential failure are all observed, but no successful turn is.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12,36,46,56,94,104,128,136,190`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:27-33`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:53-54`\\n- `dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2102-2108`\\n- Live `dsh headless --help` on 0.2.2-rc.1, exit 0\\n- Live `dsh headless \\\"Reply with the single word OK\\\"` smoke, exit 1, stderr quoted above\\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:94-134`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.86 (five fully new findings, two partially new against the resource map's\\n  already-known launcher shape)\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 1 headless contract and runtime comparison\\n- Questions answered: What exactly does `dsh headless` accept, emit and return, and how does it compare with `pi -p` and the other seven runtimes' headless contracts?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: the generated `docs/cli-help.md` is authoritative and version-matched, and\\n  the bundle README documents the exit mapping that the help omits. Pointing `DSH_HOME` inside the\\n  lineage made a live failure observable without touching the operator's home.\\n- What did not work and why: macOS has no `timeout`, so the first smoke attempt failed with exit\\n  127 before the harness ran; the retry used `perl -e 'alarm 120; exec @ARGV'`.\\n- What I would do differently: run the smoke before reading the README, so the failure text can\\n  validate the documented mapping rather than illustrate it.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 2: providers, models and reasoning levels, including whether the LLM Gateway and OpenCode Go\\ncan be expressed as custom OpenAI-compatible routes and what a closed roster would look like.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916019745,"end":1793916031011}}}}
