{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793916071866,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adbaefba001TkoawS2t4mAwHi","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbaea600014nniQ16tW4UaUG","type":"step-start","snapshot":"273ae4a0e9604c5e0d4fad4fd5ae1650815a5eb3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916081188,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbaf89d001JevGTExlbSkler","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbaea600014nniQ16tW4UaUG","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-afb1f041fa73d662","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 2: Providers, models and reasoning\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 2: how the harness declares providers and models, whether the operator's two DeepSeek V4.1\nFlash routes can be expressed, how reasoning levels work, and what a closed, fail-closed roster\nlooks like for a mode that mirrors `cli-pi`.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the provider guide's custom-model and reasoning sections.\n- Read the `llm-pi-ai` package reference for the route schema, credential reference semantics and\n  stable error codes.\n- Read the base bundle patch to find the shipped default route.\n- Cross-checked the operator's route facts against `cli-pi`'s provider roster, which already\n  records the two gateway shapes and their compatibility quirks.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. A custom OpenAI-compatible route is a `llm-pi-ai` row in\n   `$DSH_HOME/profiles/<profile>/cordis.patch.yml`: `providers.<id>` with `apiKeyEnv`, `api`\n   (one of `openai-completions`, `openai-responses`, `anthropic-messages`), `baseURL` and a\n   non-empty `models` list. The provider id is permanent, lowercase and hyphenated; one provider\n   speaks one protocol, so a gateway serving two protocols needs two providers.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:27-33]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:123]\n2. The LLM Gateway route is expressible with no harness change:\n   `llmgateway` + `api: openai-completions` + `baseURL: https://api.llmgateway.io/v1` +\n   `models: [{id: deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017}]`. Two compatibility facts travel with it: the gateway\n   takes the bare model id (a provider-prefixed id returns HTTP 400), and its `runware` upstream\n   refuses the `developer` role, which pi-ai sends to reasoning models unless\n   `compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false` is set. This is an inference from the harness schema plus\n   the route behavior already recorded by `cli-pi`, not a live dispatch.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:89]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:99]\n3. The OpenCode Go route is expressible the same way: id `opencode-go`, base URL\n   `https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1`, `api: openai-completions`, model\n   `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, `max` effort. Its declaration is not its availability: the live smoke\n   recorded in the resource map failed with `[overloaded] the server is overloaded`, exit 1, so a\n   closed roster must separate \"configured\" from \"reachable\".\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:52-54]\n4. Reasoning levels are declared per model as `reasoningEfforts`, a map from level to the wire\n   spelling sent as `reasoning_effort`; `max` is a real level, and a route-level `reasoning` sets\n   the default while a session has chosen none. DeepSeek's built-in route already offers\n   `off`, `low`, `high` and `max`; a hand-declared model declares none until the profile adds them,\n   and an unsupported selection is refused as `UNSUPPORTED_REASONING_EFFORT`.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:134-166]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2225]\n5. DeepSeek V4 behind an OpenAI-compatible gateway needs `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` so that\n   `off` sends `thinking: {type: disabled}` and every other level sends\n   `thinking: {type: enabled}` beside the effort. Without it, `off` is only the absence of\n   `reasoning_effort`, and a model that thinks unless told not to will still think.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:155-166]\n6. `apiKeyEnv` is a credential reference resolved per request through the credential seam, so no\n   secret enters a config file; a reference that resolves to nothing fails with\n   `MISSING_CREDENTIAL`, an unusable key with `INVALID_CREDENTIAL`, an unconfigured model id with\n   `UNKNOWN_MODEL`, and terminal provider failures distinguish `QUOTA` from `RATE_LIMIT`.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:38]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:123]\n7. The shipped default route is `agent-default-model` with `provider: deepseek-official` and\n   `model: deepseek-flash`. That row is the per-dispatch lever a `--model` flag would have been:\n   a `--patch <path>` overlay can replace it with `provider`, `model` and `reasoningEffort`, which\n   is how a dispatch selects one route from a closed roster without editing `$DSH_HOME`.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:90-94]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:22-33]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42]\n8. Fail-closed is only partly native: the adapter refuses an unconfigured model id, but\n   `agent-default-model` \"does not validate catalog membership\" and leaves availability diagnostics\n   to the consumer opening the request. A closed roster therefore needs the skill packet and the\n   dispatch preflight guard to pin both the provider and the model, mirroring `cli-pi`'s\n   `pi-provider-qualified-model` rule rather than relying on the harness to reject a stray id.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:33]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/hard-rules.json:28-35]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A `--model`/`--provider` dispatch flag: headless exposes none.\n- Relying on the harness catalog to enforce a model allowlist: it validates only what the profile\n  declares, and the default-model service does not check catalog membership.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Live verifying either gateway through `dsh`: requires writing a real key into a profile, which is\n  out of bounds and would leave operator credentials in the lineage.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"reasoning levels per model\" could mean the catalog ladder or the wire spelling;\n  both are recorded, since the map's value is the spelling.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: no configured key, so every route fact is documentation plus Pi-route\n  behavior rather than a live dsh dispatch.\n- Partial success: route shape and reasoning semantics are confirmed from source; gateway\n  compatibility is inferred.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:27-33,134-166`\n- `dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:38,123`\n- `dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:22-33`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:90-94`\n- `dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2225`\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42`\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:89,99`\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/hard-rules.json:28-35`\n- `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:46-55`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.79 (four fully new findings, three that extend resource-map facts)\n- Questions addressed: Angle 2 providers, models, reasoning and roster\n- Questions answered: How are providers, models and reasoning levels configured, and can LLM Gateway and OpenCode Go be added as closed, fail-closed routes?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: the provider guide is written for the exact custom-gateway case, and the\n  `llm-pi-ai` reference supplies the error-code contract the guide omits. Reading the base bundle\n  patch found the default route, which is the missing piece for per-dispatch selection.\n- What did not work and why: no route could be exercised, because that needs a credential write.\n- What I would do differently: check the base bundle first, since `deepseek-official` explains the\n  smoke failure from iteration 1 and would have shortened that diagnosis.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 3: profiles, `$DSH_HOME` and repo-local configuration, including what a `.dsh/` runtime folder\nmust contain and which files can be generated from `.skilled/`.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 2: Providers, models and reasoning\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 2: how the harness declares providers and models, whether the operator's two DeepSeek V4.1\\nFlash routes can be expressed, how reasoning levels work, and what a closed, fail-closed roster\\nlooks like for a mode that mirrors `cli-pi`.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Read the provider guide's custom-model and reasoning sections.\\n- Read the `llm-pi-ai` package reference for the route schema, credential reference semantics and\\n  stable error codes.\\n- Read the base bundle patch to find the shipped default route.\\n- Cross-checked the operator's route facts against `cli-pi`'s provider roster, which already\\n  records the two gateway shapes and their compatibility quirks.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. A custom OpenAI-compatible route is a `llm-pi-ai` row in\\n   `$DSH_HOME/profiles/<profile>/cordis.patch.yml`: `providers.<id>` with `apiKeyEnv`, `api`\\n   (one of `openai-completions`, `openai-responses`, `anthropic-messages`), `baseURL` and a\\n   non-empty `models` list. The provider id is permanent, lowercase and hyphenated; one provider\\n   speaks one protocol, so a gateway serving two protocols needs two providers.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:27-33]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:123]\\n2. The LLM Gateway route is expressible with no harness change:\\n   `llmgateway` + `api: openai-completions` + `baseURL: https://api.llmgateway.io/v1` +\\n   `models: [{id: deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017}]`. Two compatibility facts travel with it: the gateway\\n   takes the bare model id (a provider-prefixed id returns HTTP 400), and its `runware` upstream\\n   refuses the `developer` role, which pi-ai sends to reasoning models unless\\n   `compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false` is set. This is an inference from the harness schema plus\\n   the route behavior already recorded by `cli-pi`, not a live dispatch.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:89]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:99]\\n3. The OpenCode Go route is expressible the same way: id `opencode-go`, base URL\\n   `https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1`, `api: openai-completions`, model\\n   `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, `max` effort. Its declaration is not its availability: the live smoke\\n   recorded in the resource map failed with `[overloaded] the server is overloaded`, exit 1, so a\\n   closed roster must separate \\\"configured\\\" from \\\"reachable\\\".\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:52-54]\\n4. Reasoning levels are declared per model as `reasoningEfforts`, a map from level to the wire\\n   spelling sent as `reasoning_effort`; `max` is a real level, and a route-level `reasoning` sets\\n   the default while a session has chosen none. DeepSeek's built-in route already offers\\n   `off`, `low`, `high` and `max`; a hand-declared model declares none until the profile adds them,\\n   and an unsupported selection is refused as `UNSUPPORTED_REASONING_EFFORT`.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:134-166]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2225]\\n5. DeepSeek V4 behind an OpenAI-compatible gateway needs `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` so that\\n   `off` sends `thinking: {type: disabled}` and every other level sends\\n   `thinking: {type: enabled}` beside the effort. Without it, `off` is only the absence of\\n   `reasoning_effort`, and a model that thinks unless told not to will still think.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:155-166]\\n6. `apiKeyEnv` is a credential reference resolved per request through the credential seam, so no\\n   secret enters a config file; a reference that resolves to nothing fails with\\n   `MISSING_CREDENTIAL`, an unusable key with `INVALID_CREDENTIAL`, an unconfigured model id with\\n   `UNKNOWN_MODEL`, and terminal provider failures distinguish `QUOTA` from `RATE_LIMIT`.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:38]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:123]\\n7. The shipped default route is `agent-default-model` with `provider: deepseek-official` and\\n   `model: deepseek-flash`. That row is the per-dispatch lever a `--model` flag would have been:\\n   a `--patch <path>` overlay can replace it with `provider`, `model` and `reasoningEffort`, which\\n   is how a dispatch selects one route from a closed roster without editing `$DSH_HOME`.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:90-94]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:22-33]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42]\\n8. Fail-closed is only partly native: the adapter refuses an unconfigured model id, but\\n   `agent-default-model` \\\"does not validate catalog membership\\\" and leaves availability diagnostics\\n   to the consumer opening the request. A closed roster therefore needs the skill packet and the\\n   dispatch preflight guard to pin both the provider and the model, mirroring `cli-pi`'s\\n   `pi-provider-qualified-model` rule rather than relying on the harness to reject a stray id.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:33]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/hard-rules.json:28-35]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A `--model`/`--provider` dispatch flag: headless exposes none.\\n- Relying on the harness catalog to enforce a model allowlist: it validates only what the profile\\n  declares, and the default-model service does not check catalog membership.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Live verifying either gateway through `dsh`: requires writing a real key into a profile, which is\\n  out of bounds and would leave operator credentials in the lineage.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"reasoning levels per model\\\" could mean the catalog ladder or the wire spelling;\\n  both are recorded, since the map's value is the spelling.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: no configured key, so every route fact is documentation plus Pi-route\\n  behavior rather than a live dsh dispatch.\\n- Partial success: route shape and reasoning semantics are confirmed from source; gateway\\n  compatibility is inferred.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:27-33,134-166`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:38,123`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:22-33`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:90-94`\\n- `dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2225`\\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42`\\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:89,99`\\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/hard-rules.json:28-35`\\n- `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:46-55`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.79 (four fully new findings, three that extend resource-map facts)\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 2 providers, models, reasoning and roster\\n- Questions answered: How are providers, models and reasoning levels configured, and can LLM Gateway and OpenCode Go be added as closed, fail-closed routes?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: the provider guide is written for the exact custom-gateway case, and the\\n  `llm-pi-ai` reference supplies the error-code contract the guide omits. Reading the base bundle\\n  patch found the default route, which is the missing piece for per-dispatch selection.\\n- What did not work and why: no route could be exercised, because that needs a credential write.\\n- What I would do differently: check the base bundle first, since `deepseek-official` explains the\\n  smoke failure from iteration 1 and would have shortened that diagnosis.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 3: profiles, `$DSH_HOME` and repo-local configuration, including what a `.dsh/` runtime folder\\nmust contain and which files can be generated from `.skilled/`.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916074141,"end":1793916081188}}}}
