in gets its own maxBytes budget, 65,536 bytes in dsh-base, dropping broader files before truncating the most specific; loading refreshes on cwd change and first-party read/write/edit touches, never on shell navigation.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"dsh-src/packages/context/agent-instructions/README.md:30-40\\\",\\\"dsh-src/packages/context/agent-instructions/README.md:74-76\\\",\\\"AGENTS.md:1\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"--patch <path> is the only repo-local configuration lever: a repeatable overlay applied after the profile layer with the same id/disabled/config row grammar, able to replace the default-model row, enable a route or disable a plugin per dispatch.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42\\\",\\\"dsh-src/apps/cli/config/examples/ptc.yml\\\",\\\"dsh-src/apps/cli/config/examples/team-mode.yml\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"DSH_HOME can be relocated per lineage; pointing it at a lineage subdirectory produced a self-contained headless profile, session tree and storages with no dependency on ~/.dsh, which is the fan-out state-isolation mechanism and the reason the repo folder must not itself be DSH_HOME.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.dsh-home/profiles/headless/cordis.yml\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"A .dsh/ repo folder has a smaller configuration surface than .pi/ or .hermes/: patches/ for overlays, SYNC.md, generated skills/agents/prompts trees, and a hand-authored plugins/ bridge, with no settings.json analogue because defaults are an agent-default-model row and settings persist into the active profile patch.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"dsh-src/packages/settings/settings/README.md:12-24\\