{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916164196,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbc5728001z99ld3kJCISox2","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbc487d001L3hVJba6gVrQkG","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-85a8ccea6953819a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\ngrep -n \"frontmatter\\|whenToUse\\|Frontmatter\\|parse\" packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts | head -25; echo \"===DUP===\"; grep -n \"duplicate\\|same name\\|wins\\|rank\" packages/skill/skill/README.md | head -15"},"output":"6: * user roots, parses YAML frontmatter, and loads bodies through `ctx.fs` when a\n19:import { parse as parseYaml } from 'yaml'\n113:  whenToUse?: string\n218:    const parsed = await parseSkillFile(locator.path, this.ctx, options.signal, candidate.source === 'bundled')\n219:    if (parsed === undefined) return undefined\n221:      name: parsed.name,\n222:      description: parsed.description,\n223:      ...parsed.whenToUse !== undefined ? { whenToUse: parsed.whenToUse } : {},\n224:      invocation: parsed.invocation,\n228:      path: parsed.path,\n229:      ...parsed.metadata !== undefined ? { metadata: parsed.metadata } : {},\n230:      content: parsed.content,\n748:    const parsed = await parseSkillFile(locator.path, ctx, undefined, root.trustedHost === true)\n749:    if (parsed === undefined) continue\n751:      name: parsed.name,\n752:      description: parsed.description,\n753:      ...parsed.whenToUse !== undefined ? { whenToUse: parsed.whenToUse } : {},\n754:      invocation: parsed.invocation,\n760:      path: parsed.path,\n761:      ...parsed.metadata !== undefined ? { metadata: parsed.metadata } : {},\n811:async function parseSkillFile(path: string, ctx: Context, signal?: AbortSignal, trustedHost = false): Promise<ParsedSkill | undefined> {\n817:  let parsed\n819:    parsed = parseFrontmatter(raw.content)\n821:    ctx.logger.warn(`skill file ${path} ignored: invalid YAML frontmatter: ${errorMessage(error)}`)\n824:  if (!parsed) {\n===DUP===\n12:Use this package to give agents and users one catalog of reusable, task-specific instructions collected from local directories, embedded plugin data, or remote services. It resolves duplicate names predictably, validates entries, tolerates unavailable sources without discarding usable results, and loads the selected skill's full instructions on demand. Mount it when a composition needs skills from multiple or non-filesystem sources; pair it with `dsh-skill-filesystem` for local discovery and `dsh-tool-skill` for model access, because it includes no skill content itself.\n52:- **Embedded skills.** Plugins register an in-memory skill with `ctx.skills.register(...)`; the registry fills in a default invocation policy and the `runtime` provider label. Same-name runtime registrations in one layer are first-wins with a warning.\n84:The registry is host+per-scope layered, the shape the tools registry established: a registration is filed into the layer of its calling context's scope — host rows and repository plugins land in the global layer, a plugin mounted by an agent preset's standing composition lands in that preset's layer. A read merges the global layer with the viewing scope's chain; the nearest layer wins a duplicate name outright, and within one layer duplicates resolve by rank, provider registration order, then provider-local order.\n94:A read (`list`/`snapshot`) collects each layer's candidates: runtime skills first, then each provider's `list()` result, awaiting providers sequentially and containing failures. Candidates are validated, deduplicated within the layer, and merged across layers; summaries sort by name. Completed collections are cached per cwd, scope chain, and revision up to `collectCacheMaxEntries`; an in-flight collection retries once when a provider or runtime mutation bumps the revision mid-read, and a second change returns the latest candidates as an incomplete, uncached observation.\n102:The registry has no TTL: only a provider calling its registration-scoped `invalidate()`, or a runtime registration or disposal, clears completed catalogs. Each invalidation bumps a revision, clears the cache, and emits the unfiltered `skills/change` event; consumers refetch with their own lookup options. `invalidate()` takes effect only while the exact registration that received it is still active, so a late callback cannot disturb a replacement provider with the same name.\n140:- **Duplicate resolution is first-wins** — later lower-priority candidates within a layer are logged and hidden, and a nearer layer shadows a farther one silently; there is no API to inspect all shadowed definitions.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"6: * user roots, parses YAML frontmatter, and loads bodies through `ctx.fs` when a\n19:import { parse as parseYaml } from 'yaml'\n113:  whenToUse?: string\n218:    const parsed = await parseSkillFile(locator.path, this.ctx, options.signal, candidate.source === 'bundled')\n219:    if (parsed === undefined) return undefined\n221:      name: parsed.name,\n222:      description: parsed.description,\n223:      ...parsed.whenToUse !== undefined ? { whenToUse: parsed.whenToUse } : {},\n224:      invocation: parsed.invocation,\n228:      path: parsed.path,\n229:      ...parsed.metadata !== undefined ? { metadata: parsed.metadata } : {},\n230:      content: parsed.content,\n748:    const parsed = await parseSkillFile(locator.path, ctx, undefined, root.trustedHost === true)\n749:    if (parsed === undefined) continue\n751:      name: parsed.name,\n752:      description: parsed.description,\n753:      ...parsed.whenToUse !== undefined ? { whenToUse: parsed.whenToUse } : {},\n754:      invocation: parsed.invocation,\n760:      path: parsed.path,\n761:      ...parsed.metadata !== undefined ? { metadata: parsed.metadata } : {},\n811:async function parseSkillFile(path: string, ctx: Context, signal?: AbortSignal, trustedHost = false): Promise<ParsedSkill | undefined> {\n817:  let parsed\n819:    parsed = parseFrontmatter(raw.content)\n821:    ctx.logger.warn(`skill file ${path} ignored: invalid YAML frontmatter: ${errorMessage(error)}`)\n824:  if (!parsed) {\n===DUP===\n12:Use this package to give agents and users one catalog of reusable, task-specific instructions collected from local directories, embedded plugin data, or remote services. It resolves duplicate names predictably, validates entries, tolerates unavailable sources without discarding usable results, and loads the selected skill's full instructions on demand. Mount it when a composition needs skills from multiple or non-filesystem sources; pair it with `dsh-skill-filesystem` for local discovery and `dsh-tool-skill` for model access, because it includes no skill content itself.\n52:- **Embedded skills.** Plugins register an in-memory skill with `ctx.skills.register(...)`; the registry fills in a default invocation policy and the `runtime` provider label. Same-name runtime registrations in one layer are first-wins with a warning.\n84:The registry is host+per-scope layered, the shape the tools registry established: a registration is filed into the layer of its calling context's scope — host rows and repository plugins land in the global layer, a plugin mounted by an agent preset's standing composition lands in that preset's layer. A read merges the global layer with the viewing scope's chain; the nearest layer wins a duplicate name outright, and within one layer duplicates resolve by rank, provider registration order, then provider-local order.\n94:A read (`list`/`snapshot`) collects each layer's candidates: runtime skills first, then each provider's `list()` result, awaiting providers sequentially and containing failures. Candidates are validated, deduplicated within the layer, and merged across layers; summaries sort by name. Completed collections are cached per cwd, scope chain, and revision up to `collectCacheMaxEntries`; an in-flight collection retries once when a provider or runtime mutation bumps the revision mid-read, and a second change returns the latest candidates as an incomplete, uncached observation.\n102:The registry has no TTL: only a provider calling its registration-scoped `invalidate()`, or a runtime registration or disposal, clears completed catalogs. Each invalidation bumps a revision, clears the cache, and emits the unfiltered `skills/change` event; consumers refetch with their own lookup options. `invalidate()` takes effect only while the exact registration that received it is still active, so a late callback cannot disturb a replacement provider with the same name.\n140:- **Duplicate resolution is first-wins** — later lower-priority candidates within a layer are logged and hidden, and a nearer layer shadows a farther one silently; there is no API to inspect all shadowed definitions.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\ngrep -n \\\"frontmatter\\\\|whenToUse\\\\|Frontmatter\\\\|parse\\\" packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts | head -25; echo \\\"===DUP===\\\"; grep -n \\\"duplicate\\\\|same name\\\\|wins\\\\|rank\\\" packages/skill/skill/README.md | head -15\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916163880,"end":1793916164196}}}}
