{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916184825,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbc84400018A6a6CUFSZZLfp","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbc7e6f001tzTY2kCw81yNFn","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-996e8544f1721e89","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 4: Skills\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 4: the harness skill format, the directories it scans, frontmatter keys and limits, how far\nthis repo's `SKILL.md` format is from it, whether parent hubs load one skill each or must be\nflattened, and whether `.dsh/skills` should be a generated copy tree or a symlink.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the `skill`, `skill-filesystem` and `tool-skill` package references.\n- Read the filesystem provider's source for frontmatter parsing and name validation.\n- Counted this repo's canonical skill tree: 16 top-level skill directories, 57 `SKILL.md` files.\n- Compared against the `.pi/skills` symlink and the `.hermes/skills` generated-copy precedent.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. Discovery is exactly one level deep: a skill is `<root>/<name>/SKILL.md` or `<root>/<name>.md`,\n   and nested `**/SKILL.md` files are deliberately not discovered.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:147]\n2. The consequence is decisive for this repo: `.skilled/skills` has 16 top-level hub directories but\n   57 `SKILL.md` files, so a whole-tree symlink at `.dsh/skills` would surface only the 16 hubs and\n   hide the 41 nested mode packets (`cli-pi`, `deep-research`, `sk-code` modes, and the rest).\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md:1]\n3. Roots are ranked: `<projectRoot>/.dsh/skills` (100), `<projectRoot>/.agents/skills` (200),\n   configured `customSkillDirs` (300), `<dshHome>/skills` (400), `<agentsHome>/skills` (500), and an\n   optional bundled root (600). The project root is the nearest ancestor containing `.git`, else the\n   cwd, so the repo root is the scope for a checkout. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:46-56]\n4. Frontmatter requires a kebab-case `name` and a `description`; optional keys are `whenToUse`,\n   `metadata`, `disable-model-invocation` and `user-invocable`. The parser reads only those keys, so\n   this repo's extra `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`, `allowed-tools` and\n   `version` fields are ignored rather than fatal. `allowed-tools` is not enforced by the harness.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts:811-850]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:21-36]\n5. There is no content scanner, quarantine or skill size limit. An invalid file is skipped with a\n   warning the model never sees; a root that fails to read is omitted and retried on the next\n   lookup; the body is read on demand, so an oversized body costs only the load. The catalog\n   description is normalized and capped at 500 characters by default\n   (`catalogDescriptionMaxLength`). [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:85]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/tool-skill/README.md:48]\n6. Symlinked directories are explicitly supported: catalog entries and loaded skills expose the\n   resolved instruction-file path, and \"symlinked directories and flat files can open as regular-file\n   previews\"; reload locators keep the discovered path. A per-skill symlink farm therefore preserves\n   each packet's `references/`, `scripts/` and `assets/` while satisfying the one-level rule.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:40]\n7. Duplicate names resolve by layer first, then root rank, then provider order, with the loser hidden\n   and logged. Project-root skills at rank 100 therefore shadow a same-named skill in\n   `$DSH_HOME/skills` or `~/.agents/skills`, which makes a checked-in `.dsh/skills` authoritative\n   for a checkout. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:84]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/README.md:140]\n8. The smallest correct move is a generated per-skill symlink farm, not a whole-tree symlink and not\n   a markdown-only copy tree: 57 entries, each pointing at its canonical directory. Hermes needed\n   copies because its scanner quarantined linked trees; dsh has no scanner, and Pi's whole-directory\n   link would lose 41 skills here. [SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:20-26]\n   [SOURCE: .pi/SYNC.md:32-34]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A whole-directory symlink `.dsh/skills -> .skilled/skills`: one-level discovery would expose only\n  the 16 hubs.\n- Markdown-only generated copies: they would lose `references/`, `assets/` and `scripts/` unless\n  every body carried a canonical pointer, and the harness has no scanner reason to avoid links.\n- Editing canonical `SKILL.md` files to add `whenToUse` or invocation keys: extra keys are optional,\n  and changing 57 files is out of this phase's scope.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a quarantine or scan path: none exists in the filesystem provider; the only failure\n  handling is warn-and-skip.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"flatten into every nested mode\" could mean rewriting bodies or exposing each as\n  its own catalog entry; the second is what the loader supports, and it needs no body change.\n- Contradictory evidence: Pi's whole-dir symlink works there because Pi's skill discovery is\n  recursive or explicit-path based; the same mechanism does not transfer to dsh.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: the symlink behavior is documented and its code path preserves the resolved path,\n  but no dsh session with a `.dsh/skills` farm was run (that would require configuring a provider).\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36-56,85,147`\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts:811-850`\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:21-36,84`\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/README.md:140`\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/tool-skill/README.md:48`\n- `.pi/SYNC.md:32-34`, `.hermes/SYNC.md:20-26`\n- Repo skill tree counts: 16 top-level directories, 57 `SKILL.md` files\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.93 (six fully new findings, one that extends the `.pi`/`.hermes`\n  precedent into a dsh-specific decision)\n- Questions addressed: Angle 4 skill format, roots, limits and mirror mechanism\n- Questions answered: What skill format does the harness load, and should this repo use generated copies or symlinks?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: counting the tree before reading the loader contract turned an abstract\n  \"symlink or copy\" question into an arithmetic one, and the one-level rule decided it.\n- What did not work and why: the README's \"nested SKILL.md deliberately not discovered\" line is easy\n  to miss under a table; the source-level parser check confirmed the frontmatter compatibility claim.\n- What I would do differently: count the tree in iteration 3, since the `.dsh/` folder inventory\n  needed that number to be honest.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 5: agents, subagents, commands and goal, including whether `.skilled/agents` can be reached\nas harness subagents or presets and how the 35 nested commands can be exposed.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 4: Skills\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 4: the harness skill format, the directories it scans, frontmatter keys and limits, how far\\nthis repo's `SKILL.md` format is from it, whether parent hubs load one skill each or must be\\nflattened, and whether `.dsh/skills` should be a generated copy tree or a symlink.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Read the `skill`, `skill-filesystem` and `tool-skill` package references.\\n- Read the filesystem provider's source for frontmatter parsing and name validation.\\n- Counted this repo's canonical skill tree: 16 top-level skill directories, 57 `SKILL.md` files.\\n- Compared against the `.pi/skills` symlink and the `.hermes/skills` generated-copy precedent.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. Discovery is exactly one level deep: a skill is `<root>/<name>/SKILL.md` or `<root>/<name>.md`,\\n   and nested `**/SKILL.md` files are deliberately not discovered.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:147]\\n2. The consequence is decisive for this repo: `.skilled/skills` has 16 top-level hub directories but\\n   57 `SKILL.md` files, so a whole-tree symlink at `.dsh/skills` would surface only the 16 hubs and\\n   hide the 41 nested mode packets (`cli-pi`, `deep-research`, `sk-code` modes, and the rest).\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md:1]\\n3. Roots are ranked: `<projectRoot>/.dsh/skills` (100), `<projectRoot>/.agents/skills` (200),\\n   configured `customSkillDirs` (300), `<dshHome>/skills` (400), `<agentsHome>/skills` (500), and an\\n   optional bundled root (600). The project root is the nearest ancestor containing `.git`, else the\\n   cwd, so the repo root is the scope for a checkout. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:46-56]\\n4. Frontmatter requires a kebab-case `name` and a `description`; optional keys are `whenToUse`,\\n   `metadata`, `disable-model-invocation` and `user-invocable`. The parser reads only those keys, so\\n   this repo's extra `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`, `allowed-tools` and\\n   `version` fields are ignored rather than fatal. `allowed-tools` is not enforced by the harness.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts:811-850]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:21-36]\\n5. There is no content scanner, quarantine or skill size limit. An invalid file is skipped with a\\n   warning the model never sees; a root that fails to read is omitted and retried on the next\\n   lookup; the body is read on demand, so an oversized body costs only the load. The catalog\\n   description is normalized and capped at 500 characters by default\\n   (`catalogDescriptionMaxLength`). [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:85]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/tool-skill/README.md:48]\\n6. Symlinked directories are explicitly supported: catalog entries and loaded skills expose the\\n   resolved instruction-file path, and \\\"symlinked directories and flat files can open as regular-file\\n   previews\\\"; reload locators keep the discovered path. A per-skill symlink farm therefore preserves\\n   each packet's `references/`, `scripts/` and `assets/` while satisfying the one-level rule.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:40]\\n7. Duplicate names resolve by layer first, then root rank, then provider order, with the loser hidden\\n   and logged. Project-root skills at rank 100 therefore shadow a same-named skill in\\n   `$DSH_HOME/skills` or `~/.agents/skills`, which makes a checked-in `.dsh/skills` authoritative\\n   for a checkout. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:84]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/README.md:140]\\n8. The smallest correct move is a generated per-skill symlink farm, not a whole-tree symlink and not\\n   a markdown-only copy tree: 57 entries, each pointing at its canonical directory. Hermes needed\\n   copies because its scanner quarantined linked trees; dsh has no scanner, and Pi's whole-directory\\n   link would lose 41 skills here. [SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:20-26]\\n   [SOURCE: .pi/SYNC.md:32-34]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A whole-directory symlink `.dsh/skills -> .skilled/skills`: one-level discovery would expose only\\n  the 16 hubs.\\n- Markdown-only generated copies: they would lose `references/`, `assets/` and `scripts/` unless\\n  every body carried a canonical pointer, and the harness has no scanner reason to avoid links.\\n- Editing canonical `SKILL.md` files to add `whenToUse` or invocation keys: extra keys are optional,\\n  and changing 57 files is out of this phase's scope.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a quarantine or scan path: none exists in the filesystem provider; the only failure\\n  handling is warn-and-skip.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"flatten into every nested mode\\\" could mean rewriting bodies or exposing each as\\n  its own catalog entry; the second is what the loader supports, and it needs no body change.\\n- Contradictory evidence: Pi's whole-dir symlink works there because Pi's skill discovery is\\n  recursive or explicit-path based; the same mechanism does not transfer to dsh.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: the symlink behavior is documented and its code path preserves the resolved path,\\n  but no dsh session with a `.dsh/skills` farm was run (that would require configuring a provider).\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36-56,85,147`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts:811-850`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:21-36,84`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/README.md:140`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/skill/tool-skill/README.md:48`\\n- `.pi/SYNC.md:32-34`, `.hermes/SYNC.md:20-26`\\n- Repo skill tree counts: 16 top-level directories, 57 `SKILL.md` files\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.93 (six fully new findings, one that extends the `.pi`/`.hermes`\\n  precedent into a dsh-specific decision)\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 4 skill format, roots, limits and mirror mechanism\\n- Questions answered: What skill format does the harness load, and should this repo use generated copies or symlinks?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: counting the tree before reading the loader contract turned an abstract\\n  \\\"symlink or copy\\\" question into an arithmetic one, and the one-level rule decided it.\\n- What did not work and why: the README's \\\"nested SKILL.md deliberately not discovered\\\" line is easy\\n  to miss under a table; the source-level parser check confirmed the frontmatter compatibility claim.\\n- What I would do differently: count the tree in iteration 3, since the `.dsh/` folder inventory\\n  needed that number to be honest.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 5: agents, subagents, commands and goal, including whether `.skilled/agents` can be reached\\nas harness subagents or presets and how the 35 nested commands can be exposed.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-004.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916175424,"end":1793916184825}}}}
