{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916213693,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbd1804001T4e1UsJ5puDCb6","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbd06bb0016LJ7WTZkJdLyu2","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba97ef7a82234e38","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\ngrep -rn \"preset\\|persona\\|agent\" packages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md | head -20; echo \"===WORKFLOW===\"; sed -n 1,30p packages/workflow/workflow/README.md"},"output":"packages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:2:description: \"Model-facing subagent delegation tool for users and maintainers configuring, composing, or debugging delegation over a subagent provider.\"\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:6:# @deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:12:Use this package to give an agent a named tool that delegates work to a configured backend. Every call starts a managed activation and returns the child's name; the runtime owns completion notices and cleanup. Local children support messages and restoration, while external backends execute one task and return their final answer through the completion notice. Supported backends can expose approved child LLM routes. Each instance can select a child preset and depth limit.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:34:Load the subagent service, an in-process or remote backend, and this tool; then name the provider. This composition exposes a `subagent` tool that delegates to the `spawn` backend:\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:37:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent'\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:38:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-spawn-in-process'\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:39:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:42:    toolName: subagent\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:47:| `provider` | required | Provider name on `ctx.subagents` (e.g. `spawn`, `fork`, `acp`) |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:48:| `toolName` | `subagent` | Model-facing tool name; distinct for every loaded instance |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:49:| `modelSelection` | `false` | Expose optional child route fields; requires provider `agentOptions` support |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:50:| `modelDiscovery` | `false` | Register `list_subagent_models`; enable on one instance per tool scope |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:51:| `agentOptions` | — | Configured child `provider`, `model`, adapter-owned `reasoningEffort`, and positive `maxTokens` defaults; requires provider `agentOptions` support and overlays any provider-owned route defaults |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:52:| `agentPreset` | — | Default independent child preset id; requires in-process spawn |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:53:| `allowedAgentPresets` | — | Non-empty preset-id allowlist exposed as the model's optional `agent_preset` enum; must include `agentPreset` when both are set |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:56:The generated [configuration catalog](../../../docs/config-catalog.md#deepseek-aidsh-tool-subagent) is the exhaustive source for every accepted field and its JSDoc.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:60:The optional `name` argument names the child, unique among the caller's children and cannot be `lead`; omission selects `agent-1`, `agent-2`, and so on. The [subagent runtime](../subagent/README.md#agent-names) owns the name rule and its errors. Every call returns `started subagent <name>` after the runtime accepts the child, where `<name>` is the child's full name from the root, such as `reviewer/checker`. Top-level calls persist `{ kind: 'activation', name: <name> }` in result presentation metadata; nested Code dispatches retain it in the corresponding `tool/ptc-dispatch` event's `meta` field. It does not wait for the child's result. The activation owns the work independently of the completed tool call; the runtime sends a completion notice and releases execution resources.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:64:`maxDepth` caps recursion (`0` forbids delegation); omission reads the current Host `subagent.maxDepth` setting, initially `1`, at each delegation. A numeric depth requires a provider with the `depthLimit` capability; `'provider-managed'` leaves the budget to an out-of-process provider. The tool stays visible at the cap; each attempted start checks the calling agent's current depth and rejects with an errored result.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:66:<a id=\"selecting-a-child-preset\"></a>\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:67:### Selecting a child preset\n===WORKFLOW===\n---\ndescription: \"The workflow orchestration capability: run a model-written script that fans out subagents, for users and maintainers choosing or building on ctx.workflowEngine.\"\nkind: \"package-reference\"\n---\n\n# @deepseek-ai/dsh-workflow\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n## Summary\n\nRun a plain-JavaScript orchestration script that fans work out to subagents and returns the script's final JSON value. Scripts can use `agent()`, `parallel()`, `pipeline()`, `phase()`, and `log()`; models normally access them through the `workflow` tool. Each run belongs to its caller, attributes every child to the invoking agent, resolves failures and cancellation without rejecting its result, and awaits script and child cleanup during disposal. The caller must supply an execution engine, allowing the isolation strategy to change without altering visible behavior.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Use this package](#use-this-package)\n- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)\n- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)\n- [Model Experience](#model-experience)\n- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)\n- [Dev Note](#dev-note)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"use-this-package\"></a>\n## Use this package\n\nRun a workflow when a task decomposes into many independent pieces that one script should coordinate — an audit across many files, a migration, multi-angle research — and the model explicitly asks for workflow-style orchestration. For one or two delegations, prefer a plain subagent call.\n\n### The model-facing path\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"packages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:2:description: \"Model-facing subagent delegation tool for users and maintainers configuring, composing, or debugging delegation over a subagent provider.\"\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:6:# @deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:12:Use this package to give an agent a named tool that delegates work to a configured backend. Every call starts a managed activation and returns the child's name; the runtime owns completion notices and cleanup. Local children support messages and restoration, while external backends execute one task and return their final answer through the completion notice. Supported backends can expose approved child LLM routes. Each instance can select a child preset and depth limit.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:34:Load the subagent service, an in-process or remote backend, and this tool; then name the provider. This composition exposes a `subagent` tool that delegates to the `spawn` backend:\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:37:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent'\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:38:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-subagent-spawn-in-process'\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:39:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent'\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:42:    toolName: subagent\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:47:| `provider` | required | Provider name on `ctx.subagents` (e.g. `spawn`, `fork`, `acp`) |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:48:| `toolName` | `subagent` | Model-facing tool name; distinct for every loaded instance |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:49:| `modelSelection` | `false` | Expose optional child route fields; requires provider `agentOptions` support |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:50:| `modelDiscovery` | `false` | Register `list_subagent_models`; enable on one instance per tool scope |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:51:| `agentOptions` | — | Configured child `provider`, `model`, adapter-owned `reasoningEffort`, and positive `maxTokens` defaults; requires provider `agentOptions` support and overlays any provider-owned route defaults |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:52:| `agentPreset` | — | Default independent child preset id; requires in-process spawn |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:53:| `allowedAgentPresets` | — | Non-empty preset-id allowlist exposed as the model's optional `agent_preset` enum; must include `agentPreset` when both are set |\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:56:The generated [configuration catalog](../../../docs/config-catalog.md#deepseek-aidsh-tool-subagent) is the exhaustive source for every accepted field and its JSDoc.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:60:The optional `name` argument names the child, unique among the caller's children and cannot be `lead`; omission selects `agent-1`, `agent-2`, and so on. The [subagent runtime](../subagent/README.md#agent-names) owns the name rule and its errors. Every call returns `started subagent <name>` after the runtime accepts the child, where `<name>` is the child's full name from the root, such as `reviewer/checker`. Top-level calls persist `{ kind: 'activation', name: <name> }` in result presentation metadata; nested Code dispatches retain it in the corresponding `tool/ptc-dispatch` event's `meta` field. It does not wait for the child's result. The activation owns the work independently of the completed tool call; the runtime sends a completion notice and releases execution resources.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:64:`maxDepth` caps recursion (`0` forbids delegation); omission reads the current Host `subagent.maxDepth` setting, initially `1`, at each delegation. A numeric depth requires a provider with the `depthLimit` capability; `'provider-managed'` leaves the budget to an out-of-process provider. The tool stays visible at the cap; each attempted start checks the calling agent's current depth and rejects with an errored result.\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:66:<a id=\"selecting-a-child-preset\"></a>\npackages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:67:### Selecting a child preset\n===WORKFLOW===\n---\ndescription: \"The workflow orchestration capability: run a model-written script that fans out subagents, for users and maintainers choosing or building on ctx.workflowEngine.\"\nkind: \"package-reference\"\n---\n\n# @deepseek-ai/dsh-workflow\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n## Summary\n\nRun a plain-JavaScript orchestration script that fans work out to subagents and returns the script's final JSON value. Scripts can use `agent()`, `parallel()`, `pipeline()`, `phase()`, and `log()`; models normally access them through the `workflow` tool. Each run belongs to its caller, attributes every child to the invoking agent, resolves failures and cancellation without rejecting its result, and awaits script and child cleanup during disposal. The caller must supply an execution engine, allowing the isolation strategy to change without altering visible behavior.\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n- [Use this package](#use-this-package)\n- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)\n- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)\n- [Model Experience](#model-experience)\n- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)\n- [Dev Note](#dev-note)\n\n-----\n\n<a id=\"use-this-package\"></a>\n## Use this package\n\nRun a workflow when a task decomposes into many independent pieces that one script should coordinate — an audit across many files, a migration, multi-angle research — and the model explicitly asks for workflow-style orchestration. For one or two delegations, prefer a plain subagent call.\n\n### The model-facing path\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\ngrep -rn \\\"preset\\\\|persona\\\\|agent\\\" packages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md | head -20; echo \\\"===WORKFLOW===\\\"; sed -n 1,30p packages/workflow/workflow/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916213252,"end":1793916213693}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916213696,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbd1622001SZ5ikHDoXVFwd4","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbd06bb0016LJ7WTZkJdLyu2","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d6e3f4512d71820","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\nls packages | grep -i command; grep -rn \"slash command\\|custom command\\|command plane\\|commands\" docs/architecture.md | head -12; echo \"===SUBTASK SCHEMA===\"; sed -n 2050,2130p docs/tool-catalog.md"},"output":"docs/architecture.md:155:| Add a human command | register on `ctx.commands`; it dispatches without a model turn |\n===SUBTASK SCHEMA===\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"provider\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Registered LLM provider id.\"\n    },\n    \"model\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Exact model id; requires provider.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSource: [`packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/list-models.ts`](../packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/list-models.ts)\n\n### `subagent`\n\nDelegate a self-contained task to a subagent (a separate agent that works in its own context) to offload focused, independent work — research, a scoped implementation, an analysis — so it does not consume this conversation's context. The subagent returns its result, not its intermediate steps. This tool starts an independently managed subagent and immediately returns its name. If you are still online when it finishes, the runtime automatically delivers its completion notice. The notice includes the final answer unless the child sent you a message just before finishing. Use `send_message` to steer it while running or continue its conversation after it finishes.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cwd\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Initial child working directory. Relative paths use your current directory; omitted inherits it. Later directory changes in either agent are independent.\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"A short (3-5 word) description of the delegated task, for display. Use the language of the user's current request.\"\n    },\n    \"name\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Optional short name for the subagent, unique among the subagents you create: lower-case letters, digits, and hyphens, starting with a letter, at most 32 characters; lead is reserved for the root agent. Omitted names default to agent-1, agent-2, and so on.\"\n    },\n    \"prompt\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The complete, self-contained task for the subagent. It does not share this conversation's context, so include everything it needs.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"description\",\n    \"prompt\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSource: [`packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/index.ts`](../packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/index.ts)\n\nThe load-time `toolName` selects the delegation name (default `subagent`); `modelSelection` adds optional route fields. `modelDiscovery` defaults off and registers shared discovery on one instance per scope. Web and Desktop presets enable spawn discovery and route fields and leave `subagent_fork` route fields disabled. The Host settings service records authorization for each new top-level Session; child Sessions inherit it. Without a recorded policy, discovery and explicit selection permit only the current parent route. Every delegation returns the child's name promptly; local children accept follow-ups, while external backends report their single execution automatically.\n\n<a id=\"deepseek-aidsh-tool-subagent-control\"></a>\n\n## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent-control`\n\n### `interrupt_agent`\n\nAsk a subagent to stop its current work. This call returns without waiting for it to stop. You can continue a local subagent's conversation later with send_message. External executions stop permanently and cannot receive follow-ups. Subagents it started will keep running.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"agent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The name of an agent created under you: your direct child or a deeper descendant.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"agent\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSource: [`packages/subagent/tool-subagent-control/src/index.ts`](../packages/subagent/tool-subagent-control/src/index.ts)\n\n### `list_agents`\n\nList your entire subagent tree: the root agent and all reachable continuable descendants, including yourself. Rows carry names, descriptions, and status. A descendant's name is its path from the root, such as reviewer/checker. You can message any other agent in the subagent tree. running means it is working; inactive means no turn is executing; it does not indicate task completion, success, or failure. corrupt, unsupported, or unavailable means this row's own descendants could not be read; the row itself is still a member you can message. While you remain active, you will be notified when a direct child finishes; there is no need to keep checking its status. Use send_message to continue the conversation.\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"docs/architecture.md:155:| Add a human command | register on `ctx.commands`; it dispatches without a model turn |\n===SUBTASK SCHEMA===\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"provider\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Registered LLM provider id.\"\n    },\n    \"model\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Exact model id; requires provider.\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nSource: [`packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/list-models.ts`](../packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/list-models.ts)\n\n### `subagent`\n\nDelegate a self-contained task to a subagent (a separate agent that works in its own context) to offload focused, independent work — research, a scoped implementation, an analysis — so it does not consume this conversation's context. The subagent returns its result, not its intermediate steps. This tool starts an independently managed subagent and immediately returns its name. If you are still online when it finishes, the runtime automatically delivers its completion notice. The notice includes the final answer unless the child sent you a message just before finishing. Use `send_message` to steer it while running or continue its conversation after it finishes.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cwd\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Initial child working directory. Relative paths use your current directory; omitted inherits it. Later directory changes in either agent are independent.\"\n    },\n    \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"A short (3-5 word) description of the delegated task, for display. Use the language of the user's current request.\"\n    },\n    \"name\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Optional short name for the subagent, unique among the subagents you create: lower-case letters, digits, and hyphens, starting with a letter, at most 32 characters; lead is reserved for the root agent. Omitted names default to agent-1, agent-2, and so on.\"\n    },\n    \"prompt\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The complete, self-contained task for the subagent. It does not share this conversation's context, so include everything it needs.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"description\",\n    \"prompt\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSource: [`packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/index.ts`](../packages/subagent/tool-subagent/src/index.ts)\n\nThe load-time `toolName` selects the delegation name (default `subagent`); `modelSelection` adds optional route fields. `modelDiscovery` defaults off and registers shared discovery on one instance per scope. Web and Desktop presets enable spawn discovery and route fields and leave `subagent_fork` route fields disabled. The Host settings service records authorization for each new top-level Session; child Sessions inherit it. Without a recorded policy, discovery and explicit selection permit only the current parent route. Every delegation returns the child's name promptly; local children accept follow-ups, while external backends report their single execution automatically.\n\n<a id=\"deepseek-aidsh-tool-subagent-control\"></a>\n\n## `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-subagent-control`\n\n### `interrupt_agent`\n\nAsk a subagent to stop its current work. This call returns without waiting for it to stop. You can continue a local subagent's conversation later with send_message. External executions stop permanently and cannot receive follow-ups. Subagents it started will keep running.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"agent\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The name of an agent created under you: your direct child or a deeper descendant.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"agent\"\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nSource: [`packages/subagent/tool-subagent-control/src/index.ts`](../packages/subagent/tool-subagent-control/src/index.ts)\n\n### `list_agents`\n\nList your entire subagent tree: the root agent and all reachable continuable descendants, including yourself. Rows carry names, descriptions, and status. A descendant's name is its path from the root, such as reviewer/checker. You can message any other agent in the subagent tree. running means it is working; inactive means no turn is executing; it does not indicate task completion, success, or failure. corrupt, unsupported, or unavailable means this row's own descendants could not be read; the row itself is still a member you can message. While you remain active, you will be notified when a direct child finishes; there is no need to keep checking its status. Use send_message to continue the conversation.\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\nls packages | grep -i command; grep -rn \\\"slash command\\\\|custom command\\\\|command plane\\\\|commands\\\" docs/architecture.md | head -12; echo \\\"===SUBTASK SCHEMA===\\\"; sed -n 2050,2130p docs/tool-catalog.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916212770,"end":1793916213696}}}}
