{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793916222342,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adbd3b86001EL4Rwc6U7f6fsQ","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbd2ea8001wt7n8c3B9tXPK8","type":"step-start","snapshot":"c13018833e9941d94451f1c0969a170766818f78"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916223879,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbd3fe7001fVkZO0fOnhzjaY","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbd2ea8001wt7n8c3B9tXPK8","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b19d22d64eb22dea","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\ngrep -n \"command\" docs/architecture.md | sed -n 1,20p; echo \"===AGENT PKG===\"; grep -n \"persona\\|preset\\|system prompt\" packages/core/agent/README.md | head -12"},"output":"43:Supported Node applications launch through named `dsh` profiles. The shipped profiles are `web`, `headless`, `sdk`, `sdk-minimal`, and `acp`, selected with `dsh --profile <name>` or `dsh <name>`. `plugin` names the management command; a profile with that name requires `--profile plugin`. The TypeScript SDK resolves its same-version `dsh` dependency and selects `sdk`; custom plugin composition remains a profile plus ordered patch files, not another executable or inline application tree. `sdk-minimal` is a repository-owned standalone bundle behind the same launcher, not a caller-supplied Cordis tree.\n155:| Add a human command | register on `ctx.commands`; it dispatches without a model turn |\n===AGENT PKG===\n74:`Agent.ctx` is the agent's scoped context: registrations made through it (tools, prompt sections, variables, event listeners, restrictions) apply to that agent alone and unwind on disposal. The same mechanism is what agent presets use to give one session a different capability set without affecting its neighbors.\n98:`PreStepDecision` is either `{ kind: 'reject' }` or `{ kind: 'enter', messages, startsRequestSeries? }`. The enter branch contains the complete identified, frozen message batch. Acceptance does not commit it: after assembly and `step/start`, the deprecated `agent/request` hook adjusts controls without changing the step's model selection, and `prepareCall()` binds the adapter before the loop commits the system prompt and user batch. Cancellation during either async phase commits neither. `startsRequestSeries: true` declares a distinct model-message series; a wrapping listener preserves that declaration and the batch unless it intentionally replaces either one. Claiming removes offered messages from the inbox, while messages inserted after the claim remain pending for a later boundary.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"43:Supported Node applications launch through named `dsh` profiles. The shipped profiles are `web`, `headless`, `sdk`, `sdk-minimal`, and `acp`, selected with `dsh --profile <name>` or `dsh <name>`. `plugin` names the management command; a profile with that name requires `--profile plugin`. The TypeScript SDK resolves its same-version `dsh` dependency and selects `sdk`; custom plugin composition remains a profile plus ordered patch files, not another executable or inline application tree. `sdk-minimal` is a repository-owned standalone bundle behind the same launcher, not a caller-supplied Cordis tree.\n155:| Add a human command | register on `ctx.commands`; it dispatches without a model turn |\n===AGENT PKG===\n74:`Agent.ctx` is the agent's scoped context: registrations made through it (tools, prompt sections, variables, event listeners, restrictions) apply to that agent alone and unwind on disposal. The same mechanism is what agent presets use to give one session a different capability set without affecting its neighbors.\n98:`PreStepDecision` is either `{ kind: 'reject' }` or `{ kind: 'enter', messages, startsRequestSeries? }`. The enter branch contains the complete identified, frozen message batch. Acceptance does not commit it: after assembly and `step/start`, the deprecated `agent/request` hook adjusts controls without changing the step's model selection, and `prepareCall()` binds the adapter before the loop commits the system prompt and user batch. Cancellation during either async phase commits neither. `startsRequestSeries: true` declares a distinct model-message series; a wrapping listener preserves that declaration and the batch unless it intentionally replaces either one. Claiming removes offered messages from the inbox, while messages inserted after the claim remain pending for a later boundary.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\ngrep -n \\\"command\\\" docs/architecture.md | sed -n 1,20p; echo \\\"===AGENT PKG===\\\"; grep -n \\\"persona\\\\|preset\\\\|system prompt\\\" packages/core/agent/README.md | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916223463,"end":1793916223879}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916223885,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbd3e4d002JqVhkq3zS9sJ62","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbd2ea8001wt7n8c3B9tXPK8","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a615063a5ecb159a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\ngrep -rn \"agent-preset\\|persona\" packages/bundle/*/cordis.patch.yml | head -20; echo \"===COMMANDS API===\"; grep -rn \"ctx.commands\\|command adapter\" packages/core/commands/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -10; ls packages/core | grep -i command"},"output":"packages/bundle/acp-app/cordis.patch.yml:5:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:521:    # The deployment persona is a deployment choice; plan-mode and tool plugins own\npackages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:526:        personaPrefix: ''\npackages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:11:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/sdk-app/cordis.patch.yml:5:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/sdk-minimal/cordis.patch.yml:118:        personaPrefix: !!js process.env.DSH_SYSTEM_PROMPT ?? 'You are a helpful software engineer assistant.'\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:19:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:212:    # URL as optional runtime context. A complete agent-preset persona replaces\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:213:    # the sections, and a persona that suppresses optional runtime context\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:434:    # The agent-preset row in General settings: the default preset for\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:436:    - id: ui-agent-preset\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:437:      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-agent-preset'\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:598:    - id: agent-preset-registry\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:599:      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-preset-registry'\n===COMMANDS API===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"packages/bundle/acp-app/cordis.patch.yml:5:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:521:    # The deployment persona is a deployment choice; plan-mode and tool plugins own\npackages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:526:        personaPrefix: ''\npackages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:11:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/sdk-app/cordis.patch.yml:5:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/sdk-minimal/cordis.patch.yml:118:        personaPrefix: !!js process.env.DSH_SYSTEM_PROMPT ?? 'You are a helpful software engineer assistant.'\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:19:    personaPrefix: >-\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:212:    # URL as optional runtime context. A complete agent-preset persona replaces\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:213:    # the sections, and a persona that suppresses optional runtime context\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:434:    # The agent-preset row in General settings: the default preset for\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:436:    - id: ui-agent-preset\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:437:      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-agent-preset'\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:598:    - id: agent-preset-registry\npackages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:599:      name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-preset-registry'\n===COMMANDS API===\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Exited with code 1"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\ngrep -rn \\\"agent-preset\\\\|persona\\\" packages/bundle/*/cordis.patch.yml | head -20; echo \\\"===COMMANDS API===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"ctx.commands\\\\|command adapter\\\" packages/core/commands/README.md 2>/dev/null | head -10; ls packages/core | grep -i command\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916223053,"end":1793916223885}}}}
