{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916265382,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbde1b7002Z7e664iCCEdw41","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbdd9a60014Zk1XkWHre70wX","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-85e35e0b99134e7b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\ngrep -rn \"agent/pre-step\\|agent/post-step\\|tool/call\\|tool/result\\|session/start\\|session/stop\\|prompt\" docs/agent-lifecycle.md | head -25; echo \"===EVENT DOC===\"; sed -n 1,60p docs/event-producer-consumer.md"},"output":"docs/agent-lifecycle.md:25:  Note over Agent,Driver: claim pending next-step input plus one queued prompt\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:29:  Driver->>Prompt: <code>system-prompt/assemble</code> waterfall with the step tool set\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:30:  Driver->>Hooks: <code>agent/pre-step</code> waterfall\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:59:      Driver->>Session: <code>tool/call</code>\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:65:      Driver->>Session: <code>tool/result</code>\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:76:    Driver->>Hooks: <code>agent/pre-step</code> waterfall\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:87:`dsh-compaction-basic` uses `agent/pre-step` for pressure before request derivation and `agent/request-error` only for canonical context overflow. Once either trigger qualifies, optional tool-result pruning runs before summary selection. Recovery runs within the open step and retries only when pruning or summarization advances the surface replacement generation; otherwise the original request error remains authoritative. Each retry prepares its call and reconciles the retained rendered assembly before request derivation, without repeating assembly, pre-step, or user admission.\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:89:The returned `agent/pre-step` decision is authoritative; listeners wrapping `next()` preserve downstream messages and `startsRequestSeries` unless replacement is intentional. Steering and injected context pass through the same waterfall after a later claim operation takes their next-step batch.\ndocs/agent-lifecycle.md:91:SDK users that need replayable transcript data should consume `session/event`; `agent/*` is the live coordination API for queue/status, prompt interception, request construction, steering, continuation, and errors.\n===EVENT DOC===\n<!-- Generated by scripts/gen-doc-graphs.ts - do not edit by hand.\n     Run `pnpm run gen-doc-graphs` to regenerate. -->\n\n# Event Producer And Consumer Matrix\n\nThis matrix shows which packages dispatch each harness-owned event and which packages listen to it. Events are many-to-many, so the dense relation data is presented as a table rather than one large graph. Receiver and event-name types also cover contained dispatch sites that deliberately bypass `ctx.emit`, such as subagent lifecycle containment.\n\nApplication listeners are outside this package matrix. Desktop Host subscribes to `plugin-manager/operation` through [`installOperationDiagnostics`](../apps/desktop-host/src/operation-diagnostics.ts) and forwards bounded records to the shell.\n\n<!-- BEGIN GENERATED event-producer-consumer:events -->\n| Event | Mode | Declared in | Dispatchers | Listeners |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `agent-loop/config-start-failed` | `emit` | [`packages/core/agent-loop/src/index.ts:198`](../packages/core/agent-loop/src/index.ts) | [`agent-loop`](../packages/core/agent-loop) (`events.dispatch`) | - |\n| `agent-preset/selected` | `emit` | [`packages/preset/agent-preset-registry/src/types.ts:66`](../packages/preset/agent-preset-registry/src/types.ts) | [`agent-preset-registry`](../packages/preset/agent-preset-registry) (`emit`) | [`cua`](../packages/experimental/cua), `remotes` |\n| `agent/assistant-stream` | `emit` | [`packages/core/agent/src/runtime-types.ts:399`](../packages/core/agent/src/runtime-types.ts) | [`agent-l