`pnpm-workspace.yaml` after the plugin moves to a newer commit; nothing removes stale approvals.\n174:- The Git transport probe keeps the parent console on Windows, so an SSH host-key or passphrase prompt can appear in the launching terminal until `gitTransportTimeoutMs`. On POSIX a host missing from `known_hosts` fails the SSH probe, so installation stays on HTTPS until the host key is accepted once, for example with `ssh -T git@<host>`. A credential-helper dialog or ssh-agent confirmation, such as a Touch ID or `ssh-add -c` dialog, that takes longer than the deadline counts as a failed probe, and an HTTPS probe that times out lets a reachable SSH form be saved to the profile. A private repository waits up to twice `gitTransportTimeoutMs` before pnpm starts. The SSH form always uses the `git` user and SSH's default port; other SSH endpoints need a `url.<base>.insteadOf` rule. When both probes fail, the diagnostic is pnpm's HTTPS failure; the SSH probe's reason is not reported.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\ngrep -n \\\"apply(ctx\\\\|export function apply\\\\|local\\\\|file:\\\\|link:\\\\|path\\\" docs/cordis-primer.md | head -25; echo \\\"===PLUGIN ADD===\\\"; grep -n \\\"add\\\\|file:\\\\|git\\\\|local\\\" packages/boot/plugin-manager/README.md | head -25\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916276368,"end":1793916276982}}}}
