{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916281048,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adbe1f9e001vjlXOdUoE9ran5","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adbe14b8001fwbZ4WyYUHDkIN","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a2793b4ffc71044","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\nsed -n 1,60p packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/README.md | grep -n \"configPath\\|hook\\|block\\|SessionStart\\|PreToolUse\\|Stop\\|SubagentStop\\|UserPromptSubmit\\|PreCompact\" | head -25"},"output":"2:description: \"Run your existing Claude Code hooks.json or settings hook config during agent runs — block prompts and tools, attach context, or force continuation — for users and maintainers of the bridge.\"\n6:# @deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code\n12:`dsh-hooks-claude-code` runs command hooks from your existing Claude Code `hooks.json` or settings file during agent runs, without requiring a rewrite. Supported hooks can run when sessions, prompts, tools, stops, or subagents reach matching moments. They can block prompts or tool calls with model-visible reasons, add conversation context, or force another model turn. Choose this package to reuse Claude Code command hooks in the harness; use a native plugin for behavior that has no Claude Code equivalent.\n28:Hook processes and their payload `cwd` use the Session's current working directory when each hook point starts. `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` follows it unless `projectDir` is configured. `SubagentStop` reads the child's final committed directory after disposal; it cannot recover a missing directory or mutate that Session, and a failed stop hook is warned.\n30:Mount this package, point `configPath` at your hook config, and the hooks you already have start firing at the corresponding moments in agent runs. There is nothing else to set up before the first hook works.\n34:Use it when you own a Claude Code `hooks.json` (or a settings file whose `hooks` key holds the config) and its command hooks should gate prompts, tools, and turns. Skip it for behavior with no Claude Code equivalent: a native plugin has the full harness API, while this bridge runs only the reference tool's command-hook subset.\n39:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code'\n41:    configPath: ./.claude/hooks.json\n48:| `configPath` | required | Path to a `hooks.json` or a settings file whose `hooks` key holds the config |\n51:| `defaultTimeoutMs` | `600,000` | Per-hook timeout when a hook sets none (the Claude Code default) |\n52:| `stderrSummaryMaxChars` | `500` | Character cap on the persisted `hook/result` stderr summary |\n54:The generated [configuration catalog](../../../docs/config-catalog.md#deepseek-aidsh-hooks-claude-code) is the exhaustive source for every accepted field.\n56:### What your hooks can do\n58:| Your hook | When it runs | What it can do |\n60:| `SessionStart` | when a session starts | attach context the model sees in that session |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2:description: \"Run your existing Claude Code hooks.json or settings hook config during agent runs — block prompts and tools, attach context, or force continuation — for users and maintainers of the bridge.\"\n6:# @deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code\n12:`dsh-hooks-claude-code` runs command hooks from your existing Claude Code `hooks.json` or settings file during agent runs, without requiring a rewrite. Supported hooks can run when sessions, prompts, tools, stops, or subagents reach matching moments. They can block prompts or tool calls with model-visible reasons, add conversation context, or force another model turn. Choose this package to reuse Claude Code command hooks in the harness; use a native plugin for behavior that has no Claude Code equivalent.\n28:Hook processes and their payload `cwd` use the Session's current working directory when each hook point starts. `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` follows it unless `projectDir` is configured. `SubagentStop` reads the child's final committed directory after disposal; it cannot recover a missing directory or mutate that Session, and a failed stop hook is warned.\n30:Mount this package, point `configPath` at your hook config, and the hooks you already have start firing at the corresponding moments in agent runs. There is nothing else to set up before the first hook works.\n34:Use it when you own a Claude Code `hooks.json` (or a settings file whose `hooks` key holds the config) and its command hooks should gate prompts, tools, and turns. Skip it for behavior with no Claude Code equivalent: a native plugin has the full harness API, while this bridge runs only the reference tool's command-hook subset.\n39:- name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code'\n41:    configPath: ./.claude/hooks.json\n48:| `configPath` | required | Path to a `hooks.json` or a settings file whose `hooks` key holds the config |\n51:| `defaultTimeoutMs` | `600,000` | Per-hook timeout when a hook sets none (the Claude Code default) |\n52:| `stderrSummaryMaxChars` | `500` | Character cap on the persisted `hook/result` stderr summary |\n54:The generated [configuration catalog](../../../docs/config-catalog.md#deepseek-aidsh-hooks-claude-code) is the exhaustive source for every accepted field.\n56:### What your hooks can do\n58:| Your hook | When it runs | What it can do |\n60:| `SessionStart` | when a session starts | attach context the model sees in that session |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\nsed -n 1,60p packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/README.md | grep -n \\\"configPath\\\\|hook\\\\|block\\\\|SessionStart\\\\|PreToolUse\\\\|Stop\\\\|SubagentStop\\\\|UserPromptSubmit\\\\|PreCompact\\\" | head -25\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916280734,"end":1793916281048}}}}
