{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916428743,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adc05ee3002v1YZsUM6q0V70t","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc04d810015tihsgjwD1aT3j","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3bd86b9d0b34681","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json'))\nfor k in ['name','version','private','publishConfig']:\n    print(k, d.get(k))\n\"; echo \"---mcp-client pkg---\"; python3 -c \"\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('packages/mcp/mcp-client/package.json'))\nprint(d.get('name'), d.get('version'), 'private=',d.get('private'))\n\""},"output":"name @deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code\nversion 0.2.2-rc.1\nprivate None\npublishConfig {'access': 'public'}\n---mcp-client pkg---\n@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client 0.2.2-rc.1 private= None\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"name @deepseek-ai/dsh-hooks-claude-code\nversion 0.2.2-rc.1\nprivate None\npublishConfig {'access': 'public'}\n---mcp-client pkg---\n@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client 0.2.2-rc.1 private= None\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src\\npython3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json'))\\nfor k in ['name','version','private','publishConfig']:\\n    print(k, d.get(k))\\n\\\"; echo \\\"---mcp-client pkg---\\\"; python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nd=json.load(open('packages/mcp/mcp-client/package.json'))\\nprint(d.get('name'), d.get('version'), 'private=',d.get('private'))\\n\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916428003,"end":1793916428743}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1793916429614,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adc0652e001cJJn85TZ1yIZXK","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc04d810015tihsgjwD1aT3j","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"40ec9910e791acdf90034a0add28ba4a93effb11","cost":0.001072446,"tokens":{"input":197,"output":201,"reasoning":389,"cache":{"read":229632,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793916431506,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adc06c9200195aw4HDG3amt6D","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc06534001mXagvl5LtnBHcC","type":"step-start","snapshot":"40ec9910e791acdf90034a0add28ba4a93effb11"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916442555,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adc07791001MnfFZXTDtdXKn5","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc06534001mXagvl5LtnBHcC","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9be051882e878a99","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 8: MCP\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 8: how MCP servers are configured, which transports exist, where the config lives, whether\n`.pi/mcp.json` and the code-mode manual can connect, and whether a dispatch can enable or deny MCP\ntools per run.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the MCP client and MCP manager references and the memory-server guide.\n- Read `.pi/mcp.json` and the installed package inventory for `dsh-mcp-client` and the hook bridge.\n- Checked the base and web bundle patches for which MCP rows are mounted.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. One `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` row per server, with required `serverName` and `transport`\n   (`stdio` or `streamable-http`), then `command`/`args`/`env`/`cwd` for a local program or\n   `url`/`headers` for a service, plus `toolCallTimeoutMs` (60 s default), optional\n   `startupTimeoutMs`, `closeTimeoutMs`, `expandTemplates` and `failOnStartupError`.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:32-66]\n2. Tools are exposed as `mcp__<serverName>__<rawName>`, with the server namespace taken from local\n   configuration rather than the remote `serverInfo.name`, so restarts and upgrades do not rename\n   model-facing tools. Two servers may offer the same raw tool name under different namespaces.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:78-86]\n3. Server instructions join the logged system prompt as literal text, up to 32,768 bytes, and MCP\n   prompt templates are unsupported. That makes a server's instructions untrusted prompt input: a\n   hostile server can put directives in the description or instructions, and the same\n   data-not-instructions rule that covers fetched web pages must cover MCP text.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:12]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:65]\n4. MCP configuration lives only in the active profile's `cordis.patch.yml` or a `--patch` overlay;\n   there is no project MCP file. `.pi/mcp.json` cannot be read by the harness and must be translated\n   into `.dsh/mcp.yml` rows, one per server. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:23-33]\n5. The stdio bridge scrubs ambient variables whose names usually identify credentials and every\n   `DSH_*` variable before launching the child; everything a server needs must be named in the row's\n   `env`. `expandTemplates: true` adds `${credential:REF}` resolution, but requires a credentials\n   provider, which the headless profile disables by default.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:13]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:101]\n6. The repo's code-mode entry translates directly: `command: node`, `args: [.skilled/bin/mcp-code-mode-launcher.cjs]`,\n   `transport: stdio`, `env: { UTCP_CONFIG_FILE: .utcp_config.json }`, `cwd: <repo root>`. Its\n   `lifecycle: lazy` has no harness equivalent — a dsh MCP client connects with the plugin lifecycle\n   — so porting trades lazy startup for an eager connection bounded by `startupTimeoutMs`.\n   [SOURCE: .pi/mcp.json:1]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:32]\n7. Per-dispatch enable/deny has no CLI flag: the lever is the patch file. A dispatch that omits the\n   MCP rows has no MCP tools at all, and one that passes an MCP patch gets exactly the servers in\n   that patch. The live `mcp-manager` fleet controls exist only in the web/desktop profiles, not in\n   base or headless. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-manager/README.md:12]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:153-154]\n8. `dsh-mcp-client` is bundled inside the installed `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-rc.1` package (319\n   `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` packages present), while `dsh-hooks-claude-code` is not bundled despite being\n   a public, version-matched package. MCP therefore needs only a profile row; the hook bridge needs\n   an install step. This corrects the Angle 6 shorthand that called the bridge \"shipped\".\n   [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json:1]\n9. Base mounts `mcp-resources` but not `mcp-client`, so a headless dispatch has no MCP tool until a\n   patch adds a server row; the MCP route guard's `mcp__.*` matcher shape still fits the generated\n   tool names once it is rewritten as a regex. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:505-506]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Reading `.pi/mcp.json` directly: no project MCP config is scanned.\n- Per-dispatch `--mcp` or tool-allowlist flags: none exist; composition is the control.\n- Lazy MCP startup: no `lifecycle` field on the harness client.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for an MCP manager in base or headless: only the web bundle mounts it, so a headless\n  dispatch cannot enable or restart a server mid-run.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"per-dispatch enable or deny\" could mean server selection or tool filtering; the\n  harness offers server selection by composition only.\n- Contradictory evidence: the Angle 6 note treated the Claude hook bridge as shipped; the installed\n  package inventory shows it is not, and this iteration supersedes that wording.\n- Missing dependencies: no MCP server is installed or configured, so nothing was connected.\n- Partial success: the schema and translation are confirmed; a live code-mode connection is not.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:12-101`\n- `dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-manager/README.md:12`\n- `dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:9-33`\n- `.pi/mcp.json`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:505-506`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:153-154`\n- Installed package inventory at `~/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai`\n- `dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json:1`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.88 (seven fully new findings, one correction to the Angle 6 cost model,\n  one that confirms the built-in tool-name shape)\n- Questions addressed: Angle 8 MCP configuration, transports and per-dispatch control\n- Questions answered: How are MCP servers configured, and can this repo's servers and code-mode connect?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: translating `.pi/mcp.json` field by field found the one unsupported key\n  (`lifecycle`) and the one required addition (`cwd`), which a schema summary would have missed.\n- What did not work and why: assuming the hook bridge shipped because it exists in the source tree;\n  the installed inventory is the authority and it corrected the cost.\n- What I would do differently: run the installed-package inventory in Angle 6, since every port\n  verdict depends on whether the package is actually present.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 9: deep-loop fan-out fitness, the lineage command builder, and every consumer that must learn\na new executor kind.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 8: MCP\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 8: how MCP servers are configured, which transports exist, where the config lives, whether\\n`.pi/mcp.json` and the code-mode manual can connect, and whether a dispatch can enable or deny MCP\\ntools per run.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Read the MCP client and MCP manager references and the memory-server guide.\\n- Read `.pi/mcp.json` and the installed package inventory for `dsh-mcp-client` and the hook bridge.\\n- Checked the base and web bundle patches for which MCP rows are mounted.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. One `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` row per server, with required `serverName` and `transport`\\n   (`stdio` or `streamable-http`), then `command`/`args`/`env`/`cwd` for a local program or\\n   `url`/`headers` for a service, plus `toolCallTimeoutMs` (60 s default), optional\\n   `startupTimeoutMs`, `closeTimeoutMs`, `expandTemplates` and `failOnStartupError`.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:32-66]\\n2. Tools are exposed as `mcp__<serverName>__<rawName>`, with the server namespace taken from local\\n   configuration rather than the remote `serverInfo.name`, so restarts and upgrades do not rename\\n   model-facing tools. Two servers may offer the same raw tool name under different namespaces.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:78-86]\\n3. Server instructions join the logged system prompt as literal text, up to 32,768 bytes, and MCP\\n   prompt templates are unsupported. That makes a server's instructions untrusted prompt input: a\\n   hostile server can put directives in the description or instructions, and the same\\n   data-not-instructions rule that covers fetched web pages must cover MCP text.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:12]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:65]\\n4. MCP configuration lives only in the active profile's `cordis.patch.yml` or a `--patch` overlay;\\n   there is no project MCP file. `.pi/mcp.json` cannot be read by the harness and must be translated\\n   into `.dsh/mcp.yml` rows, one per server. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:23-33]\\n5. The stdio bridge scrubs ambient variables whose names usually identify credentials and every\\n   `DSH_*` variable before launching the child; everything a server needs must be named in the row's\\n   `env`. `expandTemplates: true` adds `${credential:REF}` resolution, but requires a credentials\\n   provider, which the headless profile disables by default.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:13]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:101]\\n6. The repo's code-mode entry translates directly: `command: node`, `args: [.skilled/bin/mcp-code-mode-launcher.cjs]`,\\n   `transport: stdio`, `env: { UTCP_CONFIG_FILE: .utcp_config.json }`, `cwd: <repo root>`. Its\\n   `lifecycle: lazy` has no harness equivalent — a dsh MCP client connects with the plugin lifecycle\\n   — so porting trades lazy startup for an eager connection bounded by `startupTimeoutMs`.\\n   [SOURCE: .pi/mcp.json:1]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:32]\\n7. Per-dispatch enable/deny has no CLI flag: the lever is the patch file. A dispatch that omits the\\n   MCP rows has no MCP tools at all, and one that passes an MCP patch gets exactly the servers in\\n   that patch. The live `mcp-manager` fleet controls exist only in the web/desktop profiles, not in\\n   base or headless. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-manager/README.md:12]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:153-154]\\n8. `dsh-mcp-client` is bundled inside the installed `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-rc.1` package (319\\n   `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` packages present), while `dsh-hooks-claude-code` is not bundled despite being\\n   a public, version-matched package. MCP therefore needs only a profile row; the hook bridge needs\\n   an install step. This corrects the Angle 6 shorthand that called the bridge \\\"shipped\\\".\\n   [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json:1]\\n9. Base mounts `mcp-resources` but not `mcp-client`, so a headless dispatch has no MCP tool until a\\n   patch adds a server row; the MCP route guard's `mcp__.*` matcher shape still fits the generated\\n   tool names once it is rewritten as a regex. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:505-506]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Reading `.pi/mcp.json` directly: no project MCP config is scanned.\\n- Per-dispatch `--mcp` or tool-allowlist flags: none exist; composition is the control.\\n- Lazy MCP startup: no `lifecycle` field on the harness client.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for an MCP manager in base or headless: only the web bundle mounts it, so a headless\\n  dispatch cannot enable or restart a server mid-run.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"per-dispatch enable or deny\\\" could mean server selection or tool filtering; the\\n  harness offers server selection by composition only.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the Angle 6 note treated the Claude hook bridge as shipped; the installed\\n  package inventory shows it is not, and this iteration supersedes that wording.\\n- Missing dependencies: no MCP server is installed or configured, so nothing was connected.\\n- Partial success: the schema and translation are confirmed; a live code-mode connection is not.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:12-101`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-manager/README.md:12`\\n- `dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:9-33`\\n- `.pi/mcp.json`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:505-506`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:153-154`\\n- Installed package inventory at `~/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json:1`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.88 (seven fully new findings, one correction to the Angle 6 cost model,\\n  one that confirms the built-in tool-name shape)\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 8 MCP configuration, transports and per-dispatch control\\n- Questions answered: How are MCP servers configured, and can this repo's servers and code-mode connect?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: translating `.pi/mcp.json` field by field found the one unsupported key\\n  (`lifecycle`) and the one required addition (`cwd`), which a schema summary would have missed.\\n- What did not work and why: assuming the hook bridge shipped because it exists in the source tree;\\n  the installed inventory is the authority and it corrected the cost.\\n- What I would do differently: run the installed-package inventory in Angle 6, since every port\\n  verdict depends on whether the package is actually present.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 9: deep-loop fan-out fitness, the lineage command builder, and every consumer that must learn\\na new executor kind.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-008.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916434321,"end":1793916442555}}}}
