embership (routingClass 'metadata'), so there is no advisor map entry per mode and no merged-identity projection — the advisor does not read this file at runtime. This registry is also the executor-delegation scorer's source of truth for which CLI executors exist (system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts), keyed by packetSkillName — and every mode here is a workflow executor.\",\n8:    \"packetKind\": \"The axis discriminator: 'workflow' for cli-opencode, cli-claude-code, cli-codex, cli-cursor, cli-devin, cli-pi, and cli-hermes — each classifies intent, chooses/confirms a provider, and conducts a dispatched CLI session whose writes land in this repo's workspace. No extension is declared: the transport-axis left with the cli-jev transport, which is now mode cli-jev of the cli-classifier hub at .skilled/skills/cli-classifier/, over its cli-jev packet, and no surface-axis exists because no mode in this hub is read-only evidence — all seven orchestrate, and each mode's declared writes land in this repo's workspace. cli-cursor's native worktree/cloud-worker surfaces are opt-in escape hatches, not its default dispatch shape.\",\n12:    \"routingClass\": \"How the advisor finds the mode. For cli-external-orchestration every mode is 'metadata' = resolved by hub membership; the advisor routes the single identity cli-external-orchestration and the hub picks the mode, so no mode carries an advisor map entry or a merged-identity projection.\",\n78:        \"anthropic cli second opinion\",\n108:        \"openai cli second opinion\",\n168:        \"cognition cli second opinion\",\n178:      \"workflowMode\": \"cli-pi\",\n192:      \"packet\": \"cli-pi\",\n193:      \"packetSkillName\": \"cli-pi\",\n197:        \"pi cli\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"cli-claude-code.vitest.ts\ncli-codex.vitest.ts\ncli-cursor.vitest.ts\ncli-devin.vitest.ts\ncli-hermes.vitest.ts\nc