{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916621703,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adc35015002anQ46j2oRYsuXb","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc3483b001iaCVd22dIHD0bT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac13f2cae5e38d38","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\ngrep -rn \"cli-pi\\|cli-hermes\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts 2>/dev/null | head -10; echo \"---sync script---\"; grep -n \"cli-hermes\\|cli-pi\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh 2>/dev/null | head; echo \"---agents/readme---\"; grep -n \"cli-hermes\\|cli-pi\" AGENTS.md README.md SECURITY.md .skilled/skills/README.txt 2>/dev/null | head -20"},"output":"---sync script---\n69:  \"$ROOT/.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/assets/prompt-quality-card.md\"\n72:  \"$ROOT/.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/assets/prompt-quality-card.md\"\n100:cli_skills=(cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes)\n---agents/readme---\nAGENTS.md:283:Hermes is the exception worth knowing: it has no agent flag, so naming a directory is not enough there. Each agent is also mirrored as the preloadable skill `agent-<name>`, and a dispatch binds one by preloading that skill and naming it in `HERMES_AGENT_PERSONA`. The `cli-hermes` packet owns the mechanics.\nREADME.md:71:- Every bridge but `cli-pi` refuses to dispatch the runtime it runs in, and fan-out lineages and dispatch stacks are bounded, so delegation never loops\nREADME.md:867:- **No self-dispatch.** Every bridge but `cli-pi` refuses to dispatch the runtime it runs in, so delegation never loops\nREADME.md:871:One skill with seven bridges: `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-hermes`. Describe the job and it hands the dispatch to the right one.\nREADME.md:1558:- Parent hub for external CLI dispatch: routes to `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi`, and `cli-hermes`. Stack-independent\nSECURITY.md:144:Use a read-only mode for review and research: `--permission-mode plan` for Claude Code and `--mode plan` or `--mode ask` for Cursor. `codex exec` is read-only unless you pass `--sandbox workspace-write`. When a dispatch must write, run it in a fresh git worktree so a stray delete hits a tree you can throw away. `cli-devin` and `cli-hermes` approve tool calls by default, so name a narrower mode when you dispatch them.\n.skilled/skills/README.txt:46:| [`cli-external-orchestration`](cli-external-orchestration/README.md) | Parent hub for external CLI dispatch, holding no per-mode logic: routes by `workflowMode` to `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-hermes` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---sync script---\n69:  \"$ROOT/.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/assets/prompt-quality-card.md\"\n72:  \"$ROOT/.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes/assets/prompt-quality-card.md\"\n100:cli_skills=(cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code cli-external-orchestration/cli-cursor cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex cli-external-orchestration/cli-devin cli-external-orchestration/cli-hermes)\n---agents/readme---\nAGENTS.md:283:Hermes is the exception worth knowing: it has no agent flag, so naming a directory is not enough there. Each agent is also mirrored as the preloadable skill `agent-<name>`, and a dispatch binds one by preloading that skill and naming it in `HERMES_AGENT_PERSONA`. The `cli-hermes` packet owns the mechanics.\nREADME.md:71:- Every bridge but `cli-pi` refuses to dispatch the runtime it runs in, and fan-out lineages and dispatch stacks are bounded, so delegation never loops\nREADME.md:867:- **No self-dispatch.** Every bridge but `cli-pi` refuses to dispatch the runtime it runs in, so delegation never loops\nREADME.md:871:One skill with seven bridges: `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-hermes`. Describe the job and it hands the dispatch to the right one.\nREADME.md:1558:- Parent hub for external CLI dispatch: routes to `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi`, and `cli-hermes`. Stack-independent\nSECURITY.md:144:Use a read-only mode for review and research: `--permission-mode plan` for Claude Code and `--mode plan` or `--mode ask` for Cursor. `codex exec` is read-only unless you pass `--sandbox workspace-write`. When a dispatch must write, run it in a fresh git worktree so a stray delete hits a tree you can throw away. `cli-devin` and `cli-hermes` approve tool calls by default, so name a narrower mode when you dispatch them.\n.skilled/skills/README.txt:46:| [`cli-external-orchestration`](cli-external-orchestration/README.md) | Parent hub for external CLI dispatch, holding no per-mode logic: routes by `workflowMode` to `cli-opencode`, `cli-claude-code`, `cli-codex`, `cli-cursor`, `cli-devin`, `cli-pi` and `cli-hermes` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled\\ngrep -rn \\\"cli-pi\\\\|cli-hermes\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/executor-delegation.ts 2>/dev/null | head -10; echo \\\"---sync script---\\\"; grep -n \\\"cli-hermes\\\\|cli-pi\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh 2>/dev/null | head; echo \\\"---agents/readme---\\\"; grep -n \\\"cli-hermes\\\\|cli-pi\\\" AGENTS.md README.md SECURITY.md .skilled/skills/README.txt 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916620821,"end":1793916621703}}}}
