{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793916639942,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adc39ac6001ab18GN6sU3AyEj","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc392de00103fbMp8K7DQ3ZU","type":"step-start","snapshot":"22b09de105c91275d52e752e4931fbfde0a84d8a"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916716133,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adc3dcf8002zQoKcMWyP55YBq","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc392de00103fbMp8K7DQ3ZU","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9a7d29c52ce66a3","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 9: Deep-loop fan-out fitness and the complete touch list\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 9: what a lineage command builder for `cli-deepseek` needs — write-permitting headless flags,\napproval semantics, timeout, stdin, state isolation, env filters, self-invocation detection,\nsandbox and exit-status trust — and every consumer that must learn the new executor kind.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the executor-kind tables, defaults and allowlists in `executor-config.ts`.\n- Read the Pi and Hermes builders, the adapter map, the dispatch-env builder and the recursion guard.\n- Read the runner's exit-status policy and the permission-preset and sandbox references.\n- Enumerated consumers with repo-wide searches for `cli-hermes` and `cli-pi`.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. Registering a kind means touching seven tables in `executor-config.ts`: `EXECUTOR_KINDS`,\n   `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`, `EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY`, the web-search policy\n   map, `EXECUTOR_MCP_SERVER_CAPABILITY`, the per-kind defaults, and the model allowlist plus default\n   model and Flash top-tier pin. `cli-deepseek` is a provider pass-through with no per-dispatch model\n   flag, so its allowlist must be the set of route patches the repo ships.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:93-122]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:140-148]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:194-209]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:251-276]\n2. The builder's command shape is `dsh --profile headless --json --permission-mode <mode>\n   --approval-policy never --patch <route.yml> -`, with the prompt on stdin and `input` set to the\n   prompt. `-` is required because a positional task makes the harness ignore stdin. There is no\n   model, effort, cwd or timeout flag: cwd is the spawn directory, the timeout is the runner's, and\n   the route comes from the patch. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:36]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:46]\n3. Write permission is explicit: `workspace-write` confines writes to the spawn cwd plus\n   `--add-dir` grants, `read-only` denies writes, `danger-full-access` bypasses the sandbox, and a\n   host without a usable backend fails `SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE` rather than running unconfined.\n   `--approval-policy never` rejects every call that would need a human, which is the only correct\n   setting for an unattended leaf. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:58-60]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:134]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:92]\n4. There is no turn or time budget in the headless contract. The runner's `timeoutSeconds`, signal\n   kill and the artifact check are the only bound, so the lineage patch must also disable `goal`,\n   `goal-round-driver` and `plan-mode`: an active goal can auto-continue up to 256 rounds, and plan\n   mode fails closed without a review channel. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:63]\n5. Per-lineage state isolation is `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home` in the child environment. The\n   directory bootstraps its own `headless` profile and session tree on first use and never reads the\n   operator's `~/.dsh`, which keeps locks, sessions and credentials separate across lineages.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/util/home-paths/README.md:34-40]\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.dsh-home/profiles/headless/cordis.yml]\n6. The dispatch-env filter is a strict allowlist: PATH, HOME, LANG, TMPDIR, NODE_PATH, TERM, USER,\n   LOGNAME, `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING`, `LC_*`, plus per-kind prefixes and single keys. A\n   `cli-deepseek` entry needs `DSH_HOME` as a key, and `LLMGATEWAY_` plus `DEEPSEEK_` as prefixes\n   for the two routes; `DSH_*` must not be a blanket prefix, or unrelated deployment knobs leak into\n   every leaf. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:129-186]\n7. The recursion guard needs two signals: `SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID` and the executor kind present\n   in `SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK`. The builder stamps the stack, and a `dsh` binary mapped to\n   `cli-deepseek` makes a nested dsh dispatch fail closed. dsh itself has no native self-invocation\n   guard, so this is the only prevention. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3700-3730]\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:994-1010]\n8. Exit status is trustworthy in a way Pi's is not: `0` only on a completed final turn, `1` on\n   abort, error, no owned turn, usage error or unusable session id. The runner can treat any non-zero\n   as failure, but should read the `--json` `final.reason` and `error` event to classify it, because\n   provider error, denial and timeout all collapse to `1`.\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4045-4056]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:104]\n9. The complete consumer list, one row per file and the change each needs:\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` | Add kind to all seven tables, a three-model allowlist, default model and `max` pin |\n| `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | Add `buildDeepseekLineageCommand`, adapter entry, binary probe, route map, `SPECKIT_DEEPSEEK_STATE_DIR`, `dsh` recursion binary |\n| `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts` | Add `DSH_HOME` key and `LLMGATEWAY_`/`DEEPSEEK_` prefixes; add `dsh` to the recursion binary map |\n| `runtime/tests/unit/{executor-config,fanout-run,combo-matrix,executor-audit,verify-iteration}.vitest.ts` | Add `cli-deepseek` cases and matrix exclusions |\n| `runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/{matrix-manifest.ts,live-contracts.json,cli-deepseek.vitest.ts,shims/deepseek-shim.cjs,README.md}` | Add the adapter, a shim and a live-contract row |\n| `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs` + `dispatch-audit.test.mjs` | Recognize `dsh headless` and map it to `cli-deepseek` |\n| `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs` | Add hard-rule fixtures (stdin `-`, approval `never`, profile preset) |\n| `deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs` + tests | Add the kind to its accepted list and seat fallback |\n| `deep-ai-council/SKILL.md`, `deep-research/SKILL.md`, `deep-review/SKILL.md` | Add the eighth executor kind to the documented roster |\n| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-{auto,confirm}.yaml`, `deep-review-{auto,confirm}.yaml`, `deep-ai-council-{auto,confirm}.yaml` | Add a shared-adapter note/branch for `cli-deepseek` |\n| Same assets' `*-presentation.txt` and `compiled/*.contract.markdown` | Add `cli-deepseek` to each enum and choice list |\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json` | Update the AGENTS.md agent-routing text it mirrors |\n| `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/004-cli-external-orchestration/{fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json,harness/build-artifacts.cjs}` | Add the packet to the canary and build fixtures |\n| `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/{SKILL.md,ROUTER.md,README.md,mode-registry.json,hub-router.json,leaf-manifest.json,graph-metadata.json,description.json,feature-catalog/}` | Register the eighth mode and its feature-catalog entry |\n| Sibling `cli-*/README.md` mode tables | Add the new row where the seven are listed |\n| `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh` | Add the packet to `cli_skills` |\n| `sk-prompt/SKILL.md` + `assets/cli-prompt-quality-card.md` | Add its model row and persona-reach rule |\n| `.skilled/agents/orchestrate.md`, `prompt-improver.md` | Add the kind to the executor and model tables |\n| `AGENTS.md`, root `README.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `.skilled/skills/README.txt` | Update counts, routing lines and the approval note |\n| `system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json` | Regenerate after the packet exists |\n| `sk-doc/scripts/tests/code-folder/{durable-directory-manifest.json,baseline-readme-verdicts.json}` | Add the packet's directories and README verdicts |\n| `runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md` | Document the new builder and its flags |\n\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh:69-100]\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:198-381]\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs:61-94]\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/mode-registry.json:5-12]\n  [SOURCE: README.md:867-871]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- A `--model` or `--effort` flag in the builder: headless exposes neither, so the route must be a\n  patch and the allowlist a set of patch names.\n- Reusing the Pi exit-code exception: dsh's exit status is deterministic, so a non-zero exit is a\n  real failure.\n- Passing all `DSH_*` variables to the child: only `DSH_HOME` and `DSH_PERMISSION_MODE` are needed.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a harness-side per-run budget: none exists; the runner owns the timeout, and the\n  goal driver is the overrun risk to disable.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"write-permitting flags\" could mean sandbox mode or approval policy; both are\n  required and are recorded separately.\n- Contradictory evidence: the harness sandbox defaults to `workspace-write`, which is write-permitting,\n  while its fail-safe policy default is `read-only`; headless overrides to `workspace-write`, so a\n  read-only leaf must pass the mode explicitly.\n- Missing dependencies: no configured key, so no lineage was executed through the builder.\n- Partial success: the builder design is source-backed; the touch list is complete for the files\n  that name the existing kinds, but a generated index can still surface a missed mention at build\n  time.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11-276`\n- `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2884-3120,3620-3730,4045-4056`\n- `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:129-186,994-1010`\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12,46,92,104`\n- `dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12,58-60,134`\n- `dsh-src/packages/util/home-paths/README.md:34-40`\n- `dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30`\n- `dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:63`\n- `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs:61-94`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh:69-100`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:198-381`\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/mode-registry.json:5-12`\n- `README.md:867-871`\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.90 (seven fully new builder and isolation findings, one that extends the\n  exit-status policy, and one complete touch table)\n- Questions addressed: Angle 9 fan-out fitness and cross-repo touch points\n- Questions answered: What does a deep-loop fan-out lineage builder need, and which consumers must learn the new executor kind?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: the existing builders are a checklist; every field a kind needs is already a\n  constant or a table entry for Pi or Hermes, so the new kind is an enumeration, not a design.\n- What did not work and why: searching the whole repo for `cli-hermes` timed out; scoping the\n  searches by directory and using the content-search tool produced the same list without the cost.\n- What I would do differently: start from `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and follow each table, then grep for the\n  kind names in tests, because the tables are the authoritative touch list.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 10: constraints and differences versus Pi, hard rules for the packet, the phase plan, and what\nstays UNKNOWN until a live contract pin.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 9: Deep-loop fan-out fitness and the complete touch list\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 9: what a lineage command builder for `cli-deepseek` needs — write-permitting headless flags,\\napproval semantics, timeout, stdin, state isolation, env filters, self-invocation detection,\\nsandbox and exit-status trust — and every consumer that must learn the new executor kind.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Read the executor-kind tables, defaults and allowlists in `executor-config.ts`.\\n- Read the Pi and Hermes builders, the adapter map, the dispatch-env builder and the recursion guard.\\n- Read the runner's exit-status policy and the permission-preset and sandbox references.\\n- Enumerated consumers with repo-wide searches for `cli-hermes` and `cli-pi`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. Registering a kind means touching seven tables in `executor-config.ts`: `EXECUTOR_KINDS`,\\n   `EXECUTOR_KIND_FLAG_SUPPORT`, `EXECUTOR_PREVENTIVE_SANDBOX_CAPABILITY`, the web-search policy\\n   map, `EXECUTOR_MCP_SERVER_CAPABILITY`, the per-kind defaults, and the model allowlist plus default\\n   model and Flash top-tier pin. `cli-deepseek` is a provider pass-through with no per-dispatch model\\n   flag, so its allowlist must be the set of route patches the repo ships.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:93-122]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:140-148]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:194-209]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:251-276]\\n2. The builder's command shape is `dsh --profile headless --json --permission-mode <mode>\\n   --approval-policy never --patch <route.yml> -`, with the prompt on stdin and `input` set to the\\n   prompt. `-` is required because a positional task makes the harness ignore stdin. There is no\\n   model, effort, cwd or timeout flag: cwd is the spawn directory, the timeout is the runner's, and\\n   the route comes from the patch. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:36]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:46]\\n3. Write permission is explicit: `workspace-write` confines writes to the spawn cwd plus\\n   `--add-dir` grants, `read-only` denies writes, `danger-full-access` bypasses the sandbox, and a\\n   host without a usable backend fails `SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE` rather than running unconfined.\\n   `--approval-policy never` rejects every call that would need a human, which is the only correct\\n   setting for an unattended leaf. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:58-60]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:134]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:92]\\n4. There is no turn or time budget in the headless contract. The runner's `timeoutSeconds`, signal\\n   kill and the artifact check are the only bound, so the lineage patch must also disable `goal`,\\n   `goal-round-driver` and `plan-mode`: an active goal can auto-continue up to 256 rounds, and plan\\n   mode fails closed without a review channel. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:63]\\n5. Per-lineage state isolation is `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home` in the child environment. The\\n   directory bootstraps its own `headless` profile and session tree on first use and never reads the\\n   operator's `~/.dsh`, which keeps locks, sessions and credentials separate across lineages.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/util/home-paths/README.md:34-40]\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.dsh-home/profiles/headless/cordis.yml]\\n6. The dispatch-env filter is a strict allowlist: PATH, HOME, LANG, TMPDIR, NODE_PATH, TERM, USER,\\n   LOGNAME, `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING`, `LC_*`, plus per-kind prefixes and single keys. A\\n   `cli-deepseek` entry needs `DSH_HOME` as a key, and `LLMGATEWAY_` plus `DEEPSEEK_` as prefixes\\n   for the two routes; `DSH_*` must not be a blanket prefix, or unrelated deployment knobs leak into\\n   every leaf. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:129-186]\\n7. The recursion guard needs two signals: `SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID` and the executor kind present\\n   in `SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK`. The builder stamps the stack, and a `dsh` binary mapped to\\n   `cli-deepseek` makes a nested dsh dispatch fail closed. dsh itself has no native self-invocation\\n   guard, so this is the only prevention. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3700-3730]\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:994-1010]\\n8. Exit status is trustworthy in a way Pi's is not: `0` only on a completed final turn, `1` on\\n   abort, error, no owned turn, usage error or unusable session id. The runner can treat any non-zero\\n   as failure, but should read the `--json` `final.reason` and `error` event to classify it, because\\n   provider error, denial and timeout all collapse to `1`.\\n   [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4045-4056]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:104]\\n9. The complete consumer list, one row per file and the change each needs:\\n\\n| File | Change |\\n|---|---|\\n| `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts` | Add kind to all seven tables, a three-model allowlist, default model and `max` pin |\\n| `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs` | Add `buildDeepseekLineageCommand`, adapter entry, binary probe, route map, `SPECKIT_DEEPSEEK_STATE_DIR`, `dsh` recursion binary |\\n| `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts` | Add `DSH_HOME` key and `LLMGATEWAY_`/`DEEPSEEK_` prefixes; add `dsh` to the recursion binary map |\\n| `runtime/tests/unit/{executor-config,fanout-run,combo-matrix,executor-audit,verify-iteration}.vitest.ts` | Add `cli-deepseek` cases and matrix exclusions |\\n| `runtime/tests/stress/cli-adapter/{matrix-manifest.ts,live-contracts.json,cli-deepseek.vitest.ts,shims/deepseek-shim.cjs,README.md}` | Add the adapter, a shim and a live-contract row |\\n| `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs` + `dispatch-audit.test.mjs` | Recognize `dsh headless` and map it to `cli-deepseek` |\\n| `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs` | Add hard-rule fixtures (stdin `-`, approval `never`, profile preset) |\\n| `deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs` + tests | Add the kind to its accepted list and seat fallback |\\n| `deep-ai-council/SKILL.md`, `deep-research/SKILL.md`, `deep-review/SKILL.md` | Add the eighth executor kind to the documented roster |\\n| `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-{auto,confirm}.yaml`, `deep-review-{auto,confirm}.yaml`, `deep-ai-council-{auto,confirm}.yaml` | Add a shared-adapter note/branch for `cli-deepseek` |\\n| Same assets' `*-presentation.txt` and `compiled/*.contract.markdown` | Add `cli-deepseek` to each enum and choice list |\\n| `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json` | Update the AGENTS.md agent-routing text it mirrors |\\n| `.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/004-cli-external-orchestration/{fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json,harness/build-artifacts.cjs}` | Add the packet to the canary and build fixtures |\\n| `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/{SKILL.md,ROUTER.md,README.md,mode-registry.json,hub-router.json,leaf-manifest.json,graph-metadata.json,description.json,feature-catalog/}` | Register the eighth mode and its feature-catalog entry |\\n| Sibling `cli-*/README.md` mode tables | Add the new row where the seven are listed |\\n| `system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh` | Add the packet to `cli_skills` |\\n| `sk-prompt/SKILL.md` + `assets/cli-prompt-quality-card.md` | Add its model row and persona-reach rule |\\n| `.skilled/agents/orchestrate.md`, `prompt-improver.md` | Add the kind to the executor and model tables |\\n| `AGENTS.md`, root `README.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `.skilled/skills/README.txt` | Update counts, routing lines and the approval note |\\n| `system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json` | Regenerate after the packet exists |\\n| `sk-doc/scripts/tests/code-folder/{durable-directory-manifest.json,baseline-readme-verdicts.json}` | Add the packet's directories and README verdicts |\\n| `runtime/feature-catalog/fanout/fanout-run.md` | Document the new builder and its flags |\\n\\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh:69-100]\\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:198-381]\\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs:61-94]\\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/mode-registry.json:5-12]\\n  [SOURCE: README.md:867-871]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- A `--model` or `--effort` flag in the builder: headless exposes neither, so the route must be a\\n  patch and the allowlist a set of patch names.\\n- Reusing the Pi exit-code exception: dsh's exit status is deterministic, so a non-zero exit is a\\n  real failure.\\n- Passing all `DSH_*` variables to the child: only `DSH_HOME` and `DSH_PERMISSION_MODE` are needed.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a harness-side per-run budget: none exists; the runner owns the timeout, and the\\n  goal driver is the overrun risk to disable.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"write-permitting flags\\\" could mean sandbox mode or approval policy; both are\\n  required and are recorded separately.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the harness sandbox defaults to `workspace-write`, which is write-permitting,\\n  while its fail-safe policy default is `read-only`; headless overrides to `workspace-write`, so a\\n  read-only leaf must pass the mode explicitly.\\n- Missing dependencies: no configured key, so no lineage was executed through the builder.\\n- Partial success: the builder design is source-backed; the touch list is complete for the files\\n  that name the existing kinds, but a generated index can still surface a missed mention at build\\n  time.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11-276`\\n- `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:2884-3120,3620-3730,4045-4056`\\n- `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:129-186,994-1010`\\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12,46,92,104`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12,58-60,134`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/util/home-paths/README.md:34-40`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:63`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs:61-94`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/check-prompt-quality-card-sync.sh:69-100`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs:198-381`\\n- `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/mode-registry.json:5-12`\\n- `README.md:867-871`\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.90 (seven fully new builder and isolation findings, one that extends the\\n  exit-status policy, and one complete touch table)\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 9 fan-out fitness and cross-repo touch points\\n- Questions answered: What does a deep-loop fan-out lineage builder need, and which consumers must learn the new executor kind?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: the existing builders are a checklist; every field a kind needs is already a\\n  constant or a table entry for Pi or Hermes, so the new kind is an enumeration, not a design.\\n- What did not work and why: searching the whole repo for `cli-hermes` timed out; scoping the\\n  searches by directory and using the content-search tool produced the same list without the cost.\\n- What I would do differently: start from `EXECUTOR_KINDS` and follow each table, then grep for the\\n  kind names in tests, because the tables are the authoritative touch list.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 10: constraints and differences versus Pi, hard rules for the packet, the phase plan, and what\\nstays UNKNOWN until a live contract pin.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-009.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916656888,"end":1793916716133}}}}
