{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916832375,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adc635b9002eQri6OdtQrr1xn","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc60c5c001wN6A2TS4PgKLPl","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9458a11438c223b9","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 10: Constraints, differences and the phase plan\n\n## Focus\n\nAngle 10: where the harness costs more or less than Pi — dependencies, startup, telemetry,\nrelease-candidate versioning, background services and cost per run — which constraints need a hard\nrule in the skill packet, and the recommended phase plan for 002 and later with what stays `UNKNOWN`\nuntil a live contract pin.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Read the installed package metadata and measured two startup paths.\n- Read the base telemetry row and the `subprocess-local` dependency chain behind the skipped install\n  scripts.\n- Compared the harness's dispatch, sandbox and exit contract with `cli-pi`'s.\n- Assembled the hard-rule list and the phase plan from all ten angles.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. The installed package requires Node `>=24.9.0`, declares 90 dependencies and ships 319\n   `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` packages in a 896 MB install; its version is `0.2.2-rc.1`, the npm `latest`\n   tag, so the runtime is a release candidate with no stability promise across rc bumps.\n   [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/package.json:1]\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:27-31]\n2. Startup is cheap for the launcher and moderate for a profile: `dsh --version` measured 0.07 s and\n   `dsh headless --help` 1.16 s on this machine, the latter booting the profile without a model\n   request. A real dispatch adds provider latency on top; the number to pin is the full\n   \"task to final answer\" time, not the launcher.\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.events/smoke-1.stderr]\n3. Base mounts `session-telemetry-otel` in `FEEDBACK_ONLY` mode with a default collector URL\n   (`https://dsh-otel-collector.deepseeksvc.com/v1/logs`). No telemetry leaves the process without an\n   explicit feedback event, and a headless dispatch has no feedback channel, so the default is\n   effectively silent. A hard guarantee still needs the row disabled or `DSH_TELEMETRY_MODE=DISABLED`\n   in the lineage patch. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:218-228]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/session/session-telemetry-otel/README.md:12-26]\n4. Base mounts `subprocess-local`, which declares both `node-pty` and `koffi`, and npm skipped the\n   install scripts for both. Headless mounts no terminal and needs no PTY, so the dispatch shape\n   itself does not require them; whether the `bash` tool's spawn path is affected by the skipped\n   `koffi` build is `UNKNOWN` until a live tool call. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:234-235]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/subprocess/subprocess-local/package.json:1]\n5. On cost, the harness adds no billing layer: token accounting is local, and the route bills at the\n   gateway's own per-token rate, the same rate Pi pays for the same model. The extra cost is\n   footprint (896 MB, Node 24.9+), profile boot per lineage and an rc upgrade cadence, not a markup.\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/token-meter/README.md:12]\n6. The harness is ahead of Pi on four dispatch-relevant contracts: a deterministic two-value exit\n   status, a machine-readable NDJSON stream with `final.reason`, a real per-subprocess sandbox that\n   fails closed when no backend exists, and native goal, subagent, workflow, skill and MCP services.\n   It is behind on per-dispatch model selection, prompt templates, agent files, project plugins and\n   compaction-hook coverage. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:136]\n7. The packet needs these hard rules: `headless-dash-stdin-required`, `route-patch-required`\n   (no `--model`; one checked-in patch per route), `approval-never-required`,\n   `headless-only`, `dsh-home-isolated`, `goal-plan-disabled`, `json-exit-classification`,\n   `telemetry-disabled`, `profile-version-check` and `route-compat-pinned`\n   (`supportsDeveloperRole: false`, `thinkingFormat: deepseek` for both gateways).\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:92]\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:218-228]\n8. The recommended phase plan, ranked by dependency:\n\n| Rank | Phase | Outcome | Depends on | Risk | Mode | Required | Failure prevented |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 002 live contract pin | One keyed headless write dispatch; verbatim stdout/stderr/exit; `--json` parse; bash and sandbox behavior | operator key | sandbox backend missing; skipped native builds | `sk-code` verify | required | building a mode on documentation only |\n| 2 | 003 `cli-deepseek` skill packet | SKILL, ROUTER, hard rules, references, assets, prompt card | 002 | rule drift from observed behavior | `sk-doc` create-skill | required | ad-hoc dispatch composition |\n| 3 | 004 executor kind and builder | `executor-config` tables, builder, audit, unit tests | 002 | route patch not applying; stdin misuse | `sk-code` implement | required | fan-out with unverified provenance |\n| 4 | 005 `.dsh/` runtime folder | route patches, hooks config, MCP patch, SYNC, skill-link generator | 003, 004 | symlink farm misses skills | `sk-code` implement + `sk-doc` create-readme | required | configuration drift |\n| 5 | 006 hub and routing registration | mode registry, hub files, advisor, doctor manifest, compiled fixtures | 003 | an unroutable eighth mode | `sk-doc` create-readme + `sk-code` tests | required | profile that cannot be selected |\n| 6 | 007 command and agent bridges | prompt templates, persona patch, goal-context bridge | 005 | personas truncated or unreachable | `sk-doc` create-command/create-agent | required for parity, optional for fan-out | reinventing commands per dispatch |\n| 7 | 008 hook bridge and repo guards | rewritten hooks config, `repo-guards` bundle, task-dispatch adapter | 005 | bridge package not installable | `sk-code` implement | optional | losing the repo's guard layer |\n| 8 | 009 MCP translation | `.dsh/mcp.yml`, code-mode row, route guard matcher | 005 | scrubbed env or eager startup | `sk-code` implement | optional | MCP absence or leakage |\n| 9 | 010 benchmark and playbook | manual-testing-playbook scenarios and a benchmark index | 002-009 | unverified claims | `sk-doc` create-benchmark | optional | claims without a live witness |\n| 10 | 011 propagation and generated surfaces | trigger index, doctor manifest, sk-doc manifests, changelog | 006 | stale generated index | `sk-code` implement | required before merge | routing to a packet that does not exist |\n| 11 | 012 re-pin on rc bump | refreshed contract pin and roster | 002 | silent rc breakage | `sk-code` verify | required per bump | an rc change breaking dispatch unnoticed |\n\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11]\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:1029]\n9. What stays `UNKNOWN` until a configured key: whether a `--patch` overlay actually repoints\n   `agent-default-model` in headless; whether LLM Gateway accepts the `thinkingFormat: deepseek`\n   reasoning shape and reports `max`; whether the `bash` tool works after the skipped `koffi` and\n   `node-pty` builds; whether a skill-link farm loads all 57 entries in one session; whether the\n   Claude hook bridge installs from npm and fires with rewritten matchers; whether code-mode MCP\n   connects under the scrubbed env; the real startup-plus-model latency; the per-run cost; and\n   whether telemetry stays silent in `FEEDBACK_ONLY` on a headless exit.\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:27-32]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Treating the harness as cheaper than Pi per run: same gateway rate, larger footprint.\n- Relying on `FEEDBACK_ONLY` as a telemetry hard rule: only `DISABLED` guarantees no export.\n- Building the executor kind before the keyed contract pin: the patch and stdin behavior are the\n  two risks that invalidate the builder.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Looking for a harness-side billing or cost table: token accounting is local and route pricing stays\n  with the gateway.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"cost per run\" could mean dollars or latency; both are addressed, and each is\n  `UNKNOWN` in absolute terms until a live call.\n- Contradictory evidence: the base policy default is `read-only` while the headless sandbox row\n  defaults to `workspace-write`; the headless override is the one that governs a dispatch.\n- Missing dependencies: no key, so the nine `UNKNOWN` items stay open.\n- Partial success: footprint, startup and telemetry are measured or source-confirmed; cost and\n  latency are not.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/package.json:1`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:218-235`\n- `dsh-src/packages/session/session-telemetry-otel/README.md:12-26`\n- `dsh-src/packages/subprocess/subprocess-local/package.json:1`\n- `dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12`\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:92,136`\n- `dsh-src/packages/llm/token-meter/README.md:12`\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132`\n- `resource-map.md:27-32`\n- Live `dsh --version` (0.07 s) and `dsh headless --help` (1.16 s) timings\n- The smoke stderr recorded in iteration 1\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.85 (five fully new footprint, telemetry and cost findings, two synthesis\n  findings that turn nine angles into rules and phases, two that restate measured contract facts)\n- Questions addressed: Angle 10 constraints, differences, hard rules and phase plan\n- Questions answered: Where does the harness cost more or less than Pi, what hard rules follow, and what is the phase plan?\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: measuring the two startup paths separated launcher cost from profile cost, and\n  reading the telemetry row turned \"does it phone home\" into a mode question with a concrete patch.\n- What did not work and why: the skipped install scripts cannot be tested without a model call, so\n  the honest output is an `UNKNOWN` tied to a named phase rather than a guess.\n- What I would do differently: collect the package metadata in iteration 1, since the Node floor and\n  install size shape every later recommendation.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nThe ten angles are complete. Synthesis consolidates the findings, the hard rules and the phase plan\ninto the lineage's `research.md`, with the `UNKNOWN` list preserved as open questions.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 10: Constraints, differences and the phase plan\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nAngle 10: where the harness costs more or less than Pi — dependencies, startup, telemetry,\\nrelease-candidate versioning, background services and cost per run — which constraints need a hard\\nrule in the skill packet, and the recommended phase plan for 002 and later with what stays `UNKNOWN`\\nuntil a live contract pin.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Read the installed package metadata and measured two startup paths.\\n- Read the base telemetry row and the `subprocess-local` dependency chain behind the skipped install\\n  scripts.\\n- Compared the harness's dispatch, sandbox and exit contract with `cli-pi`'s.\\n- Assembled the hard-rule list and the phase plan from all ten angles.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. The installed package requires Node `>=24.9.0`, declares 90 dependencies and ships 319\\n   `@deepseek-ai/dsh-*` packages in a 896 MB install; its version is `0.2.2-rc.1`, the npm `latest`\\n   tag, so the runtime is a release candidate with no stability promise across rc bumps.\\n   [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/package.json:1]\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:27-31]\\n2. Startup is cheap for the launcher and moderate for a profile: `dsh --version` measured 0.07 s and\\n   `dsh headless --help` 1.16 s on this machine, the latter booting the profile without a model\\n   request. A real dispatch adds provider latency on top; the number to pin is the full\\n   \\\"task to final answer\\\" time, not the launcher.\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/.events/smoke-1.stderr]\\n3. Base mounts `session-telemetry-otel` in `FEEDBACK_ONLY` mode with a default collector URL\\n   (`https://dsh-otel-collector.deepseeksvc.com/v1/logs`). No telemetry leaves the process without an\\n   explicit feedback event, and a headless dispatch has no feedback channel, so the default is\\n   effectively silent. A hard guarantee still needs the row disabled or `DSH_TELEMETRY_MODE=DISABLED`\\n   in the lineage patch. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:218-228]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/session/session-telemetry-otel/README.md:12-26]\\n4. Base mounts `subprocess-local`, which declares both `node-pty` and `koffi`, and npm skipped the\\n   install scripts for both. Headless mounts no terminal and needs no PTY, so the dispatch shape\\n   itself does not require them; whether the `bash` tool's spawn path is affected by the skipped\\n   `koffi` build is `UNKNOWN` until a live tool call. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:234-235]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/subprocess/subprocess-local/package.json:1]\\n5. On cost, the harness adds no billing layer: token accounting is local, and the route bills at the\\n   gateway's own per-token rate, the same rate Pi pays for the same model. The extra cost is\\n   footprint (896 MB, Node 24.9+), profile boot per lineage and an rc upgrade cadence, not a markup.\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/token-meter/README.md:12]\\n6. The harness is ahead of Pi on four dispatch-relevant contracts: a deterministic two-value exit\\n   status, a machine-readable NDJSON stream with `final.reason`, a real per-subprocess sandbox that\\n   fails closed when no backend exists, and native goal, subagent, workflow, skill and MCP services.\\n   It is behind on per-dispatch model selection, prompt templates, agent files, project plugins and\\n   compaction-hook coverage. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:136]\\n7. The packet needs these hard rules: `headless-dash-stdin-required`, `route-patch-required`\\n   (no `--model`; one checked-in patch per route), `approval-never-required`,\\n   `headless-only`, `dsh-home-isolated`, `goal-plan-disabled`, `json-exit-classification`,\\n   `telemetry-disabled`, `profile-version-check` and `route-compat-pinned`\\n   (`supportsDeveloperRole: false`, `thinkingFormat: deepseek` for both gateways).\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:92]\\n   [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:218-228]\\n8. The recommended phase plan, ranked by dependency:\\n\\n| Rank | Phase | Outcome | Depends on | Risk | Mode | Required | Failure prevented |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | 002 live contract pin | One keyed headless write dispatch; verbatim stdout/stderr/exit; `--json` parse; bash and sandbox behavior | operator key | sandbox backend missing; skipped native builds | `sk-code` verify | required | building a mode on documentation only |\\n| 2 | 003 `cli-deepseek` skill packet | SKILL, ROUTER, hard rules, references, assets, prompt card | 002 | rule drift from observed behavior | `sk-doc` create-skill | required | ad-hoc dispatch composition |\\n| 3 | 004 executor kind and builder | `executor-config` tables, builder, audit, unit tests | 002 | route patch not applying; stdin misuse | `sk-code` implement | required | fan-out with unverified provenance |\\n| 4 | 005 `.dsh/` runtime folder | route patches, hooks config, MCP patch, SYNC, skill-link generator | 003, 004 | symlink farm misses skills | `sk-code` implement + `sk-doc` create-readme | required | configuration drift |\\n| 5 | 006 hub and routing registration | mode registry, hub files, advisor, doctor manifest, compiled fixtures | 003 | an unroutable eighth mode | `sk-doc` create-readme + `sk-code` tests | required | profile that cannot be selected |\\n| 6 | 007 command and agent bridges | prompt templates, persona patch, goal-context bridge | 005 | personas truncated or unreachable | `sk-doc` create-command/create-agent | required for parity, optional for fan-out | reinventing commands per dispatch |\\n| 7 | 008 hook bridge and repo guards | rewritten hooks config, `repo-guards` bundle, task-dispatch adapter | 005 | bridge package not installable | `sk-code` implement | optional | losing the repo's guard layer |\\n| 8 | 009 MCP translation | `.dsh/mcp.yml`, code-mode row, route guard matcher | 005 | scrubbed env or eager startup | `sk-code` implement | optional | MCP absence or leakage |\\n| 9 | 010 benchmark and playbook | manual-testing-playbook scenarios and a benchmark index | 002-009 | unverified claims | `sk-doc` create-benchmark | optional | claims without a live witness |\\n| 10 | 011 propagation and generated surfaces | trigger index, doctor manifest, sk-doc manifests, changelog | 006 | stale generated index | `sk-code` implement | required before merge | routing to a packet that does not exist |\\n| 11 | 012 re-pin on rc bump | refreshed contract pin and roster | 002 | silent rc breakage | `sk-code` verify | required per bump | an rc change breaking dispatch unnoticed |\\n\\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11]\\n  [SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json:1029]\\n9. What stays `UNKNOWN` until a configured key: whether a `--patch` overlay actually repoints\\n   `agent-default-model` in headless; whether LLM Gateway accepts the `thinkingFormat: deepseek`\\n   reasoning shape and reports `max`; whether the `bash` tool works after the skipped `koffi` and\\n   `node-pty` builds; whether a skill-link farm loads all 57 entries in one session; whether the\\n   Claude hook bridge installs from npm and fires with rewritten matchers; whether code-mode MCP\\n   connects under the scrubbed env; the real startup-plus-model latency; the per-run cost; and\\n   whether telemetry stays silent in `FEEDBACK_ONLY` on a headless exit.\\n   [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:27-32]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Treating the harness as cheaper than Pi per run: same gateway rate, larger footprint.\\n- Relying on `FEEDBACK_ONLY` as a telemetry hard rule: only `DISABLED` guarantees no export.\\n- Building the executor kind before the keyed contract pin: the patch and stdin behavior are the\\n  two risks that invalidate the builder.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Looking for a harness-side billing or cost table: token accounting is local and route pricing stays\\n  with the gateway.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"cost per run\\\" could mean dollars or latency; both are addressed, and each is\\n  `UNKNOWN` in absolute terms until a live call.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the base policy default is `read-only` while the headless sandbox row\\n  defaults to `workspace-write`; the headless override is the one that governs a dispatch.\\n- Missing dependencies: no key, so the nine `UNKNOWN` items stay open.\\n- Partial success: footprint, startup and telemetry are measured or source-confirmed; cost and\\n  latency are not.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/package.json:1`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:218-235`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/session/session-telemetry-otel/README.md:12-26`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/subprocess/subprocess-local/package.json:1`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:92,136`\\n- `dsh-src/packages/llm/token-meter/README.md:12`\\n- `dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132`\\n- `resource-map.md:27-32`\\n- Live `dsh --version` (0.07 s) and `dsh headless --help` (1.16 s) timings\\n- The smoke stderr recorded in iteration 1\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.85 (five fully new footprint, telemetry and cost findings, two synthesis\\n  findings that turn nine angles into rules and phases, two that restate measured contract facts)\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 10 constraints, differences, hard rules and phase plan\\n- Questions answered: Where does the harness cost more or less than Pi, what hard rules follow, and what is the phase plan?\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: measuring the two startup paths separated launcher cost from profile cost, and\\n  reading the telemetry row turned \\\"does it phone home\\\" into a mode question with a concrete patch.\\n- What did not work and why: the skipped install scripts cannot be tested without a model call, so\\n  the honest output is an `UNKNOWN` tied to a named phase rather than a guess.\\n- What I would do differently: collect the package metadata in iteration 1, since the Node floor and\\n  install size shape every later recommendation.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nThe ten angles are complete. Synthesis consolidates the findings, the hard rules and the phase plan\\ninto the lineage's `research.md`, with the `UNKNOWN` list preserved as open questions.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-010.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916810681,"end":1793916832375}}}}
