{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793916875493,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"id":"prt_1adc732e5001z1ow6HrUiGQWL0","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc72895001dzKKsuoSO5pz92","type":"step-start","snapshot":"019768089d45719ceec65364bce93f329899688e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793916911355,"sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","part":{"partID":"prt_1adc73850001b9F5YLSwS7n9hM","sessionID":"ses_e52476d2effeOgPb5IbtWFIN6s","messageID":"msg_1adc72895001dzKKsuoSO5pz92","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6b14971f6661e48","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# DeepSeek Harness as a `cli-external-orchestration` runtime\n\n**Lineage:** `deepseek` · **Session:** `fanout-deepseek-1793915913100-enoz0j`\n**Executor:** `cli-opencode` `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` at `max`\n**Harness under study:** `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-rc.1` (npm `latest`), source clone at commit\n`fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159`\n**Iterations:** 10, one per research angle · **Stop reason:** `maxIterationsReached`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nDeepSeek Harness can host a `cli-deepseek` mode, and the integration is smaller than a Pi port in\nthe places that usually cost the most and larger in one place that Pi never had to solve: the\nharness owns model selection, so a dispatch cannot name a model on the command line. The mode has to\ncarry a checked-in route patch per model, pass it with `--patch`, and keep the roster closed in the\nskill packet.\n\nThe headless contract is good for automation:\n\n- `dsh --profile headless` answers one task and exits.\n- stdout carries exactly the final answer, or an NDJSON stream with `--json`.\n- exit `0` means the final turn ended `completed`; every other outcome is `1`.\n- the prompt is a positional argument or stdin via `-`.\n- `--permission-mode` and `--approval-policy` are the only per-dispatch behavior levers; model,\n  provider, reasoning effort and working directory are not flags.\n\nThe harness is ahead of Pi on deterministic exit status, machine-readable events, a real sandbox,\nand native goal/subagent/workflow/skill/MCP services. It is behind on per-dispatch model selection,\nprompt templates, agent-file loading, project plugins and compaction-hook coverage. Six of the ten\nthird-party Pi packages are already native; none needs a port. Sixteen of nineteen Pi guard\nextensions can run through a rewritten Claude-style hook config rather than new plugin code.\n\nThe recommended path is a three-model closed roster (LLM Gateway DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, OpenCode Go\nDeepSeek V4.1 Flash, and optionally one GLM route), a repo `.dsh/` folder holding route patches,\nhook config and generated skill links, one `cli-deepseek` executor kind in the deep-loop runtime, and\nan eleven-phase plan led by a keyed live contract pin.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Scope and Method\n\nTen angles, one per iteration, in the order set by `research-angles.md`. Evidence is a file and line\nin the harness source clone (`dsh-src/<path>:<line>`), a file and line in this repo, the installed\npackage, a read-only `dsh` command, or a live fetch. Documentation-only claims are marked\n`documented, unconfirmed`; guesses are `UNKNOWN`.\n\nTwo live actions were taken, both inside the lineage write surface:\n\n1. `dsh headless --help` (exit 0), which also let the launcher initialize `~/.dsh/profiles/headless`\n   on its own — the angle's read-only allowance covers that side effect.\n2. `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home dsh headless \"Reply with the single word OK\" </dev/null`, exit 1,\n   stderr `dsh: MISSING_CREDENTIAL: llm-deepseek: no API key for provider route \"deepseek-official\"`.\n\nThe harness source, the installed package and the operator's home were never modified.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Headless Dispatch Contract\n\n**Invocation.** `dsh [--profile] headless [options] [task...]`. The task is the positional argument;\nmultiple words are joined; `-` reads stdin. Options: `--json`, `--session-id <id>`,\n`--permission-mode <preset>`, `--approval-policy <ask|never>`, `--add-dir <path>` (repeatable), `-h`.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\n\n**No per-dispatch route.** There is no `--model`, `--provider`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--cwd` or\n`--timeout`. The runner resolves the task and the shared `agentDefaultModel` selection; an adopted\nsession keeps its saved route unless the deployment re-records it.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:128]\n\n**Working directory.** The child process cwd is the workspace: the sandbox row sets\n`workspaceRoot: process.cwd()` and `mode: process.env.DSH_PERMISSION_MODE ?? 'workspace-write'`.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:27-33]\n\n**Output.** Default mode prints only the final answer on stdout; stderr carries\n`dsh: reasoning:` and `dsh: <code>: <message>`. `--json` replaces stdout with NDJSON:\n`session` first, then `status`, `text`, `thinking`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `final` last.\nStrings are capped at 8 KiB, a line at 32 KiB, with `truncated` flags; `final` carries the exact\n`sessionId` and `reason`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:36]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:104]\n\n**Exit status.** `0` only when the last turn ends `completed`; `1` for aborted, error, no owned turn,\nusage errors or an unusable session id. The reliable success predicate is process exit `0` **and**\n`final.reason.kind === 'completed'`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:136]\n\n**Credentials.** Headless disables the managed credential store, `authorization` and\n`deepseek-account`. Keys come from the launch environment, then `<cwd>/.env`, then\n`$DSH_HOME/.env`; GUI-saved keys are ignored. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:56]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:38-46]\n\n**Observed failure.** The smoke produced exit 1, empty stdout and the typed\n`MISSING_CREDENTIAL` line above; first boot initialized a self-contained profile and session tree.\n\n**Comparison.** Pi sets provider, model, thinking level, tools, skills, prompts and session on the\ncommand line; dsh sets only permission and session identity. The mode therefore moves route choice\nfrom the command to a patch file. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:94-134]\n\n---\n\n## 4. Providers, Models and Reasoning\n\n**Route schema.** A custom OpenAI-compatible route is a `llm-pi-ai` row:\n`providers.<id>` with `apiKeyEnv`, `api` (`openai-completions`, `openai-responses`,\n`anthropic-messages`), `baseURL`, a non-empty `models` list, and optional per-model\n`reasoningEfforts`, `compat`, `input`, `contextWindow`, `maxTokens`. The id is permanent, lowercase,\nhyphenated; one provider speaks one protocol. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:27-33]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:123]\n\n**LLM Gateway (inference, not live).** Provider `llmgateway`, `api: openai-completions`, base URL\n`https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`. The gateway takes the bare id, and\nits `runware` upstream refuses the `developer` role, so the route needs\n`compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:89]\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:99]\n\n**OpenCode Go (inference, not live).** Provider `opencode-go`, same protocol, base URL\n`https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`. Its declaration is not\navailability: the 2026-11-05 smoke through OpenCode failed `[overloaded]`, exit 1.\n[SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:52-54]\n\n**Reasoning.** `reasoningEfforts` maps a level to the string sent as `reasoning_effort`; `max` is a\nreal level, DeepSeek's built-in route offers off/low/high/max, and a hand-declared model has no\nlevels until the profile declares them. Unsupported selections fail\n`UNSUPPORTED_REASONING_EFFORT`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:134-166]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2225]\n\n**DeepSeek V4 behind a gateway.** `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` makes `off` send\n`thinking: {type: disabled}` and every other level send `thinking: {type: enabled}` beside the\neffort. Without it, `off` is only the absence of `reasoning_effort`.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:155-166]\n\n**Default route and the patch lever.** Base ships `agent-default-model` with\n`provider: deepseek-official`, `model: deepseek-flash`. A `--patch <path>` overlay is applied after\nthe profile layer and uses the same `id`/`disabled`/`config` row grammar, so it can replace that row\nwith the closed-roster route, including `reasoningEffort`. This is the design inference the phase-002\npin must confirm. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:90-94]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:22-33]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42]\n\n**Fail-closed limits.** The adapter refuses an unconfigured model id, but `agent-default-model` does\nnot validate catalog membership. The closed roster therefore lives in the skill packet and the\ndispatch preflight, not in the harness. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:33]\n\n---\n\n## 5. Profiles, `$DSH_HOME` and the Repo Runtime Folder\n\n**Home.** Explicit config, then `$DSH_HOME`, then `~/.dsh`; a blank override is unset. The shared\nagents root is `$DSH_AGENTS_HOME` or `~/.agents` and sits outside the harness home.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/util/home-paths/README.md:34-52]\n\n**Profile.** `$DSH_HOME/profiles/<name>` with `cordis.yml`, `cordis.patch.yml`, `package.json`,\n`pnpm-workspace.yaml`, plus shared `profiles/node_modules`. There is no project-level profile\nlookup. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/boot/app-boot/README.md:52]\n\n**Workspace instructions.** The one native project read: `$DSH_HOME/AGENTS.md`, then\n`<agentsHome>/AGENTS.md`, then every candidate from the `.git` root to the cwd, broad to specific.\nCandidates default to `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, with `AGENTS.local.md` and `CLAUDE.local.md` as\nadditive overlays; identical content renders once. Each chain has its own `maxBytes`, 65,536 in\nbase; broader files are dropped before the specific file is truncated. The repo's root `AGENTS.md` is\n27,891 bytes and fits. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/context/agent-instructions/README.md:30-40]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/context/agent-instructions/README.md:74-76]\n\n**Repo-local lever.** `--patch <path>` is repeatable and applies after the profile layer; it can\nreplace the default-model row, enable a route, or disable a plugin per dispatch. It is the only\nrepo-local configuration channel. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42]\n\n**Isolation.** `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home` produced a self-contained `headless` profile, session\ntree and storages with no dependency on `~/.dsh`. That is the fan-out isolation mechanism, and it is\nwhy a repo folder must not itself be `$DSH_HOME` by default.\n\n**Repo folder shape.** Smaller than `.pi/` or `.hermes/`:\n\n- `patches/` — route and behavior overlays, unique to this repo.\n- `hooks.json` — rewritten Claude-style hook config for the harness tool names.\n- `mcp.yml` — translated MCP rows.\n- `skills/` — generated per-skill symlinks (Angle 4).\n- `agents/` or `prompts/` — generated only if Angle 5's bridges are adopted.\n- `plugins/` — one hand-authored bundle for the residual guards.\n- `SYNC.md` — the derivation inventory.\n- No `settings.json`: defaults are an `agent-default-model` row and settings persist into the active\n  profile patch.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Skills\n\n**Format.** A skill is `<root>/<name>/SKILL.md` or `<root>/<name>.md`; nested `**/SKILL.md` files are\ndeliberately not discovered. Frontmatter requires a kebab-case `name` and a `description`; optional\nkeys are `whenToUse`, `metadata`, `disable-model-invocation`, `user-invocable`. The parser ignores\nthis repo's `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`, `allowed-tools` and `version`.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts:811-850]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:21-36]\n\n**Roots and ranks.** `<projectRoot>/.dsh/skills` (100), `<projectRoot>/.agents/skills` (200),\n`customSkillDirs` (300), `<dshHome>/skills` (400), `<agentsHome>/skills` (500), bundled (600).\nProject root is the nearest `.git` ancestor, else the cwd.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:46-56]\n\n**Why a whole-tree symlink is wrong.** The repo has 16 top-level skill directories but 57\n`SKILL.md` files. A whole-directory link at `.dsh/skills` would expose only the 16 hubs and hide 41\nnested mode packets. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/SKILL.md:1]\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/SKILL.md:1]\n\n**Right mirror.** A generated per-skill symlink farm: 57 entries, each pointing at its canonical\ndirectory. Symlinked directories keep their resolved instruction path as the resource base, so\n`references/`, `assets/` and `scripts/` stay reachable. There is no scanner or quarantine, unlike\nHermes; markdown-only copies would lose those resources. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:40]\n[SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:20-26]\n\n**Catalog behavior.** No scanner, no size limit, invalid files skipped with a warning, failed roots\nomitted and retried; descriptions capped at 500 characters by default. Duplicate names resolve by\nlayer, then rank, then provider order, so the project root at rank 100 wins.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:85]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/tool-skill/README.md:48]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:84]\n\n---\n\n## 7. Agents, Commands and Goal\n\n**What headless already carries.** Base mounts goal, goal-round-driver, command-goal, plan-mode,\ntool-goal, both in-process subagent providers, subagent and control tools, the workflow engine and\ntool, skill-filesystem and tool-skill. Headless disables only HMR, credentials, authorization and\ndeepseek-account. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:315-453]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:35-46]\n\n**Agent identity.** The `system-prompt` row's `personaPrefix`; headless ships a one-line coding\npersona, and a `--patch` overlay can replace it with an agent body. There is no agent-file loader.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:9-12]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:521-526]\n\n**Presets.** Declarative `agent-preset` rows with `id` and `plugins`, mounted beside\n`agent-preset-registry`, with a `persona` row per composition. Definitions are plugin rows, not\nscanned directories; the registry is mounted by the web app, not by base or headless.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/preset/agent-preset-registry/README.md:26-41]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/preset/persona/README.md:24-35]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:598-599]\n\n**Subagents.** `description`, `prompt`, optional `name` and `cwd`; a child preset only through\n`agent_preset` when `allowedAgentPresets` is set. No persona-file argument: a repo agent is either\ninlined in the prompt or mounted as a preset.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/tool-catalog.md:2064-2110]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:47-53]\n\n**Commands.** Human commands register on `ctx.commands` and dispatch without a model turn; there is\nno filesystem command loader, and headless has no command adapter. `.skilled/commands/**` must become\nprompt templates composed by the dispatcher. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/architecture.md:155]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/command-goal/README.md:12]\n\n**Goal.** One goal per session, compare-and-set by id and revision, 256-round default cap, create and\nedit require a direct human root turn; nothing reads `goal.md`. A packet goal bridge needs a plugin\nhook or explicit instructions that call `create_goal`. The round driver auto-continues while idle,\nwhich is an overrun risk for an unattended leaf. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal/README.md:12-34]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30]\n\n**Plan mode.** Mounted in base, but `exit_plan_mode` presents over the user-questions seam and fails\nclosed without an interactive review; headless has no live approval channel. Keep it off in\ndispatches. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:63]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:93]\n\n---\n\n## 8. Plugins, Hooks and Guards\n\n**Plugin model.** A Cordis object with optional `inject` and `apply(ctx)` or a `Service` subclass,\nregistered as a profile row by package name. A repo-local plugin must be installed into the profile\nas a bundle (`file:`/`link:`); without HMR a change reports `restart-required`.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cordis-primer.md:9]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/boot/plugin-manager/README.md:31]\n\n**Seams.** `tools/pre-execute` (deny/ask), `tools/execute`, `tools/post-execute` (block with feedback\nor attach context), `tools/result`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping` (force another step),\n`agent/created`, `agent/disposed`, `session/event`, `turn/start`, `turn/end`, `approval/request`,\n`fs/write-intent`, `fs/edit-intent`, `fs/delete-intent`, `compaction/start|summary|prune|end`,\n`commands/change`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/event-producer-consumer.md:30-91]\n\n**Claude hook bridge.** Maps `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`,\n`SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`; it does not support `PreCompact` or `SessionEnd`.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/README.md:56-70]\n\n**Matcher mismatch.** Claude literal matchers are exact and case-sensitive; harness tool names are\nlowercase (`bash`, `read`, `write`, `edit`, `glob`, `grep`, `web_fetch`, `apply_patch`, `skill`,\n`subagent`). The repo's `.claude/settings.json` matchers `Bash`, `Write|Edit`, `WebFetch`, `Task`,\n`Task|Agent` and `AskUserQuestion` select nothing. A rewritten `.dsh/hooks.json` is required, not a\nnew plugin. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hook-protocol/src/matcher.ts:60-68]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/tool-catalog.md:26-52]\n\n**Coverage.** `.claude/settings.json` wires 9 `PreToolUse`, 5 `PostToolUse`, 3 `UserPromptSubmit`,\n8 `SessionStart`, 3 `Stop`, 1 `SessionEnd` and 1 `PreCompact` entry over runtime-neutral Node\nscripts. Sixteen of nineteen Pi extensions are bridge-served by the rewritten config.\n`task-dispatch-guard` needs adaptation for the `subagent` tool name and payload; `goal-context` and\n`session-compact-context` need a native plugin. [SOURCE: .claude/settings.json:1]\n[SOURCE: .pi/extensions/README.md:1]\n\n**Package availability correction.** `dsh-hooks-claude-code` exists in the source clone at\n`0.2.2-rc.1` with public publish config, but it is **not** bundled inside the installed package.\nMCP client is bundled; the hook bridge needs an install step. This supersedes the earlier shorthand\nthat called the bridge \"shipped\". [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client/package.json:1]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json:1]\n\n**One bundle or many.** The bulk arrives through the bridge, so `repo-guards` carries two plugins\n(goal context, compact context) and optionally a task-dispatch adapter — one install, one SYNC entry,\none upgrade path. [SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:26-40]\n\n---\n\n## 9. Third-Party Pi Plugin Migration\n\n| Pi package | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `@juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question` | Drop for dispatch; keep interactive | Native user-questions seam, but headless has no answer channel |\n| `@juicesharp/rpiv-todo` | Native replacement | `todo_write` persists across turns and sessions |\n| `pi-blackhole` | Replace compaction, drop memory | `compaction-basic` + result pruner + image offload; no observation store |\n| `pi-btw` | Native replacement | `subagent`/`subagent_fork` + team task board |\n| `pi-cache-optimizer` | Native replacement by config | `cacheControlFormat`, `supportsLongCacheRetention`, route `headers` |\n| `pi-claude-code-ui` | Not relevant to dispatch | Rendering only |\n| `pi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support` | Not portable | No `serviceTier`/`service_tier` model-route field |\n| `pi-plan-build` | Native for interactive; prompt phase for headless | `plan-mode` fails closed without a review |\n| `pi-statusline` | Not relevant to dispatch | Rendering only |\n| `pi-web-access` | Partial native replacement | `web_fetch`/`web_search` + DeepSeek Search/Fetch; PDF/YouTube absent |\n\nNo Pi package is a dsh bundle, and dsh ships no plugin index source, so the plugin market is not a\nmigration path. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/plugin-market.md:12]\n[SOURCE: .pi/PLUGINS.md:16-102]\n\n---\n\n## 10. MCP\n\n**Configuration.** One `dsh-mcp-client` row per server: `serverName`, `transport`\n(`stdio`/`streamable-http`), `command`/`args`/`env`/`cwd` or `url`/`headers`, `toolCallTimeoutMs`\n(60 s), optional `startupTimeoutMs`, `closeTimeoutMs`, `expandTemplates`, `failOnStartupError`.\nTools appear as `mcp__<serverName>__<rawName>`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:32-86]\n\n**Location.** Profile patch or `--patch` only; no project MCP file. `.pi/mcp.json` must be translated\nto `.dsh/mcp.yml` rows. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:23-33]\n\n**Environment.** The stdio bridge scrubs credential-like ambient variables and all `DSH_*` variables;\nname what the server needs in `env`. `expandTemplates` adds `${credential:REF}` resolution but needs\na credentials provider, which headless disables. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:13]\n\n**Code mode.** Translates to `node .skilled/bin/mcp-code-mode-launcher.cjs` with\n`UTCP_CONFIG_FILE=.utcp_config.json` and cwd at the repo root. `lifecycle: lazy` has no harness\nequivalent; the connection becomes eager and is bounded by `startupTimeoutMs`.\n[SOURCE: .pi/mcp.json:1]\n\n**Per-dispatch control.** Composition only: omit the rows for no MCP, pass an MCP patch for exactly\nthose servers. The live `mcp-manager` fleet is web/desktop only. Base mounts `mcp-resources` but not\n`mcp-client`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-manager/README.md:12]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:505-506]\n\n**Untrusted text.** Server instructions join the system prompt as literal text up to 32 KiB; prompt\ntemplates are unsupported. Treat them as data, never instructions.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:12]\n\n---\n\n## 11. Deep-Loop Fan-Out Fitness\n\n**Registration.** A new kind touches seven `executor-config.ts` tables: `EXECUTOR_KINDS`, flag\nsupport, preventive-sandbox capability, web-search policy, MCP capability, defaults, and the\nallowlist/default/pin. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11-276]\n\n**Builder.** `dsh --profile headless --json --permission-mode <mode> --approval-policy never\n--patch <route.yml> -` with the prompt as `input`. `-` is required: a positional task makes the\nharness ignore stdin. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:46]\n\n**Permission.** `workspace-write` confines writes to cwd plus `--add-dir`; `read-only` denies writes;\n`danger-full-access` bypasses; an unusable backend fails `SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE` rather than running\nunconfined. `--approval-policy never` is mandatory unattended.\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12]\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:58-60]\n\n**Timeout.** No turn or time budget exists. The runner's `timeoutSeconds` and signal kill are the\nonly bound; the lineage patch must disable goal and plan to prevent 256-round overruns and\nfail-closed plan reviews. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30]\n\n**State isolation.** `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home`.\n\n**Environment.** The dispatch filter allows PATH, HOME, LANG, TMPDIR, NODE_PATH, TERM, USER,\nLOGNAME, `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING`, `LC_*`, plus per-kind prefixes. `cli-deepseek` needs\n`DSH_HOME` as a key and `LLMGATEWAY_`/`DEEPSEEK_` prefixes — never a blanket `DSH_` prefix.\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:129-186]\n\n**Recursion.** The guard needs `SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID` plus the kind in\n`SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK`; map the `dsh` binary to `cli-deepseek` so a nested dsh dispatch fails\nclosed. dsh has no native self-invocation guard.\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3700-3730]\n\n**Exit.** Deterministic, so a non-zero exit is a real failure. Unlike Pi, no exception is needed;\nclassify `1` via the `--json` `error` event or `final.reason`.\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4045-4056]\n\n**Touch list.** 22 rows:\n\n1. `executor-config.ts` — seven tables.\n2. `fanout-run.cjs` — builder, adapter map, binary probe, route map, state env, recursion binary.\n3. `executor-audit.ts` — env keys/prefixes.\n4-8. Unit tests: `executor-config`, `fanout-run`, `combo-matrix`, `executor-audit`,\n   `verify-iteration`.\n9-13. Stress adapter: `matrix-manifest.ts`, `live-contracts.json`, `cli-deepseek.vitest.ts`,\n   `shims/deepseek-shim.cjs`, `README.md`.\n14. `dispatch-audit.mjs` + its test.\n15. `dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs`.\n16. `deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs` + tests.\n17. Deep-mode SKILLs: `deep-ai-council`, `deep-research`, `deep-review`.\n18. Command assets: 6 YAMLs, 3 presentation files, 2 compiled contracts.\n19. `doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`.\n20. Compiled-routing fixture + build harness.\n21. Hub files: `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, `README.md`, `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json`,\n    `leaf-manifest.json`, `graph-metadata.json`, `description.json`, `feature-catalog/`, plus\n    sibling mode tables.\n22. Propagation: advisor sync script, `sk-prompt` SKILL + card, `orchestrate.md`,\n    `prompt-improver.md`, root `AGENTS.md`/`README.md`/`SECURITY.md`/`skills/README.txt`, trigger\n    index, two sk-doc manifests, fan-out feature catalog.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Cross-Runtime Comparison\n\n| Dimension | dsh headless | `pi -p` |\n|---|---|---|\n| Model selection | Profile/patch only | `--provider` + `--model` per dispatch |\n| Reasoning | `reasoningEfforts` in route | `--thinking` per dispatch |\n| Prompt input | positional or stdin `-` | positional |\n| Output | final text or NDJSON | text, JSON, RPC |\n| Exit status | deterministic 0/1 + `final.reason` | non-deterministic; parse text |\n| Sandbox | real, fail-closed `read-only`/`workspace-write`/`danger-full-access` | none; tool allowlist only |\n| Tool allowlist | preset/profile composition | `--tools`, `--exclude-tools` |\n| Skills | one-level root scan, per-skill symlink | recursive/whole-dir symlink |\n| Agents | persona prefix, presets, subagent prompt | agent files, `--append-system-prompt` |\n| Commands | prompt templates (no native loader) | `--prompt-template` |\n| Hooks | plugin seams + Claude bridge | native extension API |\n| MCP | `dsh-mcp-client` rows | extension/MCP config |\n| Startup | ~1.16 s profile boot + model | process start + model |\n| Footprint | 896 MB, Node 24.9+, 90 deps | npm package + extensions |\n| Versioning | `0.2.2-rc.1`, rc cadence | release cadence |\n\n---\n\n## 13. Recommended `.dsh/` Layout\n\n```text\n.dsh/\n  SYNC.md                 # what is generated, what is authored, drift checks\n  patches/\n    llmgateway-deepseek.yml    # route + agent-default-model + compat\n    opencode-go-deepseek.yml   # route + agent-default-model + compat\n    lineage-guards.yml         # disable goal, goal-round-driver, plan-mode, telemetry\n  hooks.json              # Claude-style config with harness tool names\n  mcp.yml                 # code_mode row translated from .pi/mcp.json\n  skills/                 # generated per-skill symlinks (57)\n  prompts/                # generated command templates (flattened paths)\n  plugins/repo-guards/    # hand-authored bundle: goal context + compact context\n```\n\nNo profile, no `settings.json`, no `node_modules`, no `AGENTS.md` copy. `DSH_HOME` stays outside the\nrepo; a lineage points it at its own subdirectory.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Hard Rules for the Packet\n\n1. `headless-dash-stdin-required` — prompt on stdin through `-`, stdin closed.\n2. `route-patch-required` — no `--model`; one checked-in patch per route, model must be on the roster.\n3. `approval-never-required` — unattended leaves pass `--approval-policy never`.\n4. `headless-only` — never dispatch `web`, `tui`, `acp`, `sdk` or `sdk-minimal`.\n5. `dsh-home-isolated` — per-lineage `DSH_HOME`.\n6. `goal-plan-disabled` — lineage patch disables goal, goal-round-driver and plan-mode.\n7. `json-exit-classification` — require exit 0 and `final.reason.kind === 'completed'`; classify 1\n   from the JSON `error`/`final.reason`.\n8. `telemetry-disabled` — patch the telemetry row to `DISABLED` (or set `DSH_TELEMETRY_MODE`).\n9. `profile-version-check` — `command -v dsh` and the installed version match the pinned rc.\n10. `route-compat-pinned` — `supportsDeveloperRole: false` and `thinkingFormat: deepseek` on both\n    gateway routes.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Phase Plan\n\n| Rank | Phase | Outcome | Depends | Risk | Mode | Required | Prevents |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 002 live contract pin | Keyed write dispatch, verbatim IO, JSON parse, bash and sandbox | operator key | backend missing; native builds | `sk-code` verify | required | building on docs only |\n| 2 | 003 skill packet | SKILL/ROUTER/hard rules/references/assets | 002 | rule drift | `sk-doc` create-skill | required | ad-hoc dispatch |\n| 3 | 004 executor kind | tables, builder, audit, tests | 002 | patch route; stdin misuse | `sk-code` implement | required | unverified provenance |\n| 4 | 005 runtime folder | patches, hooks, MCP, SYNC, skill links | 003, 004 | link farm misses | `sk-code` + `sk-doc` | required | config drift |\n| 5 | 006 hub registration | registry, hub, advisor, doctor, fixtures | 003 | unroutable mode | `sk-doc` + `sk-code` | required | no selection path |\n| 6 | 007 command/agent bridges | templates, persona, goal context | 005 | truncation | `sk-doc` create-command/agent | parity required | reinvention |\n| 7 | 008 hooks + guards | rewritten config, bundle, adapter | 005 | bridge install | `sk-code` implement | optional | guard loss |\n| 8 | 009 MCP | mcp.yml, code-mode, route guard | 005 | scrubbed env | `sk-code` implement | optional | MCP absence/leak |\n| 9 | 010 benchmark | playbook + benchmark index | 002-009 | unverified claims | `sk-doc` create-benchmark | optional | claims without proof |\n| 10 | 011 propagation | trigger index, manifests, changelog | 006 | stale index | `sk-code` implement | required before merge | dangling routing |\n| 11 | 012 rc re-pin | refreshed contract and roster | 002 | rc breakage | `sk-code` verify | per bump | silent break |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Eliminated Alternatives\n\n- **A `--model`/`--provider` dispatch flag.** Does not exist; route selection is profile config.\n- **A repo-local profile.** Profile lookup is `$DSH_HOME`-only and would need `node_modules`.\n- **A whole-tree skill symlink.** One-level discovery hides 41 of 57 skills.\n- **Markdown-only skill copies.** Lose `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` with no scanner reason.\n- **Porting all 18 Pi extensions.** Sixteen are bridge-served by the repo's existing hook scripts.\n- **Mounting `.claude/settings.json` unchanged.** Capitalized matchers never match lowercase tools.\n- **Porting Pi packages as dsh plugins.** None is a dsh bundle; six capabilities are native.\n- **Reading `.pi/mcp.json` directly.** No project MCP config scan.\n- **A per-run turn budget.** None exists; disable goal/plan and rely on the runner timeout.\n- **Reusing Pi's exit-code exception.** dsh's exit status is deterministic.\n- **Plan mode as an unattended gate.** It fails closed without an interactive review.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Divergence Map\n\n- **Saturated directions:** none. The lineage ran one pass per angle with no repeated focus and no\n  pivot record.\n- **Completed pivots:** 0. **Failed pivots:** 0. **Audited overrides:** 0.\n- **Frontier:** the nine `UNKNOWN` items in §18, all gated on a configured provider key or a package\n  install.\n- **Evidence base:** 88 findings, 158 code citations and 25 other citations across ten iterations.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Open Questions / `UNKNOWN`\n\n1. Does `--patch` actually repoint `agent-default-model` in a headless dispatch?\n2. Does LLM Gateway accept `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` with `reasoningEffort: max`, and does it\n   reject `supportsDeveloperRole` without the compat flag?\n3. Does the `bash` tool work after the skipped `koffi` and `node-pty` install scripts?\n4. Does a 57-entry per-skill symlink farm load all entries in one session?\n5. Is `dsh-hooks-claude-code` installable from npm at `0.2.2-rc.1`, and do the rewritten matchers\n   fire each script with a compatible payload?\n6. Does code-mode MCP connect under the scrubbed stdio environment with only `UTCP_CONFIG_FILE`?\n7. What are the real startup-plus-model latency and cost per iteration?\n8. Does telemetry stay silent in `FEEDBACK_ONLY` on every headless exit path?\n9. How stable is the `0.2.2-rc.*` surface across rc bumps?\n\n---\n\n## 19. References\n\n- Harness source clone: `dsh-src/` at `fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159`\n  (`/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src`).\n- Installed package: `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh`.\n- Resource map: `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md`.\n- Research angles: `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research-angles.md`.\n- Repo runtime precedents: `.pi/SYNC.md`, `.pi/PLUGINS.md`, `.hermes/SYNC.md`.\n- Deep-loop runtime: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`,\n  `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts`.\n- Hook layer: `.claude/settings.json`, `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs`.\n- Iteration files: `research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-010.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Convergence Report\n\n- **Stop reason:** `maxIterationsReached` (the configured cap; convergence is telemetry only for this\n  lineage)\n- **Total iterations:** 10\n- **Questions answered:** 10 / 10\n- **Remaining questions:** 0; nine `UNKNOWN` items are recorded as open evidence gaps, not unanswered\n  angle questions\n- **Last 3 iteration summaries:** run 8 MCP (0.88) · run 9 fan-out fitness (0.90) · run 10 constraints\n  and phase plan (0.85)\n- **Convergence threshold:** 0.05 (not reached; the cap is authoritative)\n- **Divergence summary:** no divergent pivots; one correction (hook bridge not bundled) supersedes an\n  earlier shorthand\n- **Average newInfoRatio:** 0.881\n- **Source coverage:** 158 code citations, 25 other citations\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# DeepSeek Harness as a `cli-external-orchestration` runtime\\n\\n**Lineage:** `deepseek` · **Session:** `fanout-deepseek-1793915913100-enoz0j`\\n**Executor:** `cli-opencode` `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017` at `max`\\n**Harness under study:** `@deepseek-ai/dsh@0.2.2-rc.1` (npm `latest`), source clone at commit\\n`fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159`\\n**Iterations:** 10, one per research angle · **Stop reason:** `maxIterationsReached`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\nDeepSeek Harness can host a `cli-deepseek` mode, and the integration is smaller than a Pi port in\\nthe places that usually cost the most and larger in one place that Pi never had to solve: the\\nharness owns model selection, so a dispatch cannot name a model on the command line. The mode has to\\ncarry a checked-in route patch per model, pass it with `--patch`, and keep the roster closed in the\\nskill packet.\\n\\nThe headless contract is good for automation:\\n\\n- `dsh --profile headless` answers one task and exits.\\n- stdout carries exactly the final answer, or an NDJSON stream with `--json`.\\n- exit `0` means the final turn ended `completed`; every other outcome is `1`.\\n- the prompt is a positional argument or stdin via `-`.\\n- `--permission-mode` and `--approval-policy` are the only per-dispatch behavior levers; model,\\n  provider, reasoning effort and working directory are not flags.\\n\\nThe harness is ahead of Pi on deterministic exit status, machine-readable events, a real sandbox,\\nand native goal/subagent/workflow/skill/MCP services. It is behind on per-dispatch model selection,\\nprompt templates, agent-file loading, project plugins and compaction-hook coverage. Six of the ten\\nthird-party Pi packages are already native; none needs a port. Sixteen of nineteen Pi guard\\nextensions can run through a rewritten Claude-style hook config rather than new plugin code.\\n\\nThe recommended path is a three-model closed roster (LLM Gateway DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, OpenCode Go\\nDeepSeek V4.1 Flash, and optionally one GLM route), a repo `.dsh/` folder holding route patches,\\nhook config and generated skill links, one `cli-deepseek` executor kind in the deep-loop runtime, and\\nan eleven-phase plan led by a keyed live contract pin.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Scope and Method\\n\\nTen angles, one per iteration, in the order set by `research-angles.md`. Evidence is a file and line\\nin the harness source clone (`dsh-src/<path>:<line>`), a file and line in this repo, the installed\\npackage, a read-only `dsh` command, or a live fetch. Documentation-only claims are marked\\n`documented, unconfirmed`; guesses are `UNKNOWN`.\\n\\nTwo live actions were taken, both inside the lineage write surface:\\n\\n1. `dsh headless --help` (exit 0), which also let the launcher initialize `~/.dsh/profiles/headless`\\n   on its own — the angle's read-only allowance covers that side effect.\\n2. `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home dsh headless \\\"Reply with the single word OK\\\" </dev/null`, exit 1,\\n   stderr `dsh: MISSING_CREDENTIAL: llm-deepseek: no API key for provider route \\\"deepseek-official\\\"`.\\n\\nThe harness source, the installed package and the operator's home were never modified.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Headless Dispatch Contract\\n\\n**Invocation.** `dsh [--profile] headless [options] [task...]`. The task is the positional argument;\\nmultiple words are joined; `-` reads stdin. Options: `--json`, `--session-id <id>`,\\n`--permission-mode <preset>`, `--approval-policy <ask|never>`, `--add-dir <path>` (repeatable), `-h`.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\\n\\n**No per-dispatch route.** There is no `--model`, `--provider`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--cwd` or\\n`--timeout`. The runner resolves the task and the shared `agentDefaultModel` selection; an adopted\\nsession keeps its saved route unless the deployment re-records it.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:128]\\n\\n**Working directory.** The child process cwd is the workspace: the sandbox row sets\\n`workspaceRoot: process.cwd()` and `mode: process.env.DSH_PERMISSION_MODE ?? 'workspace-write'`.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:27-33]\\n\\n**Output.** Default mode prints only the final answer on stdout; stderr carries\\n`dsh: reasoning:` and `dsh: <code>: <message>`. `--json` replaces stdout with NDJSON:\\n`session` first, then `status`, `text`, `thinking`, `tool_call`, `tool_result`, and `final` last.\\nStrings are capped at 8 KiB, a line at 32 KiB, with `truncated` flags; `final` carries the exact\\n`sessionId` and `reason`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:36]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:104]\\n\\n**Exit status.** `0` only when the last turn ends `completed`; `1` for aborted, error, no owned turn,\\nusage errors or an unusable session id. The reliable success predicate is process exit `0` **and**\\n`final.reason.kind === 'completed'`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:12]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:136]\\n\\n**Credentials.** Headless disables the managed credential store, `authorization` and\\n`deepseek-account`. Keys come from the launch environment, then `<cwd>/.env`, then\\n`$DSH_HOME/.env`; GUI-saved keys are ignored. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:56]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:38-46]\\n\\n**Observed failure.** The smoke produced exit 1, empty stdout and the typed\\n`MISSING_CREDENTIAL` line above; first boot initialized a self-contained profile and session tree.\\n\\n**Comparison.** Pi sets provider, model, thinking level, tools, skills, prompts and session on the\\ncommand line; dsh sets only permission and session identity. The mode therefore moves route choice\\nfrom the command to a patch file. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/cli-reference.md:94-134]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Providers, Models and Reasoning\\n\\n**Route schema.** A custom OpenAI-compatible route is a `llm-pi-ai` row:\\n`providers.<id>` with `apiKeyEnv`, `api` (`openai-completions`, `openai-responses`,\\n`anthropic-messages`), `baseURL`, a non-empty `models` list, and optional per-model\\n`reasoningEfforts`, `compat`, `input`, `contextWindow`, `maxTokens`. The id is permanent, lowercase,\\nhyphenated; one provider speaks one protocol. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:27-33]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/llm/llm-pi-ai/README.md:123]\\n\\n**LLM Gateway (inference, not live).** Provider `llmgateway`, `api: openai-completions`, base URL\\n`https://api.llmgateway.io/v1`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017`. The gateway takes the bare id, and\\nits `runware` upstream refuses the `developer` role, so the route needs\\n`compat.supportsDeveloperRole: false`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:89]\\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/references/providers-and-models.md:99]\\n\\n**OpenCode Go (inference, not live).** Provider `opencode-go`, same protocol, base URL\\n`https://opencode.ai/inference/go/openai/v1`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`. Its declaration is not\\navailability: the 2026-11-05 smoke through OpenCode failed `[overloaded]`, exit 1.\\n[SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md:52-54]\\n\\n**Reasoning.** `reasoningEfforts` maps a level to the string sent as `reasoning_effort`; `max` is a\\nreal level, DeepSeek's built-in route offers off/low/high/max, and a hand-declared model has no\\nlevels until the profile declares them. Unsupported selections fail\\n`UNSUPPORTED_REASONING_EFFORT`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:134-166]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/config-catalog.md:2225]\\n\\n**DeepSeek V4 behind a gateway.** `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` makes `off` send\\n`thinking: {type: disabled}` and every other level send `thinking: {type: enabled}` beside the\\neffort. Without it, `off` is only the absence of `reasoning_effort`.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/providers.md:155-166]\\n\\n**Default route and the patch lever.** Base ships `agent-default-model` with\\n`provider: deepseek-official`, `model: deepseek-flash`. A `--patch <path>` overlay is applied after\\nthe profile layer and uses the same `id`/`disabled`/`config` row grammar, so it can replace that row\\nwith the closed-roster route, including `reasoningEffort`. This is the design inference the phase-002\\npin must confirm. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:90-94]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:22-33]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42]\\n\\n**Fail-closed limits.** The adapter refuses an unconfigured model id, but `agent-default-model` does\\nnot validate catalog membership. The closed roster therefore lives in the skill packet and the\\ndispatch preflight, not in the harness. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/core/agent-default-model/README.md:33]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Profiles, `$DSH_HOME` and the Repo Runtime Folder\\n\\n**Home.** Explicit config, then `$DSH_HOME`, then `~/.dsh`; a blank override is unset. The shared\\nagents root is `$DSH_AGENTS_HOME` or `~/.agents` and sits outside the harness home.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/util/home-paths/README.md:34-52]\\n\\n**Profile.** `$DSH_HOME/profiles/<name>` with `cordis.yml`, `cordis.patch.yml`, `package.json`,\\n`pnpm-workspace.yaml`, plus shared `profiles/node_modules`. There is no project-level profile\\nlookup. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/boot/app-boot/README.md:52]\\n\\n**Workspace instructions.** The one native project read: `$DSH_HOME/AGENTS.md`, then\\n`<agentsHome>/AGENTS.md`, then every candidate from the `.git` root to the cwd, broad to specific.\\nCandidates default to `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, with `AGENTS.local.md` and `CLAUDE.local.md` as\\nadditive overlays; identical content renders once. Each chain has its own `maxBytes`, 65,536 in\\nbase; broader files are dropped before the specific file is truncated. The repo's root `AGENTS.md` is\\n27,891 bytes and fits. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/context/agent-instructions/README.md:30-40]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/context/agent-instructions/README.md:74-76]\\n\\n**Repo-local lever.** `--patch <path>` is repeatable and applies after the profile layer; it can\\nreplace the default-model row, enable a route, or disable a plugin per dispatch. It is the only\\nrepo-local configuration channel. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:41-42]\\n\\n**Isolation.** `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home` produced a self-contained `headless` profile, session\\ntree and storages with no dependency on `~/.dsh`. That is the fan-out isolation mechanism, and it is\\nwhy a repo folder must not itself be `$DSH_HOME` by default.\\n\\n**Repo folder shape.** Smaller than `.pi/` or `.hermes/`:\\n\\n- `patches/` — route and behavior overlays, unique to this repo.\\n- `hooks.json` — rewritten Claude-style hook config for the harness tool names.\\n- `mcp.yml` — translated MCP rows.\\n- `skills/` — generated per-skill symlinks (Angle 4).\\n- `agents/` or `prompts/` — generated only if Angle 5's bridges are adopted.\\n- `plugins/` — one hand-authored bundle for the residual guards.\\n- `SYNC.md` — the derivation inventory.\\n- No `settings.json`: defaults are an `agent-default-model` row and settings persist into the active\\n  profile patch.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Skills\\n\\n**Format.** A skill is `<root>/<name>/SKILL.md` or `<root>/<name>.md`; nested `**/SKILL.md` files are\\ndeliberately not discovered. Frontmatter requires a kebab-case `name` and a `description`; optional\\nkeys are `whenToUse`, `metadata`, `disable-model-invocation`, `user-invocable`. The parser ignores\\nthis repo's `trigger_phrases`, `importance_tier`, `contextType`, `allowed-tools` and `version`.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:36]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/src/index.ts:811-850]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:21-36]\\n\\n**Roots and ranks.** `<projectRoot>/.dsh/skills` (100), `<projectRoot>/.agents/skills` (200),\\n`customSkillDirs` (300), `<dshHome>/skills` (400), `<agentsHome>/skills` (500), bundled (600).\\nProject root is the nearest `.git` ancestor, else the cwd.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:46-56]\\n\\n**Why a whole-tree symlink is wrong.** The repo has 16 top-level skill directories but 57\\n`SKILL.md` files. A whole-directory link at `.dsh/skills` would expose only the 16 hubs and hide 41\\nnested mode packets. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/SKILL.md:1]\\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-pi/SKILL.md:1]\\n\\n**Right mirror.** A generated per-skill symlink farm: 57 entries, each pointing at its canonical\\ndirectory. Symlinked directories keep their resolved instruction path as the resource base, so\\n`references/`, `assets/` and `scripts/` stay reachable. There is no scanner or quarantine, unlike\\nHermes; markdown-only copies would lose those resources. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:40]\\n[SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:20-26]\\n\\n**Catalog behavior.** No scanner, no size limit, invalid files skipped with a warning, failed roots\\nomitted and retried; descriptions capped at 500 characters by default. Duplicate names resolve by\\nlayer, then rank, then provider order, so the project root at rank 100 wins.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill-filesystem/README.md:85]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/tool-skill/README.md:48]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/skill/skill/src/index.ts:84]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Agents, Commands and Goal\\n\\n**What headless already carries.** Base mounts goal, goal-round-driver, command-goal, plan-mode,\\ntool-goal, both in-process subagent providers, subagent and control tools, the workflow engine and\\ntool, skill-filesystem and tool-skill. Headless disables only HMR, credentials, authorization and\\ndeepseek-account. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:315-453]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:35-46]\\n\\n**Agent identity.** The `system-prompt` row's `personaPrefix`; headless ships a one-line coding\\npersona, and a `--patch` overlay can replace it with an agent body. There is no agent-file loader.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/cordis.patch.yml:9-12]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:521-526]\\n\\n**Presets.** Declarative `agent-preset` rows with `id` and `plugins`, mounted beside\\n`agent-preset-registry`, with a `persona` row per composition. Definitions are plugin rows, not\\nscanned directories; the registry is mounted by the web app, not by base or headless.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/preset/agent-preset-registry/README.md:26-41]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/preset/persona/README.md:24-35]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/web-app/cordis.patch.yml:598-599]\\n\\n**Subagents.** `description`, `prompt`, optional `name` and `cwd`; a child preset only through\\n`agent_preset` when `allowedAgentPresets` is set. No persona-file argument: a repo agent is either\\ninlined in the prompt or mounted as a preset.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/tool-catalog.md:2064-2110]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/subagent/tool-subagent/README.md:47-53]\\n\\n**Commands.** Human commands register on `ctx.commands` and dispatch without a model turn; there is\\nno filesystem command loader, and headless has no command adapter. `.skilled/commands/**` must become\\nprompt templates composed by the dispatcher. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/architecture.md:155]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/command-goal/README.md:12]\\n\\n**Goal.** One goal per session, compare-and-set by id and revision, 256-round default cap, create and\\nedit require a direct human root turn; nothing reads `goal.md`. A packet goal bridge needs a plugin\\nhook or explicit instructions that call `create_goal`. The round driver auto-continues while idle,\\nwhich is an overrun risk for an unattended leaf. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal/README.md:12-34]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30]\\n\\n**Plan mode.** Mounted in base, but `exit_plan_mode` presents over the user-questions seam and fails\\nclosed without an interactive review; headless has no live approval channel. Keep it off in\\ndispatches. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:63]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/plan/plan-mode/README.md:93]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Plugins, Hooks and Guards\\n\\n**Plugin model.** A Cordis object with optional `inject` and `apply(ctx)` or a `Service` subclass,\\nregistered as a profile row by package name. A repo-local plugin must be installed into the profile\\nas a bundle (`file:`/`link:`); without HMR a change reports `restart-required`.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cordis-primer.md:9]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/boot/plugin-manager/README.md:31]\\n\\n**Seams.** `tools/pre-execute` (deny/ask), `tools/execute`, `tools/post-execute` (block with feedback\\nor attach context), `tools/result`, `agent/pre-step`, `agent/turn-stopping` (force another step),\\n`agent/created`, `agent/disposed`, `session/event`, `turn/start`, `turn/end`, `approval/request`,\\n`fs/write-intent`, `fs/edit-intent`, `fs/delete-intent`, `compaction/start|summary|prune|end`,\\n`commands/change`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/event-producer-consumer.md:30-91]\\n\\n**Claude hook bridge.** Maps `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`,\\n`SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`; it does not support `PreCompact` or `SessionEnd`.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/README.md:56-70]\\n\\n**Matcher mismatch.** Claude literal matchers are exact and case-sensitive; harness tool names are\\nlowercase (`bash`, `read`, `write`, `edit`, `glob`, `grep`, `web_fetch`, `apply_patch`, `skill`,\\n`subagent`). The repo's `.claude/settings.json` matchers `Bash`, `Write|Edit`, `WebFetch`, `Task`,\\n`Task|Agent` and `AskUserQuestion` select nothing. A rewritten `.dsh/hooks.json` is required, not a\\nnew plugin. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hook-protocol/src/matcher.ts:60-68]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/tool-catalog.md:26-52]\\n\\n**Coverage.** `.claude/settings.json` wires 9 `PreToolUse`, 5 `PostToolUse`, 3 `UserPromptSubmit`,\\n8 `SessionStart`, 3 `Stop`, 1 `SessionEnd` and 1 `PreCompact` entry over runtime-neutral Node\\nscripts. Sixteen of nineteen Pi extensions are bridge-served by the rewritten config.\\n`task-dispatch-guard` needs adaptation for the `subagent` tool name and payload; `goal-context` and\\n`session-compact-context` need a native plugin. [SOURCE: .claude/settings.json:1]\\n[SOURCE: .pi/extensions/README.md:1]\\n\\n**Package availability correction.** `dsh-hooks-claude-code` exists in the source clone at\\n`0.2.2-rc.1` with public publish config, but it is **not** bundled inside the installed package.\\nMCP client is bundled; the hook bridge needs an install step. This supersedes the earlier shorthand\\nthat called the bridge \\\"shipped\\\". [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client/package.json:1]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/experimental/hooks-claude-code/package.json:1]\\n\\n**One bundle or many.** The bulk arrives through the bridge, so `repo-guards` carries two plugins\\n(goal context, compact context) and optionally a task-dispatch adapter — one install, one SYNC entry,\\none upgrade path. [SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:26-40]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Third-Party Pi Plugin Migration\\n\\n| Pi package | Verdict | Evidence |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `@juicesharp/rpiv-ask-user-question` | Drop for dispatch; keep interactive | Native user-questions seam, but headless has no answer channel |\\n| `@juicesharp/rpiv-todo` | Native replacement | `todo_write` persists across turns and sessions |\\n| `pi-blackhole` | Replace compaction, drop memory | `compaction-basic` + result pruner + image offload; no observation store |\\n| `pi-btw` | Native replacement | `subagent`/`subagent_fork` + team task board |\\n| `pi-cache-optimizer` | Native replacement by config | `cacheControlFormat`, `supportsLongCacheRetention`, route `headers` |\\n| `pi-claude-code-ui` | Not relevant to dispatch | Rendering only |\\n| `pi-fast-mode-w-subagent-support` | Not portable | No `serviceTier`/`service_tier` model-route field |\\n| `pi-plan-build` | Native for interactive; prompt phase for headless | `plan-mode` fails closed without a review |\\n| `pi-statusline` | Not relevant to dispatch | Rendering only |\\n| `pi-web-access` | Partial native replacement | `web_fetch`/`web_search` + DeepSeek Search/Fetch; PDF/YouTube absent |\\n\\nNo Pi package is a dsh bundle, and dsh ships no plugin index source, so the plugin market is not a\\nmigration path. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/plugin-market.md:12]\\n[SOURCE: .pi/PLUGINS.md:16-102]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. MCP\\n\\n**Configuration.** One `dsh-mcp-client` row per server: `serverName`, `transport`\\n(`stdio`/`streamable-http`), `command`/`args`/`env`/`cwd` or `url`/`headers`, `toolCallTimeoutMs`\\n(60 s), optional `startupTimeoutMs`, `closeTimeoutMs`, `expandTemplates`, `failOnStartupError`.\\nTools appear as `mcp__<serverName>__<rawName>`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:32-86]\\n\\n**Location.** Profile patch or `--patch` only; no project MCP file. `.pi/mcp.json` must be translated\\nto `.dsh/mcp.yml` rows. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:23-33]\\n\\n**Environment.** The stdio bridge scrubs credential-like ambient variables and all `DSH_*` variables;\\nname what the server needs in `env`. `expandTemplates` adds `${credential:REF}` resolution but needs\\na credentials provider, which headless disables. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/user/guide/mcp-memory.md:13]\\n\\n**Code mode.** Translates to `node .skilled/bin/mcp-code-mode-launcher.cjs` with\\n`UTCP_CONFIG_FILE=.utcp_config.json` and cwd at the repo root. `lifecycle: lazy` has no harness\\nequivalent; the connection becomes eager and is bounded by `startupTimeoutMs`.\\n[SOURCE: .pi/mcp.json:1]\\n\\n**Per-dispatch control.** Composition only: omit the rows for no MCP, pass an MCP patch for exactly\\nthose servers. The live `mcp-manager` fleet is web/desktop only. Base mounts `mcp-resources` but not\\n`mcp-client`. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-manager/README.md:12]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/base/cordis.patch.yml:505-506]\\n\\n**Untrusted text.** Server instructions join the system prompt as literal text up to 32 KiB; prompt\\ntemplates are unsupported. Treat them as data, never instructions.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/mcp/mcp-client/README.md:12]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Deep-Loop Fan-Out Fitness\\n\\n**Registration.** A new kind touches seven `executor-config.ts` tables: `EXECUTOR_KINDS`, flag\\nsupport, preventive-sandbox capability, web-search policy, MCP capability, defaults, and the\\nallowlist/default/pin. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:11-276]\\n\\n**Builder.** `dsh --profile headless --json --permission-mode <mode> --approval-policy never\\n--patch <route.yml> -` with the prompt as `input`. `-` is required: a positional task makes the\\nharness ignore stdin. [SOURCE: dsh-src/docs/cli-help.md:100-132]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/bundle/headless/README.md:46]\\n\\n**Permission.** `workspace-write` confines writes to cwd plus `--add-dir`; `read-only` denies writes;\\n`danger-full-access` bypasses; an unusable backend fails `SANDBOX_UNAVAILABLE` rather than running\\nunconfined. `--approval-policy never` is mandatory unattended.\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:12]\\n[SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/sandbox/sandbox/README.md:58-60]\\n\\n**Timeout.** No turn or time budget exists. The runner's `timeoutSeconds` and signal kill are the\\nonly bound; the lineage patch must disable goal and plan to prevent 256-round overruns and\\nfail-closed plan reviews. [SOURCE: dsh-src/packages/goal/goal-round-driver/README.md:12-30]\\n\\n**State isolation.** `DSH_HOME=<lineage>/.dsh-home`.\\n\\n**Environment.** The dispatch filter allows PATH, HOME, LANG, TMPDIR, NODE_PATH, TERM, USER,\\nLOGNAME, `__CF_USER_TEXT_ENCODING`, `LC_*`, plus per-kind prefixes. `cli-deepseek` needs\\n`DSH_HOME` as a key and `LLMGATEWAY_`/`DEEPSEEK_` prefixes — never a blanket `DSH_` prefix.\\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts:129-186]\\n\\n**Recursion.** The guard needs `SPECKIT_FANOUT_LINEAGE_ID` plus the kind in\\n`SPECKIT_CLI_DISPATCH_STACK`; map the `dsh` binary to `cli-deepseek` so a nested dsh dispatch fails\\nclosed. dsh has no native self-invocation guard.\\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:3700-3730]\\n\\n**Exit.** Deterministic, so a non-zero exit is a real failure. Unlike Pi, no exception is needed;\\nclassify `1` via the `--json` `error` event or `final.reason`.\\n[SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:4045-4056]\\n\\n**Touch list.** 22 rows:\\n\\n1. `executor-config.ts` — seven tables.\\n2. `fanout-run.cjs` — builder, adapter map, binary probe, route map, state env, recursion binary.\\n3. `executor-audit.ts` — env keys/prefixes.\\n4-8. Unit tests: `executor-config`, `fanout-run`, `combo-matrix`, `executor-audit`,\\n   `verify-iteration`.\\n9-13. Stress adapter: `matrix-manifest.ts`, `live-contracts.json`, `cli-deepseek.vitest.ts`,\\n   `shims/deepseek-shim.cjs`, `README.md`.\\n14. `dispatch-audit.mjs` + its test.\\n15. `dispatch-rule-checks.test.mjs`.\\n16. `deep-ai-council/scripts/orchestrate-session.cjs` + tests.\\n17. Deep-mode SKILLs: `deep-ai-council`, `deep-research`, `deep-review`.\\n18. Command assets: 6 YAMLs, 3 presentation files, 2 compiled contracts.\\n19. `doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json`.\\n20. Compiled-routing fixture + build harness.\\n21. Hub files: `SKILL.md`, `ROUTER.md`, `README.md`, `mode-registry.json`, `hub-router.json`,\\n    `leaf-manifest.json`, `graph-metadata.json`, `description.json`, `feature-catalog/`, plus\\n    sibling mode tables.\\n22. Propagation: advisor sync script, `sk-prompt` SKILL + card, `orchestrate.md`,\\n    `prompt-improver.md`, root `AGENTS.md`/`README.md`/`SECURITY.md`/`skills/README.txt`, trigger\\n    index, two sk-doc manifests, fan-out feature catalog.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. Cross-Runtime Comparison\\n\\n| Dimension | dsh headless | `pi -p` |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Model selection | Profile/patch only | `--provider` + `--model` per dispatch |\\n| Reasoning | `reasoningEfforts` in route | `--thinking` per dispatch |\\n| Prompt input | positional or stdin `-` | positional |\\n| Output | final text or NDJSON | text, JSON, RPC |\\n| Exit status | deterministic 0/1 + `final.reason` | non-deterministic; parse text |\\n| Sandbox | real, fail-closed `read-only`/`workspace-write`/`danger-full-access` | none; tool allowlist only |\\n| Tool allowlist | preset/profile composition | `--tools`, `--exclude-tools` |\\n| Skills | one-level root scan, per-skill symlink | recursive/whole-dir symlink |\\n| Agents | persona prefix, presets, subagent prompt | agent files, `--append-system-prompt` |\\n| Commands | prompt templates (no native loader) | `--prompt-template` |\\n| Hooks | plugin seams + Claude bridge | native extension API |\\n| MCP | `dsh-mcp-client` rows | extension/MCP config |\\n| Startup | ~1.16 s profile boot + model | process start + model |\\n| Footprint | 896 MB, Node 24.9+, 90 deps | npm package + extensions |\\n| Versioning | `0.2.2-rc.1`, rc cadence | release cadence |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. Recommended `.dsh/` Layout\\n\\n```text\\n.dsh/\\n  SYNC.md                 # what is generated, what is authored, drift checks\\n  patches/\\n    llmgateway-deepseek.yml    # route + agent-default-model + compat\\n    opencode-go-deepseek.yml   # route + agent-default-model + compat\\n    lineage-guards.yml         # disable goal, goal-round-driver, plan-mode, telemetry\\n  hooks.json              # Claude-style config with harness tool names\\n  mcp.yml                 # code_mode row translated from .pi/mcp.json\\n  skills/                 # generated per-skill symlinks (57)\\n  prompts/                # generated command templates (flattened paths)\\n  plugins/repo-guards/    # hand-authored bundle: goal context + compact context\\n```\\n\\nNo profile, no `settings.json`, no `node_modules`, no `AGENTS.md` copy. `DSH_HOME` stays outside the\\nrepo; a lineage points it at its own subdirectory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. Hard Rules for the Packet\\n\\n1. `headless-dash-stdin-required` — prompt on stdin through `-`, stdin closed.\\n2. `route-patch-required` — no `--model`; one checked-in patch per route, model must be on the roster.\\n3. `approval-never-required` — unattended leaves pass `--approval-policy never`.\\n4. `headless-only` — never dispatch `web`, `tui`, `acp`, `sdk` or `sdk-minimal`.\\n5. `dsh-home-isolated` — per-lineage `DSH_HOME`.\\n6. `goal-plan-disabled` — lineage patch disables goal, goal-round-driver and plan-mode.\\n7. `json-exit-classification` — require exit 0 and `final.reason.kind === 'completed'`; classify 1\\n   from the JSON `error`/`final.reason`.\\n8. `telemetry-disabled` — patch the telemetry row to `DISABLED` (or set `DSH_TELEMETRY_MODE`).\\n9. `profile-version-check` — `command -v dsh` and the installed version match the pinned rc.\\n10. `route-compat-pinned` — `supportsDeveloperRole: false` and `thinkingFormat: deepseek` on both\\n    gateway routes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Phase Plan\\n\\n| Rank | Phase | Outcome | Depends | Risk | Mode | Required | Prevents |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | 002 live contract pin | Keyed write dispatch, verbatim IO, JSON parse, bash and sandbox | operator key | backend missing; native builds | `sk-code` verify | required | building on docs only |\\n| 2 | 003 skill packet | SKILL/ROUTER/hard rules/references/assets | 002 | rule drift | `sk-doc` create-skill | required | ad-hoc dispatch |\\n| 3 | 004 executor kind | tables, builder, audit, tests | 002 | patch route; stdin misuse | `sk-code` implement | required | unverified provenance |\\n| 4 | 005 runtime folder | patches, hooks, MCP, SYNC, skill links | 003, 004 | link farm misses | `sk-code` + `sk-doc` | required | config drift |\\n| 5 | 006 hub registration | registry, hub, advisor, doctor, fixtures | 003 | unroutable mode | `sk-doc` + `sk-code` | required | no selection path |\\n| 6 | 007 command/agent bridges | templates, persona, goal context | 005 | truncation | `sk-doc` create-command/agent | parity required | reinvention |\\n| 7 | 008 hooks + guards | rewritten config, bundle, adapter | 005 | bridge install | `sk-code` implement | optional | guard loss |\\n| 8 | 009 MCP | mcp.yml, code-mode, route guard | 005 | scrubbed env | `sk-code` implement | optional | MCP absence/leak |\\n| 9 | 010 benchmark | playbook + benchmark index | 002-009 | unverified claims | `sk-doc` create-benchmark | optional | claims without proof |\\n| 10 | 011 propagation | trigger index, manifests, changelog | 006 | stale index | `sk-code` implement | required before merge | dangling routing |\\n| 11 | 012 rc re-pin | refreshed contract and roster | 002 | rc breakage | `sk-code` verify | per bump | silent break |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. Eliminated Alternatives\\n\\n- **A `--model`/`--provider` dispatch flag.** Does not exist; route selection is profile config.\\n- **A repo-local profile.** Profile lookup is `$DSH_HOME`-only and would need `node_modules`.\\n- **A whole-tree skill symlink.** One-level discovery hides 41 of 57 skills.\\n- **Markdown-only skill copies.** Lose `references/`, `assets/`, `scripts/` with no scanner reason.\\n- **Porting all 18 Pi extensions.** Sixteen are bridge-served by the repo's existing hook scripts.\\n- **Mounting `.claude/settings.json` unchanged.** Capitalized matchers never match lowercase tools.\\n- **Porting Pi packages as dsh plugins.** None is a dsh bundle; six capabilities are native.\\n- **Reading `.pi/mcp.json` directly.** No project MCP config scan.\\n- **A per-run turn budget.** None exists; disable goal/plan and rely on the runner timeout.\\n- **Reusing Pi's exit-code exception.** dsh's exit status is deterministic.\\n- **Plan mode as an unattended gate.** It fails closed without an interactive review.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 17. Divergence Map\\n\\n- **Saturated directions:** none. The lineage ran one pass per angle with no repeated focus and no\\n  pivot record.\\n- **Completed pivots:** 0. **Failed pivots:** 0. **Audited overrides:** 0.\\n- **Frontier:** the nine `UNKNOWN` items in §18, all gated on a configured provider key or a package\\n  install.\\n- **Evidence base:** 88 findings, 158 code citations and 25 other citations across ten iterations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 18. Open Questions / `UNKNOWN`\\n\\n1. Does `--patch` actually repoint `agent-default-model` in a headless dispatch?\\n2. Does LLM Gateway accept `compat.thinkingFormat: deepseek` with `reasoningEffort: max`, and does it\\n   reject `supportsDeveloperRole` without the compat flag?\\n3. Does the `bash` tool work after the skipped `koffi` and `node-pty` install scripts?\\n4. Does a 57-entry per-skill symlink farm load all entries in one session?\\n5. Is `dsh-hooks-claude-code` installable from npm at `0.2.2-rc.1`, and do the rewritten matchers\\n   fire each script with a compatible payload?\\n6. Does code-mode MCP connect under the scrubbed stdio environment with only `UTCP_CONFIG_FILE`?\\n7. What are the real startup-plus-model latency and cost per iteration?\\n8. Does telemetry stay silent in `FEEDBACK_ONLY` on every headless exit path?\\n9. How stable is the `0.2.2-rc.*` surface across rc bumps?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 19. References\\n\\n- Harness source clone: `dsh-src/` at `fcc0ad462172522aaf5c93a7b2e01f6b9f0b0159`\\n  (`/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Skilled/617b2600-a71c-4154-80bb-9def2171203a/scratchpad/src/dsh-src`).\\n- Installed package: `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/lib/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh`.\\n- Resource map: `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/resource-map.md`.\\n- Research angles: `specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research-angles.md`.\\n- Repo runtime precedents: `.pi/SYNC.md`, `.pi/PLUGINS.md`, `.hermes/SYNC.md`.\\n- Deep-loop runtime: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts`,\\n  `runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs`, `runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts`.\\n- Hook layer: `.claude/settings.json`, `.skilled/hooks/dispatch/lib/dispatch-audit.mjs`.\\n- Iteration files: `research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-001.md` … `iteration-010.md`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Convergence Report\\n\\n- **Stop reason:** `maxIterationsReached` (the configured cap; convergence is telemetry only for this\\n  lineage)\\n- **Total iterations:** 10\\n- **Questions answered:** 10 / 10\\n- **Remaining questions:** 0; nine `UNKNOWN` items are recorded as open evidence gaps, not unanswered\\n  angle questions\\n- **Last 3 iteration summaries:** run 8 MCP (0.88) · run 9 fan-out fitness (0.90) · run 10 constraints\\n  and phase plan (0.85)\\n- **Convergence threshold:** 0.05 (not reached; the cap is authoritative)\\n- **Divergence summary:** no divergent pivots; one correction (hook bridge not bundled) supersedes an\\n  earlier shorthand\\n- **Average newInfoRatio:** 0.881\\n- **Source coverage:** 158 code citations, 25 other citations\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/085-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/deepseek/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793916876880,"end":1793916911355}}}}
